{"parentUuid":"8105ff44-b524-40bf-a7c7-247e47ffe218","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvHYd8unjfrfQa6JzMst","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I closed all 14 idle helpers, but `error-envelope` itself can't be closed from here. It's a finished subagent and its session entry is just a leftover record. The `list` output shows it as `completed`, so it isn't doing anything.\n\n**What's actually holding it open.** Three agent worktrees are still *locked* by the Claude agent process: `error-envelope`, `input-validation` and `note-once`. All three of their branches are merged. Git refuses to remove a locked worktree without a double force. I didn't override that, since the lock is the harness's own marker and not mine to break without asking.\n\n**What I did clean up**\n- **Shutdown requests:** the 14 teammates (the PR-body writers, the audit agent and the inventory agent) were sent shutdown requests.\n- **Worktrees removed:** the merged ones for `camel-case-fields`, `error-code-hygiene`, `usage-exit-code` and `spec-gaps`, along with their stray local branches.\n- **Still present:**\n  - `cli-polish` (#503 is still open)\n  - `changeset-process` (#495 is still open)\n  - the three locked ones above\n\n**To clear the rest, either of these works**\n- Running `/agents` and closing the finished ones removes the session entries and releases the locks.\n- Or tell me to force-unlock and remove the three worktrees. They're merged, so nothing is lost, but I'll only do that on your word.\n\nneeds input: close them with `/agents`, or say \"force it\" and I'll remove the three locked worktrees."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2033,"cache_read_input_tokens":835978,"output_tokens":664,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servic