{"parentUuid":"e4e4279b-56cf-4212-b00f-6608fd259d86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwShke9y7Be1h6LmaqcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agreed. 0.20.0 should carry this work, so **don't merge #493 yet**. It refreshes itself as new changesets land, and I'll tell you when it's ready to read as a user. I'm launching five agents in parallel on stability, performance and release safety, all against current main (green at `f06bb0fd5`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7660,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwShjxUJ3RtKozBcncxt","requestRef":"58e959c1-2b69-467c-af35-fdf6f4fe77c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e221dbe-79ab-413a-9a7e-3c3646b227af","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:19:17.400Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"1e221dbe-79ab-413a-9a7e-3c3646b227af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwShke9y7Be1h6LmaqcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014EhQGX4Xq3ZynnsssphUc9","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"error-code-reach","description":"E254 catch-all and user-reachable E171","prompt":"Task: finish the error-code cleanup before 1.0 freezes codes (docs/stability.md: \"a code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md, docs/stability.md and docs/errors.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c fix/error-code-reach origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nTwo follow-ups from the previous error-code PR (#500, merged):\n1. E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") is a catch-all. crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs (roughly lines 412 to 567) raises it for several different conditions: a bad `publish-to` value, a bad `release-trigger` value, a cargo registry `url`, an unparsable package pattern, and others. List every distinct condition behind E254 (read the code, then confirm with the built binary using small callisto.toml files). Give each condition that is not literally \"unknown key\" its own accurate code (next free numbers: E330 and up; E329 is the last used; check docs/errors.md for the real highest), keep E254 only for the condition its documented meaning names, and document every code in docs/errors.md with a precise cause and fix. Never reuse or renumber an existing code; if E254's documented meaning is not \"unknown key\", keep it for exactly what it documents.\n2. `ReleaseInvariant` (E171, \"internal release invariant violated ... report it\") is used about 45 times. For every site, decide whether a user can reach it through config, flags or workspace content (then it needs a real user-facing code), or only through a bug in Callisto (then E171 is right). Start with the suspects: release/binding.rs around lines 72 and 78 (unknown registry; a `[registries.X]` kind that does not match the publish target's ecosystem), release/derive.rs around line 756 (\"invalid configured artifact slot\"). Reproduce each reachable one with the built binary and a minimal config; fix the reachable ones with real codes, leave genuine invariants. Report the full table of sites with your decision and evidence.\n\nIMPORTANT, learned the hard way: this repo has a classification test, crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, which fails when any code in docs/errors.md is neither in `USAGE_CODES`/`USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES` (crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, exit 2) nor in the `RUNTIME_CODES` list in that test (exit 1). Every new code you add must be classified: a code is usage (exit 2) only when it means \"the user passed a bad flag value or combination on the command line\"; config content and workspace state errors are runtime (exit 1). Classify each new code and run that test. There is also an error registry architecture test (cargo test -p callisto-graph --test error_registry_architecture) and the repo's doc-check.\n\nAcceptance: a test per new code driving the real binary (fails before, passes after) showing the old code or E171 and the new code; docs/errors.md consistent; mutation check on one new test. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words which codes users will now see instead of E254 or E171 for which situations, and whether a script matching the old code could break. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code (the sandbox blocks three network tests; list them if they fail). Final report: the E254 condition table, the E171 site table, new codes with classification, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7660,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014EhQGX4Xq3ZynnsssphUc9":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"error-code-reach","description":"E254 catch-all and user-reachable E171","prompt":"Task: finish the error-code cleanup before 1.0 freezes codes (docs/stability.md: \"a code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md, docs/stability.md and docs/errors.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c fix/error-code-reach origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nTwo follow-ups from the previous error-code PR (#500, merged):\n1. E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") is a catch-all. crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs (roughly lines 412 to 567) raises it for several different conditions: a bad `publish-to` value, a bad `release-trigger` value, a cargo registry `url`, an unparsable package pattern, and others. List every distinct condition behind E254 (read the code, then confirm with the built binary using small callisto.toml files). Give each condition that is not literally \"unknown key\" its own accurate code (next free numbers: E330 and up; E329 is the last used; check docs/errors.md for the real highest), keep E254 only for the condition its documented meaning names, and document every code in docs/errors.md with a precise cause and fix. Never reuse or renumber an existing code; if E254's documented meaning is not \"unknown key\", keep it for exactly what it documents.\n2. `ReleaseInvariant` (E171, \"internal release invariant violated ... report it\") is used about 45 times. For every site, decide whether a user can reach it through config, flags or workspace content (then it needs a real user-facing code), or only through a bug in Callisto (then E171 is right). Start with the suspects: release/binding.rs around lines 72 and 78 (unknown registry; a `[registries.X]` kind that does not match the publish target's ecosystem), release/derive.rs around line 756 (\"invalid configured artifact slot\"). Reproduce each reachable one with the built binary and a minimal config; fix the reachable ones with real codes, leave genuine invariants. Report the full table of sites with your decision and evidence.\n\nIMPORTANT, learned the hard way: this repo has a classification test, crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, which fails when any code in docs/errors.md is neither in `USAGE_CODES`/`USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES` (crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, exit 2) nor in the `RUNTIME_CODES` list in that test (exit 1). Every new code you add must be classified: a code is usage (exit 2) only when it means \"the user passed a bad flag value or combination on the command line\"; config content and workspace state errors are runtime (exit 1). Classify each new code and run that test. There is also an error registry architecture test (cargo test -p callisto-graph --test error_registry_architecture) and the repo's doc-check.\n\nAcceptance: a test per new code driving the real binary (fails before, passes after) showing the old code or E171 and the new code; docs/errors.md consistent; mutation check on one new test. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words which codes users will now see instead of E254 or E171 for which situations, and whether a script matching the old code could break. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code (the sandbox blocks three network tests; list them if they fail). Final report: the E254 condition table, the E171 site table, new codes with classification, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwShjxUJ3RtKozBcncxt","requestRef":"58e959c1-2b69-467c-af35-fdf6f4fe77c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6e6513b-6a51-4edd-9bdf-c7369e380b15","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:19:26.737Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b6e6513b-6a51-4edd-9bdf-c7369e380b15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwShke9y7Be1h6LmaqcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XcZWC1AaKHkMzbZMDzXTXR","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"json-contract-complete","description":"Pin schemaVersion on every JSON output","prompt":"Task: make sure EVERY `--format json` output carries `schemaVersion`, and pin it with a test, because docs/stability.md freezes this from 1.0 (\"Every report carries schemaVersion\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c fix/json-contract-complete origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nKnown: the previous PRs added envelope-checking tests for FAILING commands (crates/callisto-cli/tests/error_envelope_tests.rs) and a camelCase guard (crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs), and put `release pending` and `release build-python` into the standard envelope. `release inspect` success deliberately prints the raw input document (a durable document with its own versioning); decide from the code whether that is acceptable under the promise and report it, do not change it without evidence it is wrong.\n\nRequired:\n1. Enumerate EVERY command and subcommand that accepts `--format json` (read crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs and the command handlers; include hidden CI-plumbing ones). For each, find what its SUCCESS output looks like, with the built binary where the command can run offline in a small temp workspace (a git repo with a Cargo workspace and `callisto init --yes`). Build a table: command, success output has schemaVersion (yes/no), command key, dryRun key, camelCase keys (yes/no), notes. Include `schema`, `completions` (not JSON, say so), `matrix`, `compose-pr-body`, `release plan|execute|inspect|artifact-manifest|build-python|pending`, `release-pr verify|decide|commit-plan`, `status`, `version`, `snapshot`, `pre`, `add`, `init`.\n2. Fix any gap in a Rust report type with the standard envelope (follow how ReleasePendingReport was added in crates/callisto-model/src/release/report.rs), keeping the payload keys unchanged.\n3. Add ONE table-driven test that runs the real binary for every command that can run offline with `--format json` and asserts: valid JSON on stdout, top-level `schemaVersion` is a number, and (for reports that have them) `command` equals the documented command name and `dryRun` is a bool; and fails with a message naming any command missing it. Commands that cannot run offline in a test (needs network or toolchain) are listed in the test as an explicit allow-list with a reason, so a new command forces a decision.\n4. Also check the callisto-action outputs (.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml and the scripts that set them) against docs/stability.md: the Stable table says the action INPUTS are stable; list the inputs and outputs in docs as they exist and note any that are undocumented or inconsistently named (do not rename anything; report).\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a script sees now versus before for any output you changed. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on the table test (remove a report's schemaVersion and confirm it fails). If you add error codes, they must be classified in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs / tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (see that test). Final report: the command table, fixes, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequen