{"parentUuid":"b6e6513b-6a51-4edd-9bdf-c7369e380b15","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fddf1b3c-8d23-4438-96c6-01148de494a2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014EhQGX4Xq3ZynnsssphUc9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: af4e7f439c8fcba8a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'af4e7f439c8fcba8a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/af4e7f439c8fcba8a.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"512e1036-470d-4440-b813-1648b8f02fec","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:00.853Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"af4e7f439c8fcba8a","description":"E254 catch-all and user-reachable E171","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Task: finish the error-code cleanup before 1.0 freezes codes (docs/stability.md: \"a code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md, docs/stability.md and docs/errors.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c fix/error-code-reach origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nTwo follow-ups from the previous error-code PR (#500, merged):\n1. E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") is a catch-all. crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs (roughly lines 412 to 567) raises it for several different conditions: a bad `publish-to` value, a bad `release-trigger` value, a cargo registry `url`, an unparsable package pattern, and others. List every distinct condition behind E254 (read the code, then confirm with the built binary using small callisto.toml files). Give each condition that is not literally \"unknown key\" its own accurate code (next free numbers: E330 and up; E329 is the last used; check docs/errors.md for the real highest), keep E254 only for the condition its documented meaning names, and document every code in docs/errors.md with a precise cause and fix. Never reuse or renumber an existing code; if E254's documented meaning is not \"unknown key\", keep it for exactly what it documents.\n2. `ReleaseInvariant` (E171, \"internal release invariant violated ... report it\") is used about 45 times. For every site, decide whether a user can reach it through config, flags or workspace content (then it needs a real user-facing code), or only through a bug in Callisto (then E171 is right). Start with the suspects: release/binding.rs around lines 72 and 78 (unknown registry; a `[registries.X]` kind that does not match the publish target's ecosystem), release/derive.rs around line 756 (\"invalid configured artifact slot\"). Reproduce each reachable one with the built binary and a minimal config; fix the reachable ones with real codes, leave genuine invariants. Report the full table of sites with your decision and evidence.\n\nIMPORTANT, learned the hard way: this repo has a classification test, crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, which fails when any code in docs/errors.md is neither in `USAGE_CODES`/`USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES` (crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, exit 2) nor in the `RUNTIME_CODES` list in that test (exit 1). Every new code you add must be classified: a code is usage (exit 2) only when it means \"the user passed a bad flag value or combination on the command line\"; config content and workspace state errors are runtime (exit 1). Classify each new code and run that test. There is also an error registry architecture test (cargo test -p callisto-graph --test error_registry_architecture) and the repo's doc-check.\n\nAcceptance: a test per new code driving the real binary (fails before, passes after) showing the old code or E171 and the new code; docs/errors.md consistent; mutation check on one new test. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words which codes users will now see instead of E254 or E171 for which situations, and whether a script matching the old code could break. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code (the sandbox blocks three network tests; list them if they fail). Final report: the E254 condition table, the E171 site table, new codes with classification, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/af4e7f439c8fcba8a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","branch":"fix/cli-polish","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b6e6513b-6a51-4edd-9bdf-c7369e380b15","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
