{"parentUuid":"2da05d41-c40c-4065-ac65-f4be328b8034","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fddf1b3c-8d23-4438-96c6-01148de494a2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PZxScRkuubxAgc2wKsiEK5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a5e465e9b44611fbd (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a5e465e9b44611fbd', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a5e465e9b44611fbd.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"bff3e847-3475-4f29-809b-3c391451f2c8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:00.990Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a5e465e9b44611fbd","description":"Pin tag names and Action inputs","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Task: add contract tests for the remaining 1.0 stable promises that have no test, test-only. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c test/stability-contracts origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\ndocs/stability.md says these are stable from 1.0. For each, first check whether a test already pins it (grep the tests and the .github/tests scripts), then add one where it is missing; report what already existed:\n1. Tag names: the default tag is `{name}@{version}`, and `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name; `tag-template` pins a name. Test with the real binary and temp workspaces (see crates/callisto-cli/tests for patterns): single ecosystem uses the bare name; two ecosystems with the same package name both switch to the qualified form (and the output of `status` or the release plan shows it); a `tag-template` overrides both.\n2. The GitHub Actions: the inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto` are stable. Write a contract test (Rust or the repo's existing shell contract-test style under .github/tests and .github/actions/*/tests; prefer extending the existing pattern and run `just workflow-contracts`) that pins the set of input names and their `required`/default values from each action.yml against a checked-in list, so removing or renaming an input fails CI and adding one requires updating the list deliberately. Do NOT change the action files. The repo's workflow policy check (.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh) forbids new secrets and write permissions; your change must not need any.\n3. Exit codes 0/1/2: the classification test exists (crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs); only add a test if you find a promise gap, and report it.\n4. `callisto.toml`: a test already rejects an unknown key in every table (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs `every_config_table_rejects_an_unknown_key`); verify it still covers every table struct currently in config/ (a table added later must be caught: consider a test that fails when a config struct has no deny_unknown_fields) and add that guard if cheap.\n\nMutation check each new test. No code or action changes unless a test reveals a real bug (then stop and report it with evidence). Do NOT add a changeset (tests only). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just workflow-contracts` judged by exit code (the sandbox blocks three network tests and gpg-signing in workflow-contracts; if so say so). Final report: per promise, what existed, what you added (test name and file), the mutation used, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a5e465e9b44611fbd.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","branch":"fix/cli-polish","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2da05d41-c40c-4065-ac65-f4be328b8034","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
