{"parentUuid":"cc5a6c0c-2358-4e5e-97b2-3f2c286dc4ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwSrTjeyfBLcEbW2PPPF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ezsiiNNR48mJmkABNiaA8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/trail162_note.py","content":"import subprocess\n\nnote = (\n    \"Audit (2026-11-11, origin/main f06bb0fd5), plan item by item. \"\n    \"1 Revert the bad merge: done. \"\n    \"2 Retry with backoff and visible stderr: done (gh_retry in create-or-update-release-pr.sh, 4 attempts, REL-PR-08, tested). \"\n    \"3 Pre-merge guard: built as a hold, not a check (REL-PR-09, hold-release-pr.yml drafts the release PR on every push to main; the action marks it ready only if main's tip still equals the commit it built from). A failed or missing refresh leaves a draft, and a draft cannot be merged. \"\n    \"4 Docs: E165 recovery is in docs/releasing.md; `callisto release pending` does not name it. \"\n    \"5 Stray-tag status warning: nothing recorded. \"\n    \"Remaining ways a stale release PR can still merge: a one-call race between the tip read and `gh pr ready`; a delayed or failed hold run; and a person marking the held draft ready by hand, which nothing stops. In each case nothing is published and the first visible failure is the post-merge Release run with E165, repeated on every push until the release payload is reverted.\"\n)\nshown = subprocess.run([\"entire\", \"trail\", \"show\", \"162\", \"--project\", \"gh/orin-dx\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\nbody = shown.split(\"Description:\\n\", 1)[1].strip() if \"Description:\\n\" in shown else \"\"\nr = subprocess.run([\"entire\", \"trail\", \"update\", \"162\", \"--project\", \"gh/orin-dx\", \"--body\", body + \"\\n\\n\" + note], capture_output=True, text=True)\nprint(\"exit\", r.returncode)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,