{"parentUuid":"927aec5b-5dc0-49fa-b3b3-08ed28d2f1a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwUHN9ccrw13ecUpx4G2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01589sgHzr16D4NhoKX3PBhv","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr505-body","description":"PR body for 505","prompt":"Write the title and body for a test-only pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr505.diff. Change: docs/stability.md freezes `--format json` reports from 1.0 (\"every report carries schemaVersion\"). An audit of every command's JSON success output found every one already carries `schemaVersion`, so no report type changed. A new table-driven test `every_json_success_output_carries_a_schema_version` runs the real binary for 21 invocations across two workspaces (a fresh init+add workspace and a release-commit fixture driven through plan, inspect, artifact-manifest and execute with fake publishers) and asserts stdout is valid JSON with a numeric top-level `schemaVersion`, and for reports that command equals the documented name and `dryRun` is a bool. It walks the clap command tree including hidden commands, so every command must be in the table or an explicit exempt list with a reason (`completions`, `help`, `schema`, `release build-python`), which makes a new command force a decision. The test makes no network calls: the fixture's GitHub-looking `origin` is given an unreachable local proxy in repo config. docs/stability.md gains a sentence: `release inspect` prints the raw intent, manifest or receipt, each with its own `schemaVersion`, and `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. Findings reported, not changed: the Action's inputs are snake_case and outputs camelCase (`hasChangesets`, `published`, `publishedPackages`), and `schema` output has no schemaVersion.\nVerified: a mutation making `matrix` print JSON without the envelope fails the test; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. No changeset (tests and one doc sentence).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":900629,"output_tokens":3310,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3310,"cache_read_input_tokens":900629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01589sgHzr16D4NhoKX3PBhv":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr505-body","description":"PR body for 505","prompt":"Write the title and body for a test-only pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr505.diff. Change: docs/stability.md freezes `--format json` reports from 1.0 (\"every report carries schemaVersion\"). An audit of every command's JSON success output found every one already carries `schemaVersion`, so no report type changed. A new table-driven test `every_json_success_output_carries_a_schema_version` run