{"parentUuid":"9825665e-9bfe-48b8-acbe-b4b6f659e2aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwUKj9EYcRd1a61agATQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NmaM3LgyqTRJ8bwr6ZU3UV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr506_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nE254 (\"unknown callisto key\") had become a catch-all for nine unrelated `callisto.toml` conditions, although an unknown key is already E325. With codes freezing at 1.0 (`docs/stability.md`: a code keeps its meaning and is never reused), E254 is retired and each condition gets its own code.\n\nE330 bad `publish-to`, E331 bad `release-trigger`, E332 bad `cascade.mode`, E333 bad `changelog.layout`, E334 unknown registry `kind`, E335 `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry, E336 `url` on a Cargo registry, E337 registry timeout outside 1s to 1h, E338 unparsable package `match` pattern.\n\nE339 covers a `[registries.X] kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem. A user can cause it, but it reported E171 (\"internal invariant violated, report it\"). It is raised at release derivation, not config load.\n\nEvery new variant carries the file path; the old release-trigger error printed an empty one. All ten are runtime errors (exit 1). Of about 40 other E171 sites, only this one was reachable by user input, and the rest stay E171. Some were judged by reading, not reproduced.\n\n## Breaking\n\nScripts matching E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes. Exit codes are unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\nTen new tests drive the real binary and assert the new code and the absence of E254 and E171. Another test checks every new code is documented. Changing E336 back to E254 fails its test. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1559,"cache_read_input_tokens":905472,"output_tokens":823,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1559,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":905472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1559},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NmaM3LgyqTRJ8bwr6ZU3UV":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr506_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nE254 (\"unknown callisto key\") had become a catch-all for nine unrelated `callisto.toml` conditions, although an unknown key is already E325. With codes freezing at 1.0 (`docs/stability.md`: a code keeps its meaning and is never reused), E254 is retired and each condition gets its own code.\n\nE330 bad `publish-to`, E331 bad `release-trigger`, E332 bad `cascade.mode`, E333 bad `changelog.layout`, E334 unknown registry `kind`, E335 `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry, E336 `url` on a Cargo registry, E337 registry timeout outside 1s to 1h, E338 unparsable package `match` pattern.\n\nE339 covers a `[registries.X] kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem. A user can cause it, but it reported E171 (\"internal invariant violated, report it\"). It is raised at release derivation, not config load.\n\nEvery new variant carries the file path; the old release-trigger error printed an empty one. All ten are runtime errors (exit 1). Of about 40 other E171 sites, only this one was reachable by user input, and the rest stay E171. Some were judged by reading, not reproduced.\n\n## Breaking\n\nScripts matching E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes. Exit codes are unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\nTen new tests drive the real binary and assert the new code and the absence of E254 and E171. Another test checks every new code is documented. Changing E336 back to E254 fails its test. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c9c95892-834a-4420-8f30-24dcbee357f0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwUKiiSM9cQ8aRsDzX23","requestRef":"447abd49-0b76-4503-aa20-e07048261154","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3012f3f1-2363-42ed-9d63-ed991f90ef38","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:40:20.050Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e465e9b44611fbd","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
