{"parentUuid":"9a966764-aca5-4109-8f03-a2dd57db0865","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwaeod5wzjNVSBL5tiCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Michi's own principles say a subprocess runner doesn't belong there, and its error layer isn't a replacement for Callisto's error codes. This is from the local checkout, which is 30 commits behind `origin/main` and has two uncommitted settings files. I couldn't fetch it because that directory is outside my write access.\n\n**What michi is**\n- **`michi-core`** (FSL, 0.9.0) is an agent-readable output layer. It holds `ErrorCode` and `DomainError`, `redact_secrets` and `redact_url_userinfo`, retry and backoff (`resilience.rs`), `RecoveryHint`, idempotency, truncation and the TOON format.\n- **`michi-pipeline`** (FSL) is async step execution on Tokio, with breaker, scheduler, per-attempt timeouts and retry. It is for steps, not OS subprocesses.\n- **`michi-graph`** (MIT) is the DAG library Callisto already uses.\n\n**Subprocess runner (wait-timeout, duct)**\n- It fails michi's own admission gates in `PRINCIPLES.md`: gate 1 (rendering, not domain logic), gate 2 (the default build depends only on `thiserror` and `compact_str`) and gate 3 (a second independent tool must already hand-roll it).\n- Its other constraints are the ones I listed earlier: the sync-vs-Tokio mismatch and the FSL licence, which `callisto-model` (MIT) can't depend on.\n- The runner stays in Callisto. Dropping in a crate would save about 15 lines.\n\n**Error codes**\n- Michi's `ErrorCode` is nine HTTP-flavoured categories (`InvalidInput`, `NotFound`, `Timeout`…) and `exit_code()` is hardcoded to 1. Callisto's 274 permanent `E###` codes and its usage/runtime exit split don't map onto that. My `exit_kind()` plan stands, and it doesn't need michi.\n\n**What is worth reusing**\n- **`redact_secrets` and `redact_url_userinfo`:** Callisto has its own redaction in `callisto-model/registry.rs` next to the duplicated credential lists. I haven't compared the two. If they overlap, deleting one is a real simplification, but the licence boundary applies, so it could only be used from the CLI side, not `callisto-model`.\n- **`resilience.rs` retry and backoff:** Callisto has retry and hold logic in its registry and release paths. I haven't compared that either.\n- Anything michi gained in the 30 commits I can't see needs a fresh pull first.\n\n**Revised investigation list:** the michi item drops out as a replacement source, leaving two real comparisons (redaction, retry) and the earlier items. If you want those compared, I'll launch the read-only agents once you've pulled michi. Otherwise they'll compare against the stale local copy.\n\nneeds input: pull michi (run `! git -C ~/Projects/michi pull` since it's outside my sandbox), then say go."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2755,"cache_read_input_tokens":121702,"output_tokens":1007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":121702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2755},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3924fe1f-76f4-4cac-a243-35ad48ff114f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwaeoJk84317M5d56JWd","requestRef":"344f50d4-485c-4bbb-8300-41e3cd64460c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c286d0ff-f5bd-4456-9425-e036ec358198","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:03:23.703Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort