 whether instead the Callisto code should be upstreamed to michi. Also list michi pieces with no Callisto overlap you looked at. Do not edit. Under 700 words, with file:line evidence."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"output_tokens":2172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":119},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DoytRBbrua9M1eCFcKqgRB":{"description":"Michi vs Callisto overlap","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only comparison, very thorough. Callisto: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (sync Rust release CLI; crates callisto-model MIT, callisto-graph and callisto-cli FSL). Michi: /Users/gabe/Projects/michi (just updated to latest main; crates michi-core FSL, michi-pipeline FSL async Tokio, michi-graph MIT). Read michi PRINCIPLES.md, AGENTS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and `git log --oneline -40` first, then the public API of michi-core (error, redact, resilience, recovery, idempotency, status, hints, truncation) and michi-pipeline.\n\nQuestion: where does Callisto hand-roll something michi already provides, or something michi should provide (passes michi's own five admission gates in PRINCIPLES.md)? Check specifically:\n1. Secret redaction: michi-core redact.rs vs callisto-model/src/registry.rs (r