{"parentUuid":"0e7dc2d1-16f2-4005-ae26-18a339653dac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwanUg3985TLeEeh9LPw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kVELbF7rVun4EX7NJkAq8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Credentials, diff, PR overlap","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only investigation in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto Rust release CLI). Do not edit. Answer with file:line evidence; you may run narrow commands and git merge-tree (use `git fetch -q origin` first; do not push).\n\nA. Credential lists. Lists: RELEASE_CREDENTIALS and ACTION_SECRET_INPUTS in crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs, RELEASE_CREDENTIALS in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/provider/registry.rs:339, SECRET_CREDENTIAL_ENV in crates/callisto-model/src/registry.rs:189. They differ (NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG vs CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG). Trace which environment each child process (build backend, publish, git, hooks) actually receives and from where those variables get set. Decide: can CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG or any other credential reach a build backend or be echoed unredacted? State the intended purpose of each list and propose the single table (name, secret-value?, withheld-from-build?, withheld-from-other-children?) that reproduces today's behaviour exactly, noting any behaviour that would change.\nB. Exit kind. List the enum variants (file:line, enum name) behind each code in USAGE_CODES and USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs. Say which error enums hold them and whether a `fn exit_kind(&self)` with `_ => Runtime` per enum would reproduce today's exit codes exactly, and where CliError::is_usage_error and main.rs consume it. Check docs/stability.md for what is promised.\nC. changed.rs: crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs changed_source_files_since_last_tag. Why are diffs pathspec-scoped? How are `ignore` excludes applied (exclude_pathspec)? Could one unscoped `git diff --name-only <commit>` per tag commit, mapped to packages via SpecIndex plus a Rust-side ignore filter (globset/ignore crates if already dependencies), give identical results? List semantics that would differ (ignore patterns, gitignored/untracked, submodules, --relative). Also note the `rev:dir` bug at lines 67-68 (git resolves rev:path from the repo top, not cwd; should be rev:./dir).\nD. Open PR overlap: for open PRs #495, #504, #505, #506, #507 on orin-dx/callisto (use `gh pr list` and `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/main origin/<branch>` pairwise), report which touch usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, error.rs, changed.rs, runner.rs, registry.rs and which pairs conflict, so a plan can order the work.\nUnder 800 words, ranked by how much each changes the plan."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"output_tokens":2172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":119},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014kVELbF7rVun4EX7NJkAq8":{"description":"Credentials, diff, PR overlap","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only investigation in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto Rust release CLI). 