{"parentUuid":"e16fad4e-4b78-4ff2-a56d-61c50eaedfbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwb9azPJaMDG8SacqsSb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Goal:** remove the over-engineering in the 0.20 batch and make the type system carry the invariants, without touching frozen 1.0 behaviour. Both investigations are done, and no code has changed yet.\n\n**What we established**\n- **Two real bugs, both confirmed:**\n  - `changedSinceLastTag` is wrongly false when the workspace is in a repo subdirectory, because `changed.rs` builds `rev:dir` instead of `rev:./dir`.\n  - `pre enter 01` and `beta.01` are accepted but fail later in `version`, because `validate_tag` hand-writes the SemVer grammar that `semver::Prerelease` already enforces.\n- **Over-engineering, verified:**\n  - Exit-code classification: `USAGE_CODES` plus a 230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string, guarded by a meta-test.\n  - Windows pathspec chunking in `changed.rs`.\n  - Five wall-clock asserts in `runner.rs`.\n  - `note_once` global state.\n- **Over-engineering, still unchecked by me:** the source-text scan tests, the `snapshot.rs` `include_str!` test, `test_auto_traits`, and the two workflow-grep shell scripts.\n- **Credential lists:** no leak, so this is cleanup at best. A single table needs four flags, which is itself the kind of over-engineering we're removing.\n- **Michi:** nothing to swap in. Its licence (FSL) blocks `callisto-model`, its error codes are nine coarse categories and its retry is async. The only upstream candidate is the token-shape masker, and it waits for a second tool.\n- **Root causes:** no typed `ErrorCode`, tests used as the invariant mechanism, hand-written grammars where a crate is the spec, and global state.\n\n**Steps, each a small PR off `origin/main` in its own named worktree**\n\n| # | PR | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Bug fixes: `rev:./dir` plus a subdirectory-workspace test, and `semver::Prerelease` for `pre enter` | Nothing, can start now |\n| 2 | You land #495, #505, #504, #506, #507 (all merge cleanly in pairs) | You |\n| 3 | `exit_kind()` per error type, deleting both code lists and the meta-test | #504 and #506 merged |\n| 4 | Deletions I'll verify first: wall-clock asserts, `test_auto_traits`, text-scan tests | Nothing |\n| 5 | `changed.rs`: unscoped diff plus `SpecIndex` and a `globset` filter, removing `PATHSPEC_BUDGET` and `list_in_chunks` | #507 merged |\n| 6 | `note_once` without the global | Nothing |\n| 7 | `AGENTS.md` invariant-ladder section (type, exhaustive match, clippy lint, one small test) plus a Brain memory | Your OK to edit `AGENTS.md` |\n| 8 | Optional: credential table, workflow-script replacement | Only if each deletes more than it adds |\n\n**Rules for every PR**\n- Signed commits, one topic per PR.\n- Checks judged by exit code, with a regression test for each bug.\n- Implementer briefs say \"prefer types, delete before adding\".\n- Changesets only for user-visible changes. The two bug fixes get one each, since they change what users see.\n\n**Open items**\n- The unchecked audit findings need verifying before PR 4.\n- The globset matcher needs `literal_separator(true)` to match git's glob behaviour.\n- The lean #505 change is still uncommitted in this worktree.\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll start PR 1 now. The rest follows your merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2081,"cache_read_input_tokens":139790,"output_tokens":1251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2081,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":139790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2081},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"15408851-190f-4886-a2bf-2f39c69b8168","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgwb9ag2ke6fz6pfYfh7u","requestRef":"8979ae34-4d8f-4a8f-a793-cf213a19b0d6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91f7a023-76c9-480e-9307-c60fe2bdef50","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:09:54.962Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
