{"parentUuid":"b911fa5d-5a5b-4fd3-be74-57df915f828d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwcnaAB7JJQ8bCVeqEhR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4872,"cache_read_input_tokens":148939,"output_tokens":2638,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4872,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2638,"cache_read_input_tokens":148939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4872},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":16534,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"bcc9f15b-8e7c-4da7-9b3d-57551411ed75","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwcnZqKdcBkm1TJ3vJF8","requestRef":"cf3d5627-4a28-4dd1-a0ac-3c17b3b39a76","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b4d0083-64a0-44ed-929c-f4a4343b7350","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:31:32.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9b4d0083-64a0-44ed-929c-f4a4343b7350","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwcnaAB7JJQ8bCVeqEhR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now checked the remaining findings against the code. Most hold up, one corrects the audit, and the biggest new one is three overlapping error-code scanners.\n\n**Confirmed, delete or replace**\n\n| Finding | Evidence | Lean fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `map_err` source scan (`architecture.rs:222-283`) | `map_err_ignore = \"deny\"` is already a workspace clippy lint (`Cargo.toml:64`), so the test and its file allowlist duplicate it | Delete test and allowlist |\n| `stale_reason_constructors_are_module_private` (`architecture.rs:196`) | Greps the source for `pub` on constructors the compiler already keeps private | Delete |\n| `release_intent_stale_is_constructed_only_…` (`architecture.rs:166`) | Private constructors can't be called from other modules, so the compiler already guarantees this | Delete |\n| `apply_permits_are_never_granted_from_a_literal` plus its self-test (`architecture.rs:289-337`) | Text scan for `granted_unless_dry_run(true)` | Make the parameter a `DryRun` newtype built only from the parsed flag, so a literal won't compile |\n| `snapshot.rs:513` `include_str!` test | Greps its own source for a function name, to pin a non-goal | Delete |\n| `cascade.rs:58-59` | `(Dev, _)` and `_` arms have identical bodies | Delete one line |\n| `test_auto_traits` (`model/lib.rs:83`) | Tiny and harmless. The auditor was partly wrong: only the two report types are bounded by `Report`. The six `thread::scope` sites already fail to compile if a type isn't `Send + Sync`. | Delete |\n\n**The bigger new finding: three overlapping error-code scanners**\n- **`model/lib.rs:98-190`:** a 12-file `include_str!` list plus a hand-written `code(E` scanner. Its own comment records that a previous hand-maintained list missed files.\n- **`error_registry_architecture.rs`:** 232 lines hand-parsing enums to check every variant carries a code.\n- **`error_code_hygiene_tests.rs` and the `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` meta-test:** two more \"is documented\" checks.\n- **Root cause:** there is no typed code, so every per-code fact is a text scan.\n- **Fix:** collapse them into one shared scan covering uniqueness, documented and present-on-every-variant. `exit_kind()` removes one of them. A full `ErrorCode` type across 274 variants would remove the rest, but it's large churn, so I'd treat it as a separate decision.\n\n**Needs your call: the workflow scripts**\n- `just ci` already runs `zizmor`. The two bespoke scripts (141 and 174 lines) add repo-specific policy: grep checks in one, and bash wrapping embedded Python and `yq` in the other.\n- Rewriting them in Rust with `yaml-rust2` is possible. But they enforce your release policy, and you've said gates shouldn't grow. I'd leave them, or trim only what `zizmor` already covers, once you decide.\n- The action scripts that run real `jq` or bash are legitimate shell tests. Keep them.\n\n**Still unchecked:** near-identical tests that `rstest` could collapse (only 5 uses today, never measured), the `has_*` bools in `init.rs`, and anything hand-rolled in `runner.rs` beyond the poll loop.\n\nPR 4 now grows to: the six deletions above, the `DryRun` newtype and the scanner collapse. The two bug fixes (PR 1) are unaffected.\n\nneeds input: go to start PR 1, and tell me whether to touch the workflow scripts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4872,"cache_read_input_tokens":148939,"output_tokens":2638,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4872,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2638,"cache_read_input_tokens":148939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4872},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bcc9f15b-8e7c-4da7-9b3d-57551411ed75","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwcnZqKdcBkm1TJ3vJF8","requestRef":"cf3d5627-4a28-4dd1-a0ac-3c17b3b39a76","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8bb41406-455e-4bb3-a932-03e4a1881c1d","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:31:35.856Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
