{"parentUuid":"52e06dbc-f8b0-41ee-9575-3d70463021ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwcpLELBVFobtbxa7y9X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, for the PRs that add the over-engineering, because deleting it afterwards means merging it and then writing a second PR. For the ones that don't, no.\n\n| PR | Fix before merge? | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#505** (JSON contract) | Yes | Commit the lean change already in this worktree: `write_document` is crate-private, `write_error_json` is added and `json_contract_tests.rs` is deleted. Update the PR body to match. |\n| **#504** (stability tests) | Yes, trim | Delete the Action-input shell script, its `.txt` lists and the `justfile` line, and the `deny_unknown_fields` source-scan guard. Keep the tag-name test and the exit-code parse-error test, which drive the real binary. If we want Action inputs covered, add one small Rust `insta` test. |\n| **#507** (perf) | Yes, small | Drop the 3,000-package wall-clock test and keep the call-counting test. The PR body currently admits it has a flake risk. |\n| **#506** (E330–E339) | Your call | These add ten new permanent codes. Consolidating them into fewer broader codes now is cheaper than after 1.0, but it contradicts your earlier \"one condition per code\" direction. I'd leave it unless you want it changed. |\n| **#495** (docs/process) | No | Docs only, no overlap. |\n\n**Already merged, so follow-up PRs:** the `PATHSPEC_BUDGET` chunking from #494 and the `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` lists. Those are items 3 and 5 in the plan.\n\nThe fixes to #504, #505 and #507 are small and independent, so I'd make each as one signed commit on its own branch and re-run the checks by exit code. #504 and #506 both edit `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`, so I'd trim #504 first and then confirm #506 still merges cleanly.\n\nneeds input: say go, and say whether to leave #506's codes as they are."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2701,"cache_read_input_tokens":153811,"output_tokens":952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":293},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":153811,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ac1031c5-a300-4a12-8e3e-b62e1791e10e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwcpKzSBxEQKD8b1tmmt","requestRef":"fbedf92f-581c-4162-9b2c-818b4712b2e1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9533a05d-c05a-44f0-9ced-fb6cf9fd77be","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:31:46.866Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
