entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"e3b77447-7559-45e2-b01d-4da30ab15be9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwdeqpA1c3oV6W1rbMJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kaj38f6KbD4sDARBPkjkr6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507_final2.md","content":"## Summary\n\nPlanning a release in a very large monorepo scaled with the number of releasing packages, so `callisto release` and the release PR body slowed sharply as more packages shipped together. Two causes, found by the same benchmark on one planning path:\n\n- The preflight that checks a package has not moved past its version commit ran one `git log` and one `git cat-file --batch` per package. It now runs one `git log` for all manifests (`first_parent_commits_by_path` in `callisto-model`, using `--first-parent -m` and literal pathspecs) plus one batched read. A package whose newest candidate is not the version-setting commit falls back to its own read, so results are unchanged.\n- `workspace_package` rescanned every package and recomputed identities on each call. It is replaced by a map built once (`ReleaseOwners`), every call site is migrated, and per-selection linear scans are now set lookups.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic monorepo (1,800 packages, 1,500 depending on one core package, 1,000 pending changesets, 20,000 tags): `release --dry-run` 13.9 s to 1.85 s and 3,012 git processes to 14 (debug), 8.10 s to 1.27 s (release build). With 20,000 commits it goes from 7.95 s to 1.63 s, and `compose-pr-body` from 12.1 s to 1.45 s (debug) and 1.90 s to 0.76 s (release). `status`, `version --dry-run` and the other dimensions benchmarked flat or linear and are untouched.\n\n## Verify\n\nOld and new output are byte-identical for `release --dry-run` text and JSON and for `compose-pr-body` on both large cases.\n\nA counting-runner test pins one `git log` and a bounded `cat-file` count at 3 and at 12 packages, and two mutations fail it. The existing version-commit tests, including a 105-edit and merge-commit cases, pass. A wall-clock test for the lookup map was dropped as flaky; the map is covered by the selection tests.\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\nNot changed: `version --emit-preview` takes 33 to 45 s when thousands of packages are bumped, about 75% of it macOS `F_FULLFSYNC` from the per-file and per-directory fsync. That is the durability invariant in AGENTS.md, so it is left alone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":193258,"output_tokens":1091,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":740,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":193258,"cache_creation_input_tokens":740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":740},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Kaj38f6KbD4sDARBPkjkr6":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507_final2.md","content":"## Summary\n\nPlanning a release in a very large monorepo scaled with the number of releasing packages, so `callisto release` and the release PR body slowed sharply as more packages shipped together. Two causes, found by the same benchmark on one planning path:\n\n- The preflight that checks a package has not moved past its version commit ran one `git log` and one `git cat-file --batch` per package. It now runs one `git log` for all manifests (`first_parent_commits_by_path` in `callisto-model`, using `--first-parent -m` and literal pathspecs) plus one batched read. A package whose newest candidate is not the version-setting commit falls back to its own read, so results are unchanged.\n- `workspace_package` rescanned every package and recomputed identities on each call. It is replaced by a map built once (`ReleaseOwners`), every call site is migrated, and per-selection linear scans are now set lookups.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic monorepo (1,800 packages, 1,500 depending on one core package, 1,000 pending changesets, 20,000 tags): `release --dry-run` 13.9 s to 1.85 s and 3,012 git processes to 14 (debug), 8.10 s to 1.27 s (release build). With 20,000 commits it goes from 7.95 s to 1.63 s, and `compose-pr-body` from 12.1 s to 1.45 s (debug) and 1.90 s to 0.76 s (release). `status`, `version --dry-run` and the other dimensions benchmarked flat or linear and are untouched.\n\n## Verify\n\nOld and new output are byte-identical for `release --dry-run` text and JSON and for `compose-pr-body` on both large cases.\n\nA counting-runner test pins one `git log` and a bounded `cat-file` count at 3 and at 12 packages, and two mutations fail it. The existing version-commit tests, including a 105-edit and merge-commit cases, pass. A wall-clock test for the lookup map was dropped as flaky; the map is covered by the selection tests.\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\nNot changed: `version --emit-preview` takes 33 to 45 s when thousands of packages are bumped, about 75% of it macOS `F_FULLFSYNC` from the per-file and per-directory fsync. That is the durability invariant in AGENTS.md, so it is left alone.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee4b669b-b9e6-4851-849c-b1b5b9abc3ca","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwdeqJtWuuEHLigU9fEx","requestRef":"04aa6877-0515-4e37-af66-e743a692d7cc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4fbae4b-0b0c-48c3-8691-05bd144f2893","tim