{"parentUuid":"da1aff29-f3eb-4f9a-b7a0-edffbe8a3ea8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwksdyvhH17fhmPHZHdt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"With #495 and #504–#507 merged, the plan's remaining work is below. I haven't pulled `origin/main` since the merges, so the first step in each worktree is a fresh branch off it.\n\n| # | PR | Why now |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Bug fixes:** `rev:./dir` in `changed.rs` (with a subdirectory-workspace test) and `semver::Prerelease` for `pre enter` | Two confirmed user-facing bugs. #507 has landed, so there's no conflict. |\n| 2 | **`exit_kind()`:** an exhaustive match per error type, deleting `USAGE_CODES`, `RUNTIME_CODES` and the meta-test | #504 and #506 are merged, so it deletes the list once. |\n| 3 | **Deletions:** the `map_err`, stale-constructor and snapshot text-scan tests, `test_auto_traits`, the cascade wildcard and the five wall-clock asserts in `runner.rs`, plus the `DryRun` newtype and collapsing the three error-code scanners | All verified, with no dependencies. |\n| 4 | **`changed.rs`:** an unscoped diff mapped through `SpecIndex`, removing `PATHSPEC_BUDGET` and the chunking | Unblocked by #507. |\n| 5 | **`note_once`** without the global | Small, with no dependencies. |\n| 6 | **`AGENTS.md` invariant ladder** plus a Brain memory | Needs your OK to edit `AGENTS.md`. |\n| 7 | **Release PR #493 (0.20.0):** refresh it, then read the rendered changelog before merging | Last, once the batch is in. You asked to include the stability and performance work in this release. |\n\nI'd start with #1, since it fixes real bugs, then #2 and #3 in parallel (the two PRs touch different files).\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll start PR 1, or reorder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53,"cache_read_input_tokens":212619,"output_tokens":1066,"output_tokens_d