actly one list; `error_envelope_tests.rs:~17` also reads the lists.\nReplace with: an `ExitKind` enum (Usage, Runtime) and `fn exit_kind(&self) -> ExitKind` on each error enum that owns a usage variant, written as an exhaustive-by-intent match that names ONLY the usage variants and defaults `_ => ExitKind::Runtime` (runtime is the safe default). Variants: 26 are CliError variants (codes E214 E216 E217 E218 E224-E229 E231 E240 E241 E242 E270 E271 E274 E275 E276 E279 E282 E283 E298 E309 E327 E329); three are GraphError variants in crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs (E195 InitInvalidForgeRepository, E196 InitInvalidTargetTriple, E324 TagInvalid); E316 ColonReference and E317 BareReference are ConfigError variants that count as usage only when their `context` starts with `--` (reachable as CliError::Config and CliError::Graph(GraphError::Config)). CliError delegates to GraphError/ConfigError. Find each variant by grepping `code(E###)`. Put ExitKind where both crates can reach it (callisto-graph, since cli depends on it) unless the layering says otherwise. `main.rs` uses `exit_kind()`.\nDelete: USAGE_CODES, USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES, the string-based `is_usage_error`, RUNTIME_CODES, and the classification meta-test (and whatever in error_envelope_tests.rs or error_code_hygiene_tests.rs consumed the lists; keep any check there that is NOT about the lists). KEEP the binary-driven tests in usage_exit_codes_tests.rs that run the real binary and assert exit 2 / exit 1 (observable behavior) and update imports. Exit codes must be byte-identical to today: before deleting, capture the classification of every documented code from the OLD lists (a scratch script, not committed) and prove the new `exit_kind` yields the same for each variant you can construct; at minimum add one small unit test per enum that constructs one usage variant and one runtime variant, plus a ConfigError test for the `--` context rule. Do not touch docs/errors.md numbering. Fix doc comments that referenced 