{"parentUuid":"d0252a4a-3805-45d8-973e-7058febb8098","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwm6cfRj4Hje9ynUGnAo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `note_once` agent stopped without changing anything, so there's nothing to review, and I'd drop that item for now.\n\n**Why it stopped:** the note fires twice because the workspace is loaded twice.\n- `init` loads it in `detect` and again in `preview` (`commands/init.rs`).\n- The `release` flows load once in `load_workspace`, then `validate_release_intent` loads again in `commands/release/capability.rs`.\n\nThe note is emitted from the locator walk, so every extra load repeats it. There's no single once-per-command place to print from. Carrying the notes upward needs a signature change across the init, release and capability paths, which was the stop condition I gave.\n\n**My read:** the global is a symptom. The real waste is the duplicate workspace load, which also costs time on large repos, and removing that would make `note_once` unnecessary. That is a different and larger change: pass the loaded workspace into `validate_release_intent` and into `preview` instead of reloading. It touches the release path, so it needs its own look at what the second load is for. I haven't checked whether it re-reads on purpose, for example to see fresh state after a write.\n\n**Decision:** I'd leave `note_once` as it is, since it's small, contained and tested by `private_workspace_root_tests.rs`. I'd add the duplicate-load question as a separate investigation after wave 1. The agent left an unused local branch `refactor/note-without-global` in its worktree, which I'll delete.\n\nThe other four agents are still running: the bug fixes, `exit_kind`, the deletions, and the `AGENTS.md` section.\n\nneeds input: tell me if you want the duplicate-load investigation queued after wave 1, or dropped."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1391,"cache_read_input_tokens":238177,"output_tokens":776,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":224},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1391,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":238177,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1391},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"046107ca-0a1b-45fa-9f5b-6c1ad3bb26c9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgwm6cP4Kj3yhJtpbNVzH","requestRef":"4da771d8-dbf8-43ad-8d71-fadf9d460f1f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"73d37af8-4684-4f8d-9514-ab3cc7e4328c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:20:20.909Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/invariant-ladder","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
