{"parentUuid":"540d523a-9a77-4d0a-8631-8af496e726a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwm84n5w9iesgky2X6kn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `AGENTS.md` change (`docs/invariant-ladder`) is good as written. It adds a 16-line \"Enforcing an invariant\" section between Invariants and Fixing bugs, and I read the diff:\n\n- **Ladder:** a type or private constructor, then an exhaustive `match`, then an existing lint, then one small test, then nothing.\n- **Rules:** no source-text tests, no hand-maintained lists that mirror code, prefer crates already in `Cargo.lock`, prefer fewer broader codes, and delete a check before adding one.\n- **Checks:** the agent reports `just doc-check` and `just pre-push` exit 0 and the commit is signed. It did not run `lint` or `test`, which doesn't matter for a docs-only change.\n\nI'll open its PR once the other branches are in, so the PR text and changesets go through the courier agents in one pass. Three agents are still running: the bug fixes, `exit_kind` and the deletions. The finished agents left temporary worktree branches that I'll delete when we wrap up.\n\nThe `note_once` question from my last message is still open: queue the duplicate-workspace-load investigation after wave 1, or drop it?\n\nneeds input: queue or drop the duplicate-load investigation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4824,"cache_read_input_tokens":241429,"output_tokens":411,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":411,"cache_read_input_tokens":241429,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"