{"parentUuid":"4103b29c-d3bd-4e52-a4b8-c3705efa4de3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwmZNMhYV7o6gXE2ZAcB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0147H5HUcUnqFS5aJFv1FL9x","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a3264fad8587e83c7","summary":"Check sibling rev:path sites for subdir workspaces","message":"Your two fixes are correct. AGENTS.md says to grep for structurally identical code, and I found five sibling sites on origin/main that build `{rev}:{path}` object specs from `normalized_git_path` (workspace-relative, no `./`), so git resolves them from the repo TOP when the workspace is a repo subdirectory: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs `git_file` (~line 760) and `batch_manifest_blobs_at` (~820); commands/version.rs `prefetch_head_manifests` (~499), `head_has_pending_changeset` (~569) and `manifest_blob_at` (~596). (release/version_commit.rs already uses `HEAD:./`, and commands/version/tests.rs:191 builds a test spec.) On the same branch: 1) with a REAL run, build a repo r1/ with the callisto workspace at r1/ws (cargo package, a pending changeset, a commit after it) and run the real binary from r1/ws for `version --dry-run`, `status`, and `release plan --dry-run` (whichever exist; use the harness in crates/callisto-cli/tests/common) and see which of the five sites misbehave (wrong result or error) versus a same-content repo whose root is the workspace. 2) For each site that is actually wrong, fix it the smallest way (prefer one shared helper that produces the `./`-anchored spec, or change `normalized_git_path` callers to prefix `./`; do not add parameters across many signatures) and add ONE real-git regression test that fails before and passes after. 3) If a site is NOT affected, say why (e.g. it runs git with a different cwd). Same house rules: signed commit (retry with dangerouslyDisableSandbox if gpg fails in the sandbox), verify with the verify.sh script by exit code, push the same branch, no PR. Report in under 150 words: which sites were broken, red/green proof, verify results.","type":"message","recipient":"a3264fad8587e83c7","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Your two fixes are correct. AGENTS.md says to gre…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1081,"cache_read_input_tokens":256889,"output_tokens":1334,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":579},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1081,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1334,"cache_read_input_tokens":256889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1081},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0147H5HUcUnqFS5aJFv1FL9x":{"to":"a3264fad8587e83c7","summary":"Check sibling rev:path sites for subdir workspaces","message":"Your two fixes are correct. AGENTS.md says to grep for structurally identical code, and I found five sibling sites on origin/main that build `{rev}:{path}` object specs from `normalized_git_path` (workspace-relative, no `./`), so git resolves them from the repo TOP when the workspace is a repo subdirectory: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs `git_file` (~line 760) and `batch_manifest_blobs_at` (~820); commands/version.rs `prefetch_head_manifests` (~499), `head_has_pending_changeset` (~569) and `manifest_blob_at` (~596). (release/version_commit.rs already uses `HEAD:./`, and commands/version/tests.rs:191 builds a test spec.) On the same branch: 1) with a REAL run, build a repo r1/ with the callisto workspace at r1/ws (cargo package, a pending changeset, a commit after it) and run the real binary from r1/ws for `version --dry-run`, `status`, and `release plan --dry-run` (whichever exist; use the harness in crates/callisto-cli/tests/common) and see which of the five sites misbehave (wrong result or error) versus a same-content repo whose root is the workspace. 2) For each site that is actually wrong, fix it the smallest way (prefer one shared helper that produces the `./`-anchored spec, or change `normalized_git_path` callers to prefix `./`; do not add parameters across many signatures) and add ONE real-git regression test that fails before and passes after. 3) If a site is NOT affected, say why (e.g. it runs git with a different cwd). Same house rules: signed commit (retry with dangerouslyDisableSandbox if gpg fails in the sandbox), verify with the verify.sh script by exit code, push the same branch, no PR. Report in under 150 words: which sites were broken, red/green proof, verify results."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd0db3dc-eaeb-4511-b0d6-0c8eaa8bfe8c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwmZN3rGePubj4ETNtbP","requestRef":"f111529b-265b-4b29-bbc1-fd8696cb62a4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9052a0c-c784-4fb9-b3db-fa4a2f66a454","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:26:27.327Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"refactor/exit-kind","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
