{"parentUuid":"90364a47-06f8-414d-ad92-2db7e3e6602c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwmumkfh5XDaLR1UXejq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CXNRVqvYYpNVMZDvhqiG7e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exitkind.md","content":"## Summary\n- Exit-code classification was stringly typed: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, a string-matching `is_usage_error`, and a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string kept honest by a meta-test. This replaces all of it with `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` and an `exit_kind()` method on `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError`. Each names only its usage variants and defaults to `Runtime`, and `main.rs` maps `Usage` to exit 2.\n- Exit codes are unchanged. A scratch test (not committed) compared the old `is_usage_error` with the new `exit_kind` on 76 error values built from every usage variant, covering all 31 usage codes including E316 and E317 (`--` flags vs `callisto.toml`). The runtime variants of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and the model errors were not all built; they count as runtime because none defines a usage code.\n- Tradeoff: a new usage error must be added to its `exit_kind` match deliberately. Before, the meta-test failed when a documented code was unclassified; now an unlisted variant exits 1. Net +15 lines (+106/-91).\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: no CLI flag, output or `callisto.toml` change.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: no observable behavior change.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [ ] Not run: CI, and `just ci` as a single target\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_token