d `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [ ] Not run: CI, and `just ci` as a single target\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1,"newLines":17,"lines":[" ## Summary","+- Exit-code classification was stringly typed: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, a string-matching `is_usage_error`, and a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string kept honest by a meta-test. This replaces all of it with `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` and an `exit_kind()` method on `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError`. Each names only its usage variants and defaults to `Runtime`, and `main.rs` maps `Usage` to exit 2.","+- Exit codes are unchanged. A scratch test (not committed) compared the old `is_usage_error` with the new `exit_kind` on 76 error values built from every usage variant, covering all 31 usage codes including E316 and E317 (`--` flags vs `callisto.toml`). The runtime variants of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and the model errors were not all built; they count as runtime because none defines a usage code.","+- Tradeoff: a new usage error must be added to its `exit_kind` match deliberately. Before, the meta-test failed when a documented code was unclassified; now an unlisted variant exits 1. Net +15 lines (+106/-91)."," ","-Exit-code classification was stringly typed: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, a string-matching `is_usage_error`, and a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string kept honest by a meta-test. This replaces all of it with `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` and an `exit_kind()` method on `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError`. Each type names only its usage variants and defaults to `Runtime`, and `main.rs` maps `Usage` to exit 2. The compiler now owns the classification instead of string lists and a test that scans them.","+## Type of change","+- [x] Internal refactor: no CLI flag, output or `callisto.toml` change."," ","-Exit codes are unchanged. The old and new classification agree on all 76 error values built from every usage variant, covering 31 usage codes, including E316 and E317 (`--` flags vs `callisto.toml`).","+## Changeset","+- [x] None needed: no observable behavior change."," ","-Tradeoff: a new usage error must be added to its `exit_kind` match deliberately. Before, the meta-test failed when a documented code was unclassified. Now an unlisted variant exits 1 (runtime). Net +15 lines (+106/-91) because the 26-arm match replaces the string lists.","+## Docs","+- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes."," ","-No changeset: no user-visible change.","-","-## Verify","-","-`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` all exit 0 locally. CI has not run yet.","-","-The equivalence was checked with a scratch test, not committed, that compared the old `is_usage_error` with the new `exit_kind` on each of the 76 values. The runtime variants of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and the model errors were not all built; they count as runtime because none defines a usage code.","+## Test Plan","+- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0","+- [ ] Not run: CI, and `just ci` as a single target"]}],"originalFile":"## Summary\n\nExit-code classification was stringly typed: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, a string-matching `is_usage_error`, and a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string kept honest by a meta-test. This replaces all of it with `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` and an `exit_kind()` method on `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError`. Each type names only its usage variants and defaults to `Runtime`, and `main.rs` maps `Usage` to exit 2. The compiler now owns the classification instead of string lists and a test that scans them.\n\nExit codes are unchanged. The old and new classification agree on all 76 error values built from every usage variant, covering 31 usage codes, including E316 and E317 (`--` flags vs `callisto.toml`).\n\nTradeoff: a new usage error must be added to its `exit_kind` match deliberately. Before, the meta-test failed when a documented code was unclassified. Now an unlisted variant exits 1 (runtime). Net +15 lines (+106/-91) because the 26-arm match replaces the string lists.\n\nNo changeset: no user-visible change.\n\n## Verify\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` all exit 0 locally. CI has not run yet.\n\nThe equivalence was checked with a scratch test, not committed, that compared the old `is_usage_error` with the new `exit_kind` on each of the 76 values. The runtime variants of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and the model errors were not all built; they count as runtime because none defines a usage code.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30ac589c-8e9b-4977-a1b5-d7e2d1f98c93","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
