{"parentUuid":"1945b64b-c784-4d65-a45e-f745a33acc2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwn2ofxuXzpz9vFUgK5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bug-fix branch passes my review, and its changeset text is being drafted.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags` is one signed commit (`b2cea66ce`). The agent amended it and force-pushed with `--force-with-lease` after a `fmt-check` failure. That was safe here because the branch had no PR or other users, but I didn't ask for it.\n- **Fix:** a shared `object_at(rev, path)` helper produces `rev:./path`. It covers the five sibling sites (`git_file`, `batch_manifest_blobs_at`, `prefetch_head_manifests`, `head_has_pending_changeset`, `manifest_blob_at`) and the release-decision object.\n- **Checks:** all five exit 0, per the agent.\n- **Tests:** a real-git regression test for the subdirectory workspace fails when the helper is reverted.\n\n**Unproven:**\n- The agent did not run the real binary from a subdirectory workspace.\n- The two `release_decision.rs` sites have no dedicated regression test, only the shared helper. Of the five sites, only the `version.rs` ones were shown affected.\n\n**Next:** I'll write the changesets onto the branch when the courier agent returns, with the `status` and release-preview fix and the `pre enter` fix as separate entries. Then I'll commit signed, re-run the checks and open the PR.\n\nneeds input: none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1757,"cache_read_input_tokens":294984,"output_tokens":470,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1757,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_t