{"parentUuid":"383c0f58-b17c-45ad-a1c1-0900e5d96864","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwnGF81r3EUmJw2j7m1L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CeH9PYoh4HaRWhEja12EZS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_bugfix.md","content":"## Summary\n- `callisto status` and the release preview now give correct results when the callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repo (`repo/ws`). git resolves `rev:path` from the repository top, not the cwd, so `changed_since_last_tag` compared two missing objects as equal. `status` reported `changedSinceLastTag: false` for packages with committed changes, and the release preview dropped its uncovered-change warnings. The fix uses `rev:./dir`. The same latent problem existed at five sibling sites (`git_file`, `batch_manifest_blobs_at`, `prefetch_head_manifests`, `head_has_pending_changeset`, `manifest_blob_at`), so they now go through one shared `object_at(rev, path)` helper in `release_decision.rs`.\n- `pre enter 01` and `beta.01` were accepted, then `version` failed with E035. The dotted tag check now uses `semver::Prerelease::new`, so these are rejected up front with E324. `semver` was already a workspace dependency and is now added to `callisto-graph`.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/status-in-subdirectory-workspace.md` (patch). The leading-zero tag note is folded into the unreleased `.changeset/catch-bad-input-early.md`.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flag or config change, and E324 is an existing code.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally\n- [x] A real-git test with the workspace at `r1/ws` in `changed.rs` fails before the fix. A real-git `check_partial_run_refuses_in_a_workspace_below_the_repository_root` test fails when the helper is reverted. An rstest table covers the tag grammar, including `01` and `beta.01`.\n- [ ] Not proven: the real binary was not run from a subdirectory workspace, and the two `release_decision.rs` sites have no dedicated regression test (they use the shared helper). CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1772,"cache_read_input_tokens":308387,"output_tokens":879,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":62},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":308387,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1772},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CeH9PYoh4HaRWhEja12EZS":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_bugfix.md","content":"## Summary\n- `callisto status` and the release preview now give correct results when the callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repo (`repo/ws`). git resolves `rev:path` from the repository top, not the cwd, so `changed_since_last_tag` compared two missing objects as equal. `status` reported `changedSinceLastTag: false` for packages with committed changes, and the release preview dropped its uncovered-change warnings. The fix uses `rev:./dir`. The same latent problem existed at five sibling sites (`git_file`, `batch_manifest_blobs_at`, `prefetch_head_manifests`, `head_has_pending_changeset`, `manifest_blob_at`), so they now go through one shared `object_at(rev, path)` helper in `release_decision.rs`.\n- `pre enter 01` and `beta.01` were accepted, then `version` failed with E035. The dotted tag check now uses `semver::Prerelease::new`, so these are rejected up front with E324. `semver` was already a workspace dependency and is now added to `callisto-graph`.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/status-in-subdirectory-workspace.md` (patch). The leading-zero tag note is folded into the unreleased `.changeset/catch-bad-input-early.md`.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flag or config change, and E324 is an existing code.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally\n- [x] A real-git test with the workspace at `r1/ws` in `changed.rs` fails before the fix. A real-git `check_partial_run_refuses_in_a_workspace_below_the_repository_root` test fails when the helper is reverted. An rstest table covers the tag grammar, including `01` and `beta.01`.\n- [ ] Not proven: the real binary was not run from a subdirectory workspace, and the two `release_decision.rs` sites have no dedicated regression test (they use the shared helper). CI has not run.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"98289ebf-a2a9-43ca-b714-c0db032dbca9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwnGEqQCfhMARjDEqJoq","requestRef":"a4f7fd2c-301e-4fc4-a53a-659e07a71e04","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fd75503-09a1-45f9-9dd7-ecae0b326a46","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:35:36.651Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
