{"parentUuid":"81d35c54-debe-42f8-8e68-29d5d64ea90b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwpJSmnc44zXKEmBVpBT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QrznYqz1fHRdVhcbq3xmBo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Docs versus code drift audit","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY drift audit; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7 (branch fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags, = origin/main plus a small fix). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first; docs/stability.md is the 1.0 contract. You may run the built binary (`cargo run -q -p callisto-cli -- ...` or target/debug/callisto if present) against temp fixture repos in $TMPDIR; do not run the full test suite.\n\nFind places where the documentation promises something the code does not do (or the reverse), prioritising what users and scripts rely on at 1.0. Check specifically:\n1. docs/stability.md promises: exit codes (0/1/2), JSON envelope keys (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`), camelCase keys, what `--format json` prints for every command, error-code permanence. Run each command's `--format json` on a fixture and compare with the claim; flag any command whose output breaks it.\n2. docs/errors.md vs code: every `#[diagnostic(code(E###))]` in crates vs the table rows (codes in docs but not in code, in code but not docs, duplicated), and whether each row's description and \"when\" text matches the variant's message/conditions for a sample of at least 25 codes, weighting the newest (E3xx).\n3. docs/config.md vs the config structs and `ConfigKey` constants in crates/callisto-graph/src/config: documented keys absent in code, code keys undocumented, wrong defaults or allowed values.\n4. docs/specs/*.json and `callisto schema` output vs real output: field names, required fields, enums.\n5. README/`--help` text for flags that no longer exist or behave differently (run `callisto <cmd> --help` for each command and spot-check three flags per command by running them).\nEarlier audits found about 14% of spec criteria false or partly true; assume drift exists and find it. Refute each candidate before reporting (re-run, read the code path). Do NOT report style or wording nits.\nReport under 600 words: ranked by user impact; per finding the doc file:line, the code file:line or the command and output that contradicts it, expected vs actual, confidence. End with areas you checked and found accurate."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2191,"cache_read_input_tokens":313668,"output_tokens":2825,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":905},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2191,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2825,"cache_read_input_tokens":313668,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2191},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QrznYqz1fHRdVhcbq3xmBo":{"description":"Docs versus code drift audit","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY drift audit; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7 (branch fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags, = origin/main plus a small fix). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first; docs/stability.md is the 1.0 contract. You may run the bu