d stays exit 1 — read the criterion and keep each clause accurate), CLI-INIT-10 (E240/E241), CLI-INIT-11 (E242), CLI-INIT-12 (E195/E196), CLI-SURF-06 (unknown command, E283). For EACH criterion, verify by running the binary (`cargo run -q -p callisto-cli -- ...` in a temp fixture dir under $TMPDIR) that the stated exit code is what actually happens before editing; do not change a criterion whose stated code is already right. Also CLI-OUT-06 lists the JSON error envelope as {schemaVersion, command, error}: add `dryRun` if the code emits it (crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs format_error_json).\n2. `snapshot --tag` help (crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs ~248: \"e.g. a commit SHA or branch name\") is wrong: only letters, digits and `-` are accepted, so `feature/x` fails E324. Reword the doc comment to say that in one short line (for example \"letters, digits and `-` only, e.g. a short commit SHA or PR number\"). Update any snapshot of the help text (crates/callisto-cli/tests/cmd/*.trycmd, insta snapshots) and docs/specs/cli.json CLI-SNAP-01 if it repeats the claim.\n3. Do NOT touch docs/config.md pre-major-inference (owner decision pending) or docs/errors.md wording.\n\nREPORT (under 120 words): which criteria you changed (and any you left because they were already right), the help change, commit signed?, five verify results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":326622,"output_tokens":2546,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":848,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2546,"cache_read_input_tokens":326622,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_