{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":11704,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"45512d71-aea0-4024-92d0-f4c2f5c1ce33","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwppAtPsr4gLkYZLJEnd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The drift audit found real mismatches, and I verified the top three in the repo. An agent is fixing the docs side of them now (Sonnet, low effort, isolated worktree).\n\n**Verified**\n- **Spec says exit 1, code exits 2:** `docs/specs/cli.json` states exit 1 for usage failures in CLI-OUT-06/07, ADD-04/05/06, INIT-10/11/12 and SURF-06. The binary exits 2, which matches `docs/stability.md`.\n- **`snapshot --tag` help:** it says \"commit SHA or branch name\", but branches like `feature/x` are rejected with E324.\n- **`pre-major-inference`:** `\"false\"` is accepted as `off` in the code, and `docs/config.md` doesn't mention it.\n\n**What the agent is doing:** it will check each criterion against the real binary before editing, and fix the spec text and the `snapshot --tag` help line. It will push a `docs/align-cli-spec-with-exit-codes` branch with a signed commit and the five checks; I'll open the PR after reviewing it. It won't touch `config.md`, `errors.md` or any other file.\n\n**Clean results:** 276 error codes in code and docs with no gaps or duplicates, every config key documented, and the JSON envelopes and schemas matching their docs.\n\n**Two decisions for you, which I haven't acted on**\n1. **Exit-code consistency:** unknown package passed as a flag (`--package cargo/zzz`) exits 1 (E102), but `release --package zzz` (E227) exits 2. Likewise `init --product-package` invalid (E189) exits 1 while the other `init` flag errors exit 2. Exit codes freeze at 1.0, so the choice has to be made now. I'd make bad flag values uniformly exit 2, but that changes behavior and builds on #508.\n2. **`pre-major-inference = \"false\"`:** document it as an alias, or remove it before it becomes permanent? Removing it is breaking for anyone who used it.\n\nThe `release plan` double load stays as it is, since the 200 ms saving doesn't justify the new signatures.\n\nneeds input: decisions 1 and 2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6055,"cache_read_input_tokens":327470,"output_tokens":721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":327470,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b0058faa-57f7-4b43-a8a1-22691fdd77ca","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwppAbXnBubuMUFNDRNz","requestRef":"eb14b8f2-46f4-4199-9657-92ed2a3af1f4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1a51745-7ff8-490f-ad94-3070f5f12f1b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:09:04.005Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
