 --no-renames --relative --name-only -z <commit>` per distinct tag commit (keep `--relative`: workspaces below the repo root must keep working), map each path to its owning packages with `SpecIndex`, and apply the `ignore` patterns in Rust instead of as git pathspecs, using `globset` (already a dependency; `ignore` crate also is). The ignore semantics must stay identical: look at `exclude_pathspec` (a trailing `/` names a directory at any depth => `**/dir/**`, anything else a file glob => `**/pat`), git's `:(exclude,glob)` magic (so `*` does not cross `/`: build the matcher with `literal_separator(true)`), and the default ignore list (~line 97). Note `{a,b}` and `\\` behave differently in globset than git; check whether any default or documented user pattern uses them and, if a user could, pick the globset settings closest to git and say what differs in the report. The untagged-package path (`ls-files -z`, one per untagged package) can stay scoped to its own directories or become one `ls-files` mapped through SpecIndex; choose the smaller code. Delete PATHSPEC_BUDGET, list_in_chunks, the budget parameter and tests that only exercise chunking. Results must be identical to today for: a file under several packages' directories, packages at the workspace root (`.`), ignore patterns (dir and file forms), subdirectory workspaces, deleted files, a package directory containing glob metacharacters such as `pkg[1]` (today's pathspec mis-matches; the Rust mapping should be correct, a behavior change in the good direction; mention it). Existing tests must keep passing; adapt tests that asserted the exact git arguments or call count only where the new single-diff shape requires it (a test asserting one `git diff` per tag commit should stay). Add one real-git test only if no existing test covers ignore handling end to end.\nREPORT (under 200 words): lines removed/added, how ignore semantics are preserved and any difference, a one-sentence measure of the diff on a large synthetic workspace if cheap (skip if not), commit signed?, five verify results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":340996,"output_tokens":4230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":387},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1036,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4230,"cache_read_input_tokens":340996,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1036},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014rLc4ZfwNAt35L9tCJpKwd":{"description":"changed.rs unscoped diff rewrite","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES (mandatory): prefer types and the compiler over tests; delete before adding; no speculative generality; Windows is unsupported; add no error code/JSON key/flag. Comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY; never hard-wrap prose. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false). No Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL for pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts); all five must PASS. Push (`git