{"parentUuid":"d58fc998-c041-43d6-ad85-fd8a9cf9bc7a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwqD6kk8a4CdT4ueLcS8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SoeQdjGxmck1eBKYRm9mXK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Collapse error-code scanners","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md (note the new \"Enforcing an invariant\" section). Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c refactor/one-error-code-scan origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES (mandatory): prefer types and the compiler over tests; delete before adding; no speculative generality; add no error code/JSON key/flag, and change no code number. Comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY; no history comments (\"a prior version...\"); never hard-wrap prose. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false). No Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL for pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts); all five must PASS. Push (`git push -u origin refactor/one-error-code-scan`). Do NOT open a PR; no changeset.\n\nTASK: error codes (`#[diagnostic(code(E###))]` on miette-derived enums; registry in docs/errors.md) are checked by several overlapping source-text scanners: (a) crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs `DIAGNOSTIC_CODE_SOURCE_FILES` (a hand-maintained list of ~12 `include_str!` files), `extract_diagnostic_codes`, tests `test_all_diagnostic_codes_are_unique` and `every_diagnostic_code_is_documented`; (b) crates/callisto-graph/tests/error_registry_architecture.rs (~232 lines hand-parsing enums to check every Diagnostic variant carries its own code or is `transparent`, and that no `callisto::name`-style code survives); (c) crates/callisto-cli/tests/error_code_hygiene_tests.rs (checks a few hard-coded codes appear in docs); plus whatever remains in crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs that reads docs/errors.md. First map exactly which property each test guards and which of them overlap. Then consolidate into ONE test file/module with one shared scan helper that DISCOVERS source files by walking crates/*/src (no hand-maintained file list, so a new file or crate is covered automatically), covering exactly: codes are unique across the workspace; every code in code appears in docs/errors.md and every documented code exists in code (276 each today); every Diagnostic-deriving enum variant has a code or is transparent; no non-numeric code. Keep the existing helper style in crates/callisto-graph/tests/common if reusable. Delete the superseded tests, the `include_str!` file list, the history comment in model/lib.rs, and any hard-coded code lists. Do not weaken any property: before deleting a test, name the property it guarded and the new test that covers it, and demonstrate by a throwaway mutation (duplicate a code, remove a code from docs/errors.md, remove a `code(...)` from one variant; revert after) that the consolidated test fails for each. Prefer a net deletion of lines.\nREPORT (under 200 words): the property map (old test -> new test), net lines removed/added, mutation results, commit signed?, five verify results, anything unproven."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":340996,"output_tokens":4230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":387},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1036,"ep