: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY; never hard-wrap prose. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false). No Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL for pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts); all five must PASS. Push (`git push -u origin refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs`). Do NOT open a PR; no changeset unless output changes (it must not).\n\nTASK: `crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs` `changed_source_files_since_last_tag` already groups packages by tag commit and runs one `git diff` per distinct commit, mapping files back to packages via `SpecIndex::owners_of`. What remains is pathspec scoping: `PATHSPEC_BUDGET = 24_000`, `list_in_chunks`, the `budget` parameter of `changed_source_files_in_batches`, and `exclude_pathspec` (git `:(exclude,glob)` specs), which exist for a Windows command-line limit (Windows is unsupported). Replace them: run ONE unscoped `git diff --no-renames --relative --name-only -z <commit>` per distinct tag commit (keep `--relative`: workspaces below the repo root must keep working), map each path to its owning packages with `SpecIndex`, and apply the `ignore` patterns in Rust instead of as git pathspecs, using `globset` (already a dependency; `ignore` crate also is). The ignore semantics must stay identical: look at `exclude_pathspec` (a trailing `/` names a directory at any depth => `**/dir/**`, anything else a file glob => `**/pat`), git's `:(exclude,glob)` magic (so `*` does not cross `/`: build the matcher with `literal_separator(true)`), and the default ignore list (~line 97). Note `{a,b}` and `\\` behave differently in globset than git; check whether any default or documented user pattern uses them and, if a user could, pick the globset settings closest to git and say what differs in the report. The untagged-package path (`ls-files -z`, one per untagged package) can stay scoped to its own directories or become one `ls-files` mapped through SpecIndex; choose the smaller code. Delete PATHSPEC_BUDGET, list_in_chunks, the budget parameter and tests that only exercise chunking. Results must be identical to today for: a file under several packages' directories, packages at the workspace root (`.`), ignore patterns (dir and file forms), subdirectory workspaces, deleted files, a package directory containing glob metacharacters such as `pkg[1]` (today's pathspec mis-matches; the Rust mapping should be correct, a behavior change in the good direction; mention it). Existing tests must keep passing; adapt tests that asserted the exact git arguments or call count only where the new single-diff shape requires it (a test asserting one `git diff` per tag commit should stay). Add one real-git test only if no existing test covers ignore handling end to end.\nREPORT (under 200 words): lines removed/added, how ignore semantics are preserved and any difference, a one-sentence measure of the diff on a large synthetic workspace if cheap (skip if not), commit signed?, five verify results.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aa1335c8970c67a54.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8aa93a79-3a09-47f6-8bad-879383f5874b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7","branch":"fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","r