icate code, a code removed from docs, an extra code added to docs (`E999`), a non-numeric code (`callisto::x`), and a `code(...)` removed from one variant all fail the consolidated tests.\n  \n  **Commit:** signed with `git commit -S`. `%G?` shows `E` because the signature can't be checked locally.\n  \n  **Unproven:** the \"276 each\" count is implied rather than printed. The undocumented-code and stale-code assertions both pass, which means the two sets are equal. The variant scan is still the old brace-depth text heuristic.\n</agent-message>"}
