mat, or `callisto.toml` schema)\\n- [ ] Documentation only\\n\\nTest-only refactor with no change to shipped behavior.\\n\\n## Changeset\\n- [x] No changeset: tests only, no observable behavior change.\\n\\n## Docs\\n- [x] No doc change needed. `docs/errors.md` is unchanged and is now enforced in both directions by the test.\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` each exit 0 locally.\\n- [x] Mutation-checked, each reverted afterwards. Each of these makes the consolidated tests fail: a duplicated code, a code removed from `docs/errors.md`, an extra code (`E999`) added to `docs/errors.md`, a non-numeric code (`callisto::x`), and a `code(...)` removed from one variant.\\n- [ ] CI has not run yet.\\n- [ ] Regression check against `callisto-fixtures`: not run separately, no fixture-facing code changed.\\n\\nNot proven:\\n- The variant check is still the old brace-depth text heuristic, only moved. It can miss unusual formatting.\\n- The count of 276 codes is implied, not printed: both set-difference assertions pass, so the sets match, but the test does not assert or print the count.\\n\"\n    ,\n    \"labels\": [\"refactor\", \"tests\"],\n    \"reasoning\": \"Followed the repo template sections. Led with the purpose (one scanner, no file list, new stale-doc check) rather than the file diff. Put the unproven items in the body as required, not only here. Marked the 276 count as implied. Chose no changeset per the supplied facts. Omitted Related since no issue was given. Left the fixtures box unchecked and said why; that reason is inferred from the facts given (tests only), so a reviewer may want to confirm. No session link or trailer added, per the user's rules. I did not run the diff command; the body is built from the facts supplied.\"\n  }\n  ```\n</agent-message>\n\nThat \"other Claude session\" is an agent working inside this same session — a subagent or teammate spawned on your user's behalf 