{"parentUuid":"d742d835-15ae-4d1f-a390-119a0195e5f5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwqiiMwFj3HAux2LrgH5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RQKQXBDAzKJ8QRv1mKfGWJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_scan.md","content":"## Summary\n- Error codes are now checked by one test file, `crates/callisto-graph/tests/error_registry_architecture.rs`, which walks `crates/*/src`. It checks that codes are numeric and unique, that every code in source appears in `docs/errors.md` and every documented code exists in source, and that every `Diagnostic` enum variant has a code or is transparent.\n- Several overlapping source-text scanners did this before: a hand-maintained 12-file `include_str!` list in `callisto-model/src/lib.rs` with its own scanner and two tests, the old `error_registry_architecture.rs`, and two doc tests in `error_code_hygiene_tests.rs`. They were removed (net +67/-311). A new file or crate was only covered if someone remembered to add it to a list.\n- The new scan has no file list, so new files and crates are covered automatically. It also checks the stale-doc direction (a documented code that no longer exists in source), which nothing checked before.\n- The behavior tests in `error_code_hygiene_tests.rs` are unchanged.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: tests only, no change to shipped behavior.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: tests only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None needed. `docs/errors.md` is unchanged and is now enforced in both directions by the test.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally\n- [x] Mutation-checked, each reverted afterwards: a duplicated code, a code removed from `docs/errors.md`, an extra code (`E999`) added to `docs/errors.md`, a non-numeric code (`callisto::x`), and a `code(...)` removed from one variant each make the consolidated tests fail\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n- [ ] Not proven: the variant check is still the old brace-depth text heuristic, only moved, so it can miss unusual formatting. The 276-code count is implied (both set-difference assertions pass), not printed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1853,"cache_read_input_tokens":364338,"output_tokens":792,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1853,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":364338,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1853},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RQKQXBDAzKJ8QRv1mKfGWJ":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_scan.md","content":"## Summary\n- Error codes are now checked by one test file, `crates/callisto-graph/tests/error_registry_architecture.rs`, which walks `crates/*/src`. It checks that codes are numeric and unique, that every code in source appears in `docs/errors.md` and every documented code exists in source, and that every `Diagnostic` enum variant has a code or is transparent.\n- Several overlapping source-text scanners did this before: a hand-maintained 12-file `include_str!` list in `callisto-model/src/lib.rs` with its own scanner and two tests, the old `error_registry_architecture.rs`, and two doc tests in `error_code_hygiene_tests.rs`. They were removed (net +67/-311). A new file or crate was only covered if someone remembered to add it to a list.\n- The new scan has no file list, so new files and crates 