{"parentUuid":"c0d4a77f-127c-40fd-a65d-0048ad335552","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwrR1pHMVZQEUBy6CVKV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019FCadZFqDewKSm4qfV2jYN","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md","old_string":"Related: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]","new_string":"**Follow-up (2026-11-11):** the cleanup shipped as #508-#515 (exit_kind, one error-code registry test, pathspec chunking removed, AGENTS.md \"Enforcing an invariant\"). Verify audit claims before deleting: an auditor said clippy `map_err_ignore` made a scan test redundant, but it only flags bare `|_|`, so the test stayed; a `DryRun` newtype would have been a net addition (41 call sites), so skip when the type fix is bigger than the check. Agents' `%G?` reads `E` in the sandbox: confirm signatures with `gh api .../commits/<sha> --jq .commit.verification.reason`. The duplicate workspace load is deliberate for the validate flows; `note_once` stays.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":398451,"output_tokens":490,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":398451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019FCadZFqDewKSm4qfV2jYN":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md","old_string":"Related: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]","new_string":"**Follow-up (2026-11-11):** the cleanup shipped as #508-#515 (exit_kind, one error-code registry test, pathspec chunking removed, AGENTS.md \"Enforcing an invariant\"). Verify audit claims before deleting: an auditor said clippy `map_err_ignore` made a scan test redundant, but it only flags bare `|_|`, so the test stayed; a `DryRun` newtype would have been a net addition (41 call sites), so skip when the type fix is bigger than the check. Agents' `%G?` reads `E` in the sandbox: confirm signatures with `gh api .../commits/<sha> --jq .commit.verification.reason`. The duplicate workspace load is deliberate for the validate flows; `note_once` stays.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7423779a-2339-4669-8bf2-77c7308688f7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwrR1XRhL5ZcZyk583mG","requestRef":"df476613-ac2b-4fc4-a720-6e83da33ae86","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e487bc68-e5eb-442e-bb81-8f769b895db5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:30:01.829Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"e487bc68-e5eb-442e-bb81-8f769b895db5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6b7c858c-20ba-40c0-9e3d-ce3a9d0561be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019FCadZFqDewKSm4qfV2jYN","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"ff2fb5ac-e200-47e2-b2cd-c0b5d8a168da","timestamp":"2026-11-11T21:30:02.095Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md","oldString":"Related: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]","newString":"**Follow-up (2026-11-11):** the cleanup shipped as #508-#515 (exit_kind, one error-code registry test, pathspec chunking removed, AGENTS.md \"Enforcing an invariant\"). Verify audit claims before deleting: an auditor said clippy `map_err_ignore` made a scan test redundant, but it only flags bare `|_|`, so the test stayed; a `DryRun` newtype would have been a net addition (41 call sites), so skip when the type fix is bigger than the check. Agents' `%G?` reads `E` in the sandbox: confirm signatures with `gh api .../commits/<sha> --jq .commit.verification.reason`. The duplicate workspace load is deliberate for the validate flows; `note_once` stays.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]]","originalFile":"---\nname: rust-types-not-tests-lean\ndescription: \"Prefer compiler-enforced structure over tests, shell, text scans and string lists; delete before adding; no speculative generality. User called out over-engineering in the 0.20 stability batch.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\n  modified: 2026-11-11T17:48:56.843Z\n---\n\nIn Rust, enforce invariants with types (a trait bound, a private constructor, an exhaustive `match`) so the compiler checks them. A test is the fallback for what types cannot see, and it should be small.\n\n**Why:** In the 0.20 stability batch (2026-11-11) I let implementer agents add shell scripts plus text files to pin Action inputs, a source-text scan for `deny_unknown_fields`, a 21-invocation binary test for `schemaVersion` that the `Report` trait already guaranteed, a 233-code string list to classify exit codes, a Windows-length pathspec budget for an unsupported platform, and 15 new error codes (each a permanent frozen API). The user said \"you're not thinking in the rust way and you're over-engineering way too much\". The repo had already deleted a source-grepping test (#488).\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Before adding a test, ask whether a type or a private function makes the bug unrepresentable; do that instead. Reuse what is already in the tree (`insta`, `yaml-rust2`, `emit_report`/`Report`) rather than shell or text files.\n- No source-text scanning tests, no hand-maintained lists of strings that mirror code, no wall-clock assertions (count calls instead).\n- No code for unsupported platforms or hypothetical limits (docs/stability.md says Windows is unsupported).\n- Every new public surface (an error code, a JSON key, a flag) is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones.\n- Put \"prefer types, delete before adding, no speculative generality\" in every implementer brief, and review agent output for these before pushing.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]], [[feedback_measure_value_before_building]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: 6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","-  modified: 2026-11-11T17:48:56.843Z","+  modified: 2026-11-11T21:30:02.011Z"," ---"," "," In Rust, enforce invariants with types (a trait bound, a private constructor, an exhaustive `match`) so the compiler checks them. A test is the fallback for what types cannot see, and it should be small."]},{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":4,"newStart":19,"newLines":6,"lines":[" - Every new public surface (an error code, a JSON key, a flag) is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones."," - Put \"prefer types, delete before adding, no speculative generality\" in every implementer brief, and review agent output for these before pushing."," ","+**Follow-up (2026-11-11):** the cleanup shipped as #508-#515 (exit_kind, one error-code registry test, pathspec chunking removed, AGENTS.md \"Enforcing an invariant\"). Verify audit claims before deleting: an auditor said clippy `map_err_ignore` made a scan test redundant, but it only flags bare `|_|`, so the test stayed; a `DryRun` newtype would have been a net addition (41 call sites), so skip when the type fix is bigger than the check. Agents' `%G?` reads `E` in the sandbox: confirm signatures with `gh api .../commits/<sha> --jq .commit.verification.reason`. The duplicate workspace load is deliberate for the validate flows; `note_once` stays.","+"," Related: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]], [[feedback_measure_value_before_building]]."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e487bc68-e5eb-442e-bb81-8f769b895db5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
