WHY; never hard-wrap prose. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (five PASS lines). Push (`git push -u origin fix/flag-value-errors-exit-2`). No PR and no changeset (the caller writes them).\nBACKGROUND: docs/stability.md promises exit 2 for \"a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing\". Exit classification is `exit_kind()` (ExitKind::Usage / Runtime) on GraphError, ConfigError and CliError (crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs, crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs), naming only usage variants with `_ => Runtime`. A drift audit found the promise is not applied uniformly: an unknown package passed as a FLAG value exits 1 with E102 (reproduced: `add --package cargo/zzz:minor`, `matrix --package cargo/zzz`, `release --dry-run --package cargo/zzz`) while `release --package zzz` (E227) exits 2; `init --product-package` invalid (E189) exits 1 while `--forge-repository` (E195) and `--artifact-target` (E196) exit 2; E187, E188, E230, E232, E233 and E299 also exit 1 and the first four look like flag-value or flag-presence checks.\nTASK: make the exit code follow the rule: a failure caused by the value or combination of a COMMAND-LINE FLAG/ARGUMENT exits 2; failures caused by workspace, config-file, git, registry or release state exit 1. For EVERY error code that currently exits 1 and could be caused by a flag value (start with E102, E187, E188, E189, E230, E232, E233, E299, then scan the other runtime codes' call sites for ones that report a bad flag value), read each call site and decide: flag-caused => Usage; state-caused => leave Runtime. When one variant is reachable from BOTH a flag and a config file (E102 package-not-found may be: from `--package` vs a `callisto.toml` reference; compare how E316/E317 use a `context.starts_with(\"--\")` rule in ConfigError::exit_kind), classify by origin the same way and say how; if the variant carries no origin and adding one would be a signature change across many call sites, STOP on that code and report it instead. Do not guess: list each code with the call sites and your decision in the report.\nThen: update crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (real-binary tests) for the newly exit-2 flag cases (keep it small: one invocation per changed code family, runtime cases stay asserting 1), update the exit-code wording in docs/specs/cli.json where criteria state exit 1 for a case that now exits 2 (CLI-ADD-06 unknown package from `--package`, CLI-INIT-12 E187/E188/E189 etc.; verify each by running the binary), and add one sentence to docs/stability.md if it needs to say how a flag-vs-config origin is decided. Do NOT touch docs/errors.md.\nREPORT (under 250 words): a table (code, call sites, decision), anything you left Runtime on purpose and why, codes you stopped on, commit signed?, five verify results.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a444090653d1cbe25.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07d346d2-b968-4910-85b8-dae630fce803","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","branch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visi