ap prose. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (five PASS lines). Push (`git push -u origin docs/errors-fix-column`). No PR, no changeset, add no tests.\nTASK: docs/errors.md line ~11 says the \"Fix\" column is the code's help text verbatim, but a drift audit found several rows paraphrase it. The code is the source of truth. For every row, compare the Fix cell with the `help(\"...\")` string on the matching `#[diagnostic(code(E###), help(...))]` in crates/*/src (variants with no help or a formatted/dynamic help: see how the table treats them and keep that convention), and make the cell match the code's help text exactly (static text only; for formatted help with placeholders use the template as the file already does). Known mismatches to start with: E111 (doc 'Verify callisto.toml TOML syntax formatting.' vs code 'Fix the TOML syntax error at the reported line in callisto.toml.'), E169 (doc adds 'never a version `callisto snapshot` wrote' which the code help lacks; check whether the code enforces it before deciding whether to drop the clause from the doc or leave a clearly marked doc note), E158, E305, E306, E307, E316, E318, E319, E327, E328. Do the full table, not just these. Do not change the 'When' or meaning columns and do not edit any code. If a doc claim is a true statement the help lacks (like E169), keep it in the 'When' column rather than deleting information. Keep Markdown table formatting intact; run `just doc-check`.\nREPORT (under 120 words): number of rows changed, any row you left and why, commit signed?, five verify results.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a20e20f9f7f14f165.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07d346d2-b968-4910-85b8-dae630fce803","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/wo