{"parentUuid":"c96656a5-03a2-4ca7-9a26-909a8bdc1ff7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwxWNKezBduK1PXejiQc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The release PR #493 reads well as a user. It lists 15 changes with clear Breaking and Action notes, including the exit-2 entry and the leading-zero tag text from #511. One problem: GitHub shows it as `DIRTY`, meaning merge conflicts, even though it was regenerated recently at 22:44 UTC. I'd expect the release workflow to rebuild it on the next push to `main`, and I'll re-check after #515 and #495 merge, since I can't resolve conflicts on a generated branch.\n\n**Caliper change #224** needs a session started in the Caliper repo, since this one can't write there. Here is a ready prompt for it:\n\n> In `~/Projects/caliper` on branch `feat/checker-supplies-facts` (fetch origin first; the local main is far behind). In `crates/semantic/src/convert.rs`, the name-only traversal around line 400 calls `rpc.base_types` only when `states_bases(&info)` is true, and `states_bases` checks `OBJECT_CLASS | OBJECT_INTERFACE`. An instantiated generic interface such as `Props<string>` (with `interface Props<T> extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement> { value: T }`) has only the Reference object flag, so it returns an empty list and `composes` loses `HTMLAttributes`. First add a fixture and a failing test for that shape, then fix it by resolving the generic target of a Reference type and following that (check whether the RPC layer already has a call for the target). Run the repo's own checks by exit code, commit signed, one topic per PR.\n\nFive agents are running (Dependabot pin and config, the Python parser bug, uniform exit 2, `docs/errors.md` wording, and a read-only over-engineering audit). I'll review each branch and report as they land.\n\nneeds input: none. I'll bring back the results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3086,"cache_read_input_tokens":446301,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":511},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3086,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":446301,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3086},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"facbd9fe-4f6c-4c0e-bf41-d9a289108d72","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwxWN157QBMS7k7cgExU","requestRef":"2f84ff4f-f75d-4a27-a97d-a0aee90d61e5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"534e52cb-2f74-47f6-94c6-7dcbf5b027a6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:50:00.969Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a444090653d1cbe25","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
