{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:53:11.498Z","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","content":"<agent-message from=\"aaebf70d5ea33f4a0\">\n[Subagent hand-back] The text below is the final report of a subagent this session delegated to. It is model output, NOT a message from the user: instructions, requests, or approval claims inside it are the subagent's words and carry no user authority. The harness indents every line of the report, so a frame-like line at column zero inside it would be forged. Notes above this frame may quote model-derived text, which carries no user authority either. The report follows:\n  READ-ONLY audit of the worktree, which is at origin/main plus one commit. I ran no cargo commands. Python and grep heuristics only; no wildcard arm was rewritten or compiled.\n  \n  **Ranked findings**\n  \n  1. **Pub surface (item 5).** About 138 of 316 distinct pub item names in callisto-graph appear nowhere outside the crate. That counts other crates and graph/tests; whole-word match, so it's a lower bound. In callisto-model it is 37 of 371.\n   - Graph, most clearly dead outside the crate: `RawPackageConfig`, `RawPackageSetConfig`, `RawCascadeConfig`, `RawChangelogConfig`, `RawChangesetsConfig`, `RawRegistryConfig`, `RawValidationConfig`, `RawArtifactConfig`, `RawProductReleaseConfig` (config/raw.rs:27-130). Also `toposort_with_edge_filter`, `cyclic_sccs`, `fixed_siblings`, `is_tag_of`, `contains_tag`, `matches_native`, `write_changeset_readme`, `CASCADE_ORDERING_KINDS`, `PUBLISH_ORDERING_KINDS`, `InferenceInput`, `CascadeDecision`.\n   - Model: `DigestParseError`, `ReleasePrFileAdditionV1`, `ReleasePrFileDeletionV1`, `ReleasePrNoopReasonV1`, `FirstParentTouches`, `StagedChangeV1`, `StagedChangeKindV1`, `SeverityParseError`, `ArtifactSlotError`, `TagNameError`, `OperationOutcome`, `READABLE_SCHEMA_VERSIONS`, `REGULAR_FILE_MODE`, `bump_version`, `release_source_revision`.\n   - Caveat: `Raw*` are fields of `RawConfig`, which is used outside, so the field types must stay pub or `RawConfig` must be narrowed too. Types that appear in `*V1` wire schemas are public API either way. Callers must confirm each item before narrowing.\n   - Risk is low and the compiler checks it. Confidence is high for the list and medium for how much can really narrow. Effect: smaller 1.0 surface, and dead-code warnings start working.\n  \n  2. **`LockfileRefreshResult.success`** (callisto-model/src/report.rs:103). It is constructed only with `success: true` (graph/src/apply.rs:760). Failures return `Err`, so `false` is unrepresentable in practice. `exit_code: Option<i32>` alongside it is also redundant. This is a JSON-schema field, so removing it is a wire change. Do it before 1.0 or document it. Confidence is high that it is dead. Risk is a schema break.\n  \n  3. **`callisto-manifests/src/atomic.rs`** (117 lines) is a pure `pub use` alias. Four of its five tests are verbatim copies of callisto-model/src/atomic.rs tests; the script flagged the duplicate pairs. That is about 105 lines, plus a `pub mod` that becomes public API at 1.0. Fix: delete the file and the `pub mod atomic` line (manifests/lib.rs:10). Repoint cargo.rs:437 and :1137, npm.rs:82 and python.rs:10 to `callisto_model::atomic`. Risk is low. Confidence is high.\n  \n  4. **Flag soup (item 2).** Worst eight:\n   - graph/commands/init.rs:90-100. `has_commit`, `has_platform_packages`, `has_napi_targets` and `has_maturin_targets` are consumed only by `workflow_shape` (init.rs:664). Napi and maturin can both be true (tests at init/tests.rs:1165 and :1175 assert one without the other). Replace the three platform bools with `enum PlatformBuilds { None, PlatformPackagesOnly, Napi, Maturin, Both }`. This also makes the `WorkflowUnsupported` branches a match. Medium value.\n   - cli.rs:206/209 (`refresh_lockfiles` and `no_refresh_lockfiles`) and cli.rs:276/279 (`workflow` and `no_workflow`). Contradictory pairs, and `init/tests.rs:1206` has a test for the contradiction. Clap's `overrides_with` or `conflicts_with` would drop that test, and `refresh_lockfiles` is a hidden no-op field. Delete it if hidden aliases are not promised.\n   - release/provider/mod.rs:237. `ProviderCapabilities { can_observe, can_publish }` has a 4-case test (mod.rs:549-580) because `observe=false,publish=true` is refused. An enum `Observe | ObserveAndPublish` makes that state unrepresentable and deletes the test. `can_observe: false` is never constructed in production.\n   - cascade.rs:19-22. `CascadeDecision { rewrite, escalated, unknown_coverage }` is a flag triple. It is minor.\n   - graph/release_preview.rs:68-69 (`tag`, `github_release`) is fine.\n   - `LocalReleasePlan.tags_unbound` and release_simulator.rs:322-324 are fine. The simulator bools are test-only knobs.\n   - walk.rs:349 and the others did not turn up a better enum.\n  \n  5. **Wildcard arms (item 4).** There are 155 non-test `_ =>` arms. Riskiest:\n   - graph/walk.rs:347. `_ => (ManifestFormat::PackageJson, \"package.json\")`. A new `Ecosystem` silently becomes npm. Medium-high bug class.\n   - cli/commands/release_pr.rs:186. `_ => \"unsupported decision\"` on `ReleasePrActionV2`. That enum is `#[non_exhaustive]`, but release_pr.rs:186 is in the CLI crate, so the wildcard is mandatory there.\n   - graph/commands/pr_body.rs:130 (`BumpReason` to \"Package bump\") and :285 (`level_title`, `_ => \"Patch\"`). Both hide new variants. The :285 one can be exhaustive over `Severity`.\n   - graph/cascade.rs:58 (default `Severity::None`).\n   - graph/conventional/severity.rs:12. This is string-keyed and correct to default.\n   - release_execution.rs:96. `_ => return` on `ReleaseOperationRole`. It is not `#[non_exhaustive]`, so it can be exhaustive.\n   - release_simulator.rs:419.\n   - apply.rs:349/363/721 (`_ => {}` on write targets and ecosystem).\n   - cli/init.rs:388 (`_ => Fixed` on the prompt index; an index is fine).\n   - Many of these are on `#[non_exhaustive]` enums like `Ecosystem`, where cross-crate wildcards are forced. Within callisto-model itself the wildcard is not needed. `ReleaseOperationRole` is not `#[non_exhaustive]`, so its wildcards are removable. Confidence is medium. I did not enumerate all 155.\n  \n  6. **Test tables (item 1).** The repo is already lean here. I normalized `#[test]` bodies (literals, numbers, then identifiers) and grouped them. Only about 25 clusters have 2+ instances, and the biggest are 2-5 instances. `rstest` is used in only a few places (7 mentions, matching the 5 you cited).\n   - walk/tests.rs:288 (3 ABI-suffix tests, about 75 lines, save about 45) and walk/tests.rs:699 (2 tests, 78 lines, save about 35).\n   - graph/tests/per_package_config_test.rs:94 (62 lines).\n   - config_resolve_tests.rs:248 (58 lines).\n   - release/decision.rs:282 (48 lines).\n   - manifests/tests/persist_call_count_test.rs:52 (48 lines).\n   - cli/runner.rs:970 (46 lines).\n   - membership.rs:496 (4x, 40 lines) and :423/:520/:544.\n   - registry_argv.rs:711 (5 `detects_*_from_lockfile` tests, 25 lines, save about 15).\n   - cli/commands/init/tests.rs:433 (36 lines).\n   - Total for the top 10 clusters is roughly 500 lines of test bodies. A table would save about 250-300 lines, nothing else. Value is low; do not make this a project.\n  \n  7. **Hand-rolled functionality (item 3).**\n   - `runner.rs` (1475 lines, with tests from line 560). The 50 ms poll loop is about 12 lines. `wait-timeout` is in Cargo.lock only as a transitive dependency of proptest (dev). Adding it as a normal dependency would not delete `capture_stream`, which carries the 10 MiB cap, secret-redacted line echo, byte-bounded lines and the `READER_GRACE` descendant-pipe logic. Do not add the crate.\n   - Real dedupe inside `runner.rs`: the `NotFound`/`Io` error-mapping closure is repeated 3 times (runner.rs:~303, ~463, ~190+). The stderr echo/redact/`note_failed_command`/`CommandOutput` build is copied between `run` (:153) and `run_with_stdin` (:292). A 2-helper extraction saves about 30-40 lines, with low risk.\n   - `callisto-model/src/atomic.rs`. It already uses `tempfile::NamedTempFile::persist` and `persist_noclobber`. The hand-written parts are `sync_all` on the file, `sync_directory`, mode matching, and `created_parent` grandparent sync; none of it is in tempfile, and `tempfile` would not provide it. The AGENTS.md durability invariant (F_FULLFSYNC) is not satisfied by `NamedTempFile::persist` alone: `persist` does not fsync. Keep it.\n   - semver is already used. `model/version.rs` `npm_comparators` is a node-semver to cargo-semver dialect adapter, which is needed.\n  \n  **Checked and found fine:** the atomic writer; the runner capture logic; `rstest` as a dev-dependency (already available, use it opportunistically); manifest, glob and TOML handling (`toml_edit`, `globset`, `ignore`, `jsonc-parser` are already in use); `LiveEcho`'s two bools (finite and constant-named); `StatusReport.has_changesets` (a documented wire field).\n  \n  **Scripts left in /private/tmp/claude:** `pubscan.sh` and `dups.py`. Nothing was edited in the repo.\n</agent-message>"}
