e comments only for a non-obvious WHY; shell fixes must stay minimal (do not rewrite the test in another language, do not add scripts or helpers). Verify by exit code with the repo's `just workflow-contracts` (run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; exit 0). Push `git push -u origin fix/flaky-release-pr-contract`. No PR, no changeset.\nPROBLEM: `just workflow-contracts` failed once with exit 141 (SIGPIPE) in `.github/actions/callisto-action/tests/test_release_pr_contract.sh`, on the case \"a release PR built from an older tip must stay a draft\" (~lines 476-490), and passed on re-run. It is flaky and can flake CI. The script runs under `set -euo pipefail` (check the head of the file and of the scripts it calls: `.github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/create-or-update-release-pr.sh` and any helper); SIGPIPE typically comes from a pipeline whose reader exits early (`grep -q`, `head -n1`, `read` from a here-string) while the writer is still writing, under pipefail.\nTASK: 1) Find the pipelines in the test script and the action scripts it exercises that can SIGPIPE (grep for `| grep -q`, `| head`, `| jq -e ... |`, `printf ... | read`, `echo ... | grep -q` under pipefail). 2) Reproduce: run the test script in a loop (e.g. 100-300 iterations in this shell with a plain `for` loop, counting non-zero exits and recording the exit codes; use the exact invocation `just workflow-contracts` runs for this file). Report the rate. 3) Fix each SIGPIPE-prone pipeline minimally (use `grep -q <<<\"$var\"` or capture the output into a variable first, or `|| true` only where truly intended), keeping the test's meaning identical. 4) Re-run the loop to show zero failures over the same count, then run `just workflow-contracts` (exit 0).\nREPORT (under 150 words): the culprit lines, repro rate before and after, the diff size, commit signed?, the exit code of `just workflow-contracts`. If you cannot reproduce in 300 iterations, say so, list the pipelines you consider risky, and fix only those you can justify.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/ada94700137762e4a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"38146f41-46f1-4637-b2de-4d92c14f558e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","branch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02f09293-5e1b-4b26-971c-94e8e35a480f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"ci/dependabot-composite-actions","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
