{"parentUuid":"6c3b4ddb-20fb-44e7-ab0e-6b1a4e6fab62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwyh3jdsew5T2WDduaXv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two more PRs are open, and #516 is now green.\n\n- **#516 (Dependabot bump):** after the pin fix on its branch, all checks pass (Clippy, tests, coverage, Workflow Contracts, Entire Gates, artifact preflights). It's ready for you to merge.\n- **#519 (Python parser):** fixes parse, render, parse idempotency. The root cause was `trim_start_matches('[')` and `trim_end_matches(']')` stripping every repeated bracket. It now strips one pair, and the proptest seed is checked in. 200,000-case runs found nothing else.\n- **#520 (Dependabot config):** adds `/.github/actions/*` to the github-actions directories so future bumps update composite actions. The PR says plainly that this can't be tested locally; the next action bump will show whether it works.\n- **#517 (cargo bump):** nothing is failing (16 passing, 1 skipped).\n\nAlso open from earlier: #515, #518 and #495.\n\n**New finding:** two agents hit the same `workflow-contracts` flake (`test_release_contract.sh` and `test_release_pr_contract.sh`, SIGPIPE exit 141). An agent is looping the test to reproduce it and fix the pipelines that can SIGPIPE under `pipefail`.\n\nStill running: the flake fix, uniform exit 2, the atomic alias, the exhaustive matches, and the flags-to-enums branch.\n\nneeds input: none. I'll review each as it reports."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":512681,"output_tokens":495,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"out