{"parentUuid":"941f77ce-dc08-4f47-a742-8328676276d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwz45nzrH6iqcmtWXt25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013HHyizSaHMXdn4eseNupAt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_atomic.md","content":"## Summary\n- Delete `callisto_manifests::atomic`, a one-line re-export of `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`, and point its callers (`callisto-manifests` cargo/npm/python, `callisto-graph` `apply.rs`, `callisto-cli` `pre.rs`) at `callisto_model::atomic` directly.\n- Move the one test the model crate lacked, concurrent `atomic_write`, into `callisto-model/src/atomic.rs`, condensed with `thread::scope`.\n- Why: the alias was a backward-compat shim that kept two paths to one function. Four of its five tests were verbatim copies of tests already in `callisto-model`, and the fifth only checked that the alias was the same function. Net -127/+24 lines.\n- No behavior change. `atomic_write` itself is untouched.\n- Removes the public module `callisto_manifests::atomic`. The docs describe that crate as internal, so I expect no outside users; that is inferred from the docs, not checked against external dependents. Anyone importing it must switch to `callisto_model::atomic`.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: no CLI flag, output or `callisto.toml` change.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: internal crate API only, nothing a CLI user can observe.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just test` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once in `test_release_pr_contract.sh`, a shell test this diff does not touch, and exited 0 on re-run; that flake is being investigated separately.\n- [x] Concurrent-write coverage is kept: the model crate now has the concurrent `atomic_write` test that previously lived only in the deleted file.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9487,"cache_read_input_tokens":543294,"output_tokens":1856,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":241},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9487,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1856,"cache_read_input_tokens":543294,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9487},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013HHyizSaHMXdn4eseNupAt":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_atomic.md","content":"## Summary\n- Delete `callisto_manifests::atomic`, a one-line re-export of `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`, and point its callers (`callisto-manifests` cargo/npm/python, `callisto-graph` `apply.rs`, `callisto-cli` `pre.rs`) at `callisto_model::atomic` directly.\n- Move the one test the model crate lacked, concurrent `atomic_write`, into `callisto-model/src/atomic.rs`, condensed with `thread::scope`.\n- Why: the alias was a backward-compat shim that kept two paths to one function. Four of its five tests were verbatim copies of tests already in `callisto-model`, and the fifth only checked that the alias was the same function. Net -127/+24 lines.\n- No behavior change. `atomic_write` itself is untouched.\n- Removes the public module `callisto_manifests::atomic`. The docs describe that crate as internal, so I expect no outside users; that is inferred from the docs, not checked against external dependents. Anyone importing it must switch to `callisto_model::atomic`.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: no CLI flag, output or `callisto.toml` change.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: internal crate API only, nothing a CLI user can observe.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just test` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once in `test_release_pr_contract.sh`, a shell test this diff does not touch, and exited 0 on re-run; that flake is being investigated separately.\n- [x] Concurrent-write coverage is kept: the model crate now has the concurrent `atomic_write` test that previously lived only in the deleted file.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0536e837-3066-456d-b3df-694a92c6ac14","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgwz458KWaUhHMbGx2gPt","requestRef":"13c541b8-2dc1-49a3-a019-8dbdac0827a3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b1eb1d3-b61f-4f99-975f-20f00635fedb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:10:15.634Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a444090653d1cbe25","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/flaky-release-pr-contract","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9b1eb1d3-b61f-4f99-975f-20f00635fedb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwz45nzrH6iqcmtWXt25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vb2jd7oX5BrPZ9fM7KDbhr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_caps.md","content":"## Summary\n- Deletes `ProviderCapabilities { can_observe, can_publish }`, the `capabilities()` trait method, `require_observable`, the `ReleasePreconditionRequirement::ObservableProvider` variant and the two tests that only exercised them. `checked_provider_for` becomes the infallible `provider_for` (13 call sites in `capability.rs`). Net +32/-173.\n- Why: the struct allowed an invalid state (observe=false, publish=true was refused at runtime and needed a 4-case test), but every production provider was always `{true, true}`, so the check could never fire. Nothing serializes the struct, and `ObservableProvider` was a thiserror display variant that nothing could produce any more (also not serialized). Deleting the type removes the invalid state instead of replacing the flags with an enum that would have exactly one live value.\n- No behavior change: no provider, config key, CLI output or error message a user can reach is affected.\n- Not done: an enum for the four `has_*` bools in `init.rs` `workflow_shape`. It would add about as many lines as it removes and rewrite six test fixtures, so it is not a net simplification.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: internal types only, no observable behavior change.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once with no failure visible, then 0 on a clean re-run; a known flaky shell test is being investigated separately.\n- [x] The deleted tests covered only the removed capability checks, so no coverage of reachable behavior is lost.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9487,"cache_read_input_tokens":543294,"output_tokens":1856,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":241},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9487,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1856,"cache_read_input_tokens":543294,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9487},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Vb2jd7oX5BrPZ9fM7KDbhr":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_caps.md","content":"## Summary\n- Deletes `ProviderCapabilities { can_observe, can_publish }`, the `capabilities()` trait method, `require_observable`, the `ReleasePreconditionRequirement::ObservableProvider` variant and the two tests that only exercised them. `checked_provider_for` becomes the infallible `provider_for` (13 call sites in `capability.rs`). Net +32/-173.\n- Why: the struct allowed an invalid state (observe=false, publish=true was refused at runtime and needed a 4-case test), but every production provider was always `{true, true}`, so the check could never fire. Nothing serializes the struct, and `ObservableProvider` was a thiserror display variant that nothing could produce any more (also not serialized). Deleting the type removes the invalid state instead of replacing the flags with an enum that would have exactly one live value.\n- No behavior change: no provider, config key, CLI output or error message a user can reach is affected.\n- Not done: an enum for the four `has_*` bools in `init.rs` `workflow_shape`. It would add about as many lines as it removes and rewrite six test fixtures, so it is not a net simplification.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: internal types only, no observable behavior change.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once with no failure visible, then 0 on a clean re-run; a known flaky shell test is being investigated separately.\n- [x] The deleted tests covered only the removed capability checks, so no coverage of reachable behavior is lost.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0536e837-3066-456d-b3df-694a92c6ac14","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cgwz458KWaUhHMbGx2gPt","requestRef":"13c541b8-2dc1-49a3-a019-8dbdac0827a3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"adcd6d7d-d09a-4d58-aaf8-72fe64ffe9c9","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:10:18.842Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a444090653d1cbe25","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/flaky-release-pr-contract","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
