{"parentUuid":"38398d8e-81fb-4792-bb02-e694fed5df0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwz9PzWtPCsrtyRj8P9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019JfRBtAatkoNXFMFup5uZB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit2.md","content":"## Summary\n- Errors caused by a flag's value now exit 2 instead of 1, matching `docs/stability.md`, which promises exit 2 for a bad or missing argument or flag, including values validated after parsing. A script that checked for exit 1 after a bad flag now sees 2.\n- Now exit 2 (via `exit_kind()`): unknown `--package` on add, matrix and release (E102); invalid `init --forge-repository` (E187) and `--product-package` (E189); `release pending --from` that is not a release commit (E328); a repeated `--package` in a release selection (E169, Duplicate reason only); invalid `--decision`, `--preview` or `--snapshot` values (E281); `release execute` flags that contradict the intent (E232, E233); `release plan --artifact-repository` that mismatches the config (E230, plan site only: a `from_flag: bool` field was added to that variant's two call sites, no new code or key).\n- Still exit 1 on purpose: a valid flag meeting workspace, config, git or intent state that cannot support it (E188, E299, E219, E308, E304, E202, E234, E277, E123, E124), and the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or `pre.json`. The rule is now one sentence in `docs/stability.md`.\n- E103 is unchanged: `add --package` reaches it, but a changeset can too through `version`, and the variant carries no origin.\n- Decision to confirm before merge: this changes exit codes on a surface that freezes at 1.0. It follows an agent-assisted recommendation, so please confirm the 1-versus-2 split, in particular the flag-sourced versus state-sourced boundary and leaving E103 at 1.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n- [x] Breaking change: exit codes are a documented CLI surface. Migration: a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2; a check for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Extended the unreleased `.changeset/usage-errors-exit-2.md` rather than adding a new one.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] `docs/stability.md` states the rule. Spec text updated in `docs/specs/cli.json` (CLI-ADD-06, CLI-INIT-12), `docs/specs/matrix.json` and `docs/specs/release.json`. No new error codes or keys, so `docs/errors.md` and `docs/config.md` are unchanged.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just test` exit 0. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once in an unrelated flaky shell test (`test_release_pr_contract.sh`, SIGPIPE exit 141) and passed on re-run.\n- [x] Real-binary cases in `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`: one each for E102, E169, E328 and E281, plus a new init test (E187 and E189 exit 2, E188 exits 1, which pins the boundary).\n- [ ] Not covered by binary tests: E230, E232, E233, because they need the release-plan machinery.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5739,"cache_read_input_tokens":556889,"output_tokens":1248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5739,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1248,"cache_read_input_tokens":556889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5739},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019JfRBtAatkoNXFMFup5uZB":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit2.md