{"parentUuid":"d364dc23-c6e3-4c9d-8f5c-58e8216d4145","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzAndaeLnfNmczHGgqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The flake came from the test stub never reading stdin, so the pipeline hit SIGPIPE and `pipefail` returned 141; I reproduced it at 2.1% before the fix and 0% after. I'm opening that two-line PR now, along with the exit-2 and exhaustive-matches PRs.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5376,"cache_read_input_tokens":566394,"output_tokens":2048,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5376,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2048,"cache_read_input_tokens":566394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5376},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"af1f8fd3-500f-476a-9511-1dc556be033a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwzAnGkNbswRULeQ8z8n","requestRef":"58d918ef-fbde-4828-b11c-840abe7b7e27","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b71b9444-3596-430c-8a2c-6841fdecbdfb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:11:46.010Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a444090653d1cbe25","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/flag-value-errors-exit-2","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b71b9444-3596-430c-8a2c-6841fdecbdfb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzAndaeLnfNmczHGgqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EtDRqNy6Vt6tQWCCYDC369","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exhaustive.md","content":"## Summary\n- Replace wildcard `_ =>` arms on Callisto's own enums with named variants, so adding a variant fails to compile at each site instead of silently taking the fallback. Covers `Ecosystem`, `Severity`, `ReleaseOperationRole`, `FaultKind`, `Remote` and `TraceEvent`.\n- In `callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`, the old `match eco { Cargo, Npm, Pypi, _ => PackageJson }` would have turned any new ecosystem into an npm manifest. It now uses the existing `Ecosystem::canonical_manifest_format()` and `ManifestFormat::file_name()`, and skips ecosystems with no canonical format. The wildcard there was the worst case because the fallback was a wrong answer (npm), not a neutral default.\n- No behavior change for Cargo, npm and pypi. For Go, Maven, NuGet, Deno and Jsr (`canonical_manifest_format()` is `None`), `walk.rs` now skips them where it used to emit a `package.json` declaration. I did not check whether those ecosystems can reach that loop today.\n- Left alone on purpose: `BumpReason` in `pr_body.rs` (non-exhaustive in `callisto-model`, and an exhaustive match would put PR-body text in the model crate), `apply.rs` (guarded arms, and a match over the other crate's `Ecosystem`), and the `exit_kind` `_ => Runtime` fallback.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: no observable change for the supported ecosystems.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once in an unrelated flaky shell test and passed on re-run; the fix is a separate PR.\n- [x] No new tests: the compiler enforces the change, and the existing tests cover the Cargo, npm and pypi paths.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5376,"cache_read_input_tokens":566394,"output_tokens":2048,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5376,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2048,"cache_read_input_tokens":566394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5376},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EtDRqNy6Vt6tQWCCYDC369":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exhaustive.md","content":"## Summary\n- Replace wildcard `_ =>` arms on Callisto's own enums with named variants, so adding a variant fails to compile at each site instead of silently taking the fallback. Covers `Ecosystem`, `Severity`, `ReleaseOperationRole`, `FaultKind`, `Remote` and `TraceEvent`.\n- In `callisto-graph/src/walk.rs`, the old `match eco { Cargo, Npm, Pypi, _ => PackageJson }` would have turned any new ecosystem into an npm manifest. It now uses the existing `Ecosystem::canonical_manifest_format()` and `ManifestFormat::file_name()`, and skips ecosystems with no canonical format. The wildcard there was the worst case because the fallback was a wrong answer (npm), not a neutral default.\n- No behavior change for Cargo, npm and pypi. For Go, Maven, NuGet, Deno and Jsr (`canonical_manifest_format()` is `None`), `walk.rs` now skips them where it used to emit a `package.json` declaration. I did not check whether those ecosystems can reach that loop today.\n- Left alone on purpose: `BumpReason` in `pr_body.rs` (non-exhaustive in `callisto-model`, and an exhaustive match would put PR-body text in the model crate), `apply.rs` (guarded arms, and a match over the other crate's `Ecosystem`), and the `exit_kind` `_ => Runtime` fallback.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: no observable change for the supported ecosystems.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally. `just workflow-contracts` exited 1 once in an unrelated flaky shell test and passed on re-run; the fix is a separate PR.\n- [x] No new tests: the compiler enforces the change, and the existing tests cover the Cargo, npm and pypi paths.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"af1f8fd3-500f-476a-9511-1dc556be033a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwzAnGkNbswRULeQ8z8n","requestRef":"58d918ef-fbde-4828-b11c-840abe7b7e27","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"87b452a2-f861-4b4c-bf05-e41f779cbbf5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:11:49.300Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a444090653d1cbe25","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/flag-value-errors-exit-2","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
