{"parentUuid":"ae589231-bf86-4199-87a6-7cc9eb87c9ef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"55fd7449-25d6-4254-8edc-5f53ec06365a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FjmZTJhMF2ZHXyd16GYQgv","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_flake.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"dcf3a9af-e47a-4bf3-9f70-8b534ee61049","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:11:52.928Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_flake.md","content":"## Summary\n- `just workflow-contracts` occasionally failed with exit 141 (SIGPIPE) in `test_release_pr_contract.sh`, and passed on re-run. Four agents and one Dependabot PR hit it.\n- Cause: `create-or-update-release-pr.sh` runs `printf '%s' \"$existing_body\" | callisto compose-pr-body ... --existing-body -`. The test's `callisto` stub never read stdin in its `compose-pr-body` arm, so if the stub exited before `printf` finished writing, `printf` took SIGPIPE and `pipefail` made it exit 141. The real binary reads stdin, so only the stub was affected.\n- Fix: the stub drains stdin when `--existing-body -` is passed. Two lines in one file.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix: test stub only, no production code.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: test stub only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just workflow-contracts` exits 0\n- [x] The exact pipeline shape, run in isolation 3,000 times under `pipefail`, failed 63 times (2.1%) before the change and 0 times after\n- [ ] Not reproduced in the full script: it takes about 3 minutes per run, so a few hundred iterations were not practical. The diagnosis rests on the isolated reproduction and on reading the stub, which never read stdin.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"af1f8fd3-500f-476a-9511-1dc556be033a","context":{"git_state":{