{"parentUuid":"307b48de-35dc-4ae8-8a7b-b586f77362bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzEWFSvbFTiZhdETBPS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All seven PRs from this batch are open and every commit on them shows `valid` on GitHub. CI hasn't run on them yet, and merging is yours.\n\n| PR | Content |\n|---|---|\n| #519 | Python parser: stray `[` in extras now round-trips. The bug was repeated-bracket trimming, and the proptest seed is checked in. |\n| #520 | Dependabot now updates composite actions under `.github/actions/`. |\n| #521 | Removes the 117-line `callisto_manifests::atomic` alias (net −127/+24, removes a public module of a crate documented as internal). |\n| #522 | Deletes `ProviderCapabilities` (net +32/−173), because every production provider was always `{true, true}`. |\n| #523 | Flag-caused failures exit 2 (E102, E187, E189, E328, E169, E281, E232, E233, E230). It extends the existing `usage-errors-exit-2.md` changeset. The PR text asks you to confirm the 1-versus-2 split, and I left E103 at 1. |\n| #524 | Exhaustive matches on our own enums. A new `Ecosystem` can no longer silently become npm in `walk.rs`. |\n| #525 | Fixes the flaky `workflow-contracts` test: the `callisto` stub never read stdin, so `printf` took SIGPIPE (exit 141). The same pipeline shape failed 2.1% of runs before the fix and 0% after, but it was not reproduced in the full script. |\n\nAlso now green: #516 (Dependabot bump), and #517 had nothing failing.\n\n**Not done, needs you**\n- **Release PR #493 (0.20.0):** GitHub showed it as conflicting (DIRTY) earlier. I'll re-read it after your merges. #523 changes its exit-2 note, which is already in the 0.20.0 notes.\n- **`LockfileRefreshResult.success`:** the field is always true. Removing it changes the JSON schema, so I left it for your decision.\n- **Caliper change #224:** it needs a session in the Caliper repo, and I gave you the prompt earlier.\n- **`NEXT-W