{"parentUuid":"43b2de9c-1f29-4264-9426-4f7115f68b0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx7xHbBTSvNWuvagXT6C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lg8NKvfDQwTiq4ypJexFLq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"1.0 blockers verification audit","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), main checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (use `git show origin/main:<path>`; run `git fetch origin` is fine). Read AGENTS.md, docs/stability.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/adr/README.md. The local plan /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md and its archive are STALE (written for 0.14, now 0.20): treat every item there as a lead, verify against current code before believing it.\nGOAL: produce the verified list of what actually stands between Callisto 0.20 and a credible 1.0 (lockstep versioning, all four crates to 1.0, libraries documented internal are already decided). Check:\n1. docs/stability.md promises vs reality for anything still unpinned: list each promise and whether code or a test enforces it (exit codes, JSON envelope/camelCase, error-code permanence, tag formats, Action inputs/outputs, callisto.toml keys, schemaVersion per report). Flag promises with no enforcement and surfaces that exist but are not promised (JSON keys, flags, config keys that would freeze by accident).\n2. Open ADRs and owner-decision items in NEXT-WORK.md: for each, is it still open (check ADR status, code, `gh issue list --limit 50` and `gh pr list --state open`), what is the smallest action, and does it block 1.0 or can it follow it.\n3. Release pipeline safety gaps: re-verify the 'manual Ready for review override' gap and the two small E165 help changes noted earlier (search docs/adr and code for E165, release hold/retry); anything in AGENTS.md or incident memory that says a fix was declared but not shipped.\n4. Spec drift: docs/specs/*.json criteria vs behavior for a sample of 25 criteria across the commands NOT covered by the recent audit (the audit covered cli.json exit codes, errors.md, config.md keys, JSON envelopes): pick criteria in release.json, versioning.json, changelog or matrix specs and test them against the binary on a temp fixture.\n5. Quick performance sanity: `just bench` or the benches in crates/callisto-cli/benches if they run in under 5 minutes; report numbers for 200 and 1,800 packages vs the previous numbers in docs or PR #507 (release --dry-run about 1.3 s at 1,800).\nREPORT (under 700 words): ranked list of verified 1.0 blockers (with evidence and smallest fix), then things that can wait, then stale items you found already done. Mark anything you could not verify. Do not pad."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_read_input_tokens":592520,"output_tokens":3527,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1392},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1012,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3527,"cache_read_input_tokens":592520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1012},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Lg8NKvfDQwTiq4ypJexFLq":{"description":"1.0 blockers verification audit","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), main checkout /Use