{"parentUuid":"83ac27d8-8ae4-4428-a46c-09e849b22ff9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx83n4atYRAjFsg58b54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The merged batch is cleaned up and two agents are working on the next set.\n\n**Cleaned up:** 9 more worktrees and their local branches are removed. Each was clean with nothing unpushed, and I also deleted 8 stray `worktree-agent-*` and `fix-pin` branches. Kept: my current worktree (`fix/flag-value-errors-exit-2`, merged, removable at the end), the two running agents' worktrees, and the three `chore/callisto-*` branches in `~/Projects/callisto-fixtures/` that aren't mine.\n\n**Release PR #493 (0.20.0):** it's a draft because the hold workflow is refreshing it after your merges, and CI on `main` is still queued. I'll re-read the rendered changelog once it's ready for review. The earlier conflict state has cleared (it now shows UNKNOWN, meaning still recalculating).\n\n**Running now (Sonnet)**\n- **1.0 blockers check (read-only):** `NEXT-WORK.md` is stale, so this verifies what really stands between 0.20 and 1.0. It checks unenforced `stability.md` promises, open ADRs and owner items, the release-safety gaps, 25 spec criteria not covered by the earlier audit, and a performance sanity run at 200 and 1,800 packages.\n- **`LockfileRefreshResult.success` removal:** it removes the always-true field if `stability.md` allows it with a `schemaVersion` bump pre-1.0, and stops and reports instead of forcing it if the change is inconsistent. I made this call myself, so it's flagged for your confirmation in its PR.\n\nneeds input: none yet. I'll bring back the blockers list and the removal result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":823,"cache_read_input_tokens":604573,"output_tokens":565,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_sear