{"parentUuid":"d0d9be0c-0de6-4480-a64e-df5fb20bf223","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx8LFNLbYVeefqSjtuTG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `LockfileRefreshResult` branch is pushed, and its changeset is being drafted.\n\n- **Change:** removes `success` and `exitCode` from the lockfile refresh result in the `version` report. `success` was only ever `true` (a failed refresh returns E208), and `exitCode` just mirrored it.\n- **Version bump:** the shared `PACKAGE_REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION` goes 2 to 3. That means `status`, `snapshot` and `matrix` also report `schemaVersion: 3` even though only the `version` report changed shape. The constant is shared on purpose (its doc comment says the four package reports move together), so splitting it would add a constant. I'll flag it plainly in the PR so you can choose.\n- **Files:** `report.rs`, `apply.rs`, the schema-guard and CLI tests, and the `cli.json` and `matrix.json` specs. The five repo checks exit 0, per the agent. I haven't confirmed the commit shows `valid` on GitHub yet, because the agent's local check hit a shell error.\n\nNext: the changeset lands on the branch, then the PR text, then the PR. The 1.0 blockers check is still running.\n\nneeds input: none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":612630,"output_tokens":406,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":612630,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_