{"parentUuid":"12a69303-5e55-4b4e-abbd-cdb01ece7ca7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"46a99c82-2069-4d31-b822-5b5effb1145d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TNf919irUGz5Ag2xN5qq7C","type":"tool_result","content":"## Release Preview\n\nThis automated PR was generated by [Callisto](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto). Merging this PR will publish the updated packages to their release targets.\n\n### 📊 Release Summary\n\n| Package | Ecosystem | Current | Target | Bump | Reason |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-cli` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Changeset (`camel-case-json-fields`) |\n| `callisto-fixtures` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-graph` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-manifests` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-model` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **5 package(s)** queued for versioning. Minor bumps below 1.0.0 can include breaking changes, so read the changes below before merging.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Read before merging**\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it, and replace `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` with `\"off\"`.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a script checks for `command == \"release\"` on a failing `release pending`, match `release pending` instead.\n\n### 🚀 Merging will publish\n\n| Package | Goes to |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-model` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-manifests` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-graph` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-cli` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag · GitHub release · 5 assets |\n\nVersioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).\n\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**15 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Every JSON field Callisto writes is now camelCase, so scripts see one naming style.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `version` and `snapshot` `--format json` reports: `reason.dep_kind` and `reason.dependency_to` are now `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n- Release plumbing files: the preview's `short_sha` is `shortSha`, and the receipt's `peeled_commit`, `tag_name` and `byte_length` are `peeledCommit`, `tagName` and `byteLength`.\n- A test now walks every report and file type and fails on a snake_case key.\n\nBreaking: scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n\nAction: keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n\nPull request #498\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Mistyped config keys and pre-release tags are caught where you make them.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- An unknown key inside a `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` block now fails with an error naming the key. Before, it was silently ignored.\n- `callisto pre enter` rejects a tag with a space, `!`, `/`, an empty part or a number with a leading zero such as `01` (E324) and writes nothing. Before, it wrote `pre.json` and `version` failed later with a confusing version error. Dotted tags such as `beta.1` still work.\n\n- `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` is rejected (E256). It was accepted as `off` but never documented; use `\"off\"`.\n\nAction: if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it, and replace `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` with `\"off\"`.\n\nPull request #501\n\n</details>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cda3e3cf-69d4-47c4-9802-5eb6ba4016fd","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:07:36.799Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Release Preview\n\nThis automated PR was generated by [Callisto](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto). Merging this PR will publish the updated packages to their release targets.\n\n### 📊 Release Summary\n\n| Package | Ecosystem | Current | Target | Bump | Reason |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-cli` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Changeset (`camel-case-json-fields`) |\n| `callisto-fixtures` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-graph` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-manifests` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-model` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **5 package(s)** queued for versioning. Minor bumps below 1.0.0 can include breaking changes, so read the changes below before merging.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Read before merging**\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it, and replace `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` with `\"off\"`.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a script checks for `command == \"release\"` on a failing `release pending`, match `release pending` instead.\n\n### 🚀 Merging will publish\n\n| Package | Goes to |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-model` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-manifests` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-graph` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-cli` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag · GitHub release · 5 assets |\n\nVersioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).\n\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**15 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Every JSON field Callisto writes is now camelCase, so scripts see one naming style.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `version` and `snapshot` `--format json` reports: `reason.dep_kind` and `reason.dependency_to` are now `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n- Release plumbing files: the preview's `short_sha` is `shortSha`, and the receipt's `peeled_commit`, `tag_name` and `byte_length` are `peeledCommit`, `tagName` and `byteLength`.\n- A test now walks every report and file type and fails on a snake_case key.\n\nBreaking: scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n\nAction: keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n\nPull request #498\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Mistyped config keys and pre-release tags are caught where you make them.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- An unknown key inside a `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` block now fails with an error naming the key. Before, it was silently ignored.\n- `callisto pre enter` rejects a tag with a space, `!`, `/`, an empty part or a number with a leading zero such as `01` (E324) and writes nothing. Before, it wrote `pre.json` and `version` failed later with a confusing version error. Dotted tags such as `beta.1` still work.\n\n- `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` is rejected (E256). It was accepted as `off` but never documented; use `\"off\"`.\n\nAction: if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it, and replace `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` with `\"off\"`.\n\nPull request #501\n\n</details>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"