{"parentUuid":"6db5a27f-678c-4088-a4aa-e44e73cc38ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx91eMYUs5CfrbweMpor","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FzHsRQinM8X2zoAd2F8tzi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr view 493 --json body --jq '.body' | sed -n 75,200p | cut -c1-300","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2154,"cache_read_input_tokens":625095,"output_tokens":672,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":544},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2154,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":625095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2154},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FzHsRQinM8X2zoAd2F8tzi":{"command":"gh pr view 493 --json body --jq '.body' | sed -n 75,200p | cut -c1-300","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d75ab957-0f25-4870-91db-76af9778f469","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgx91e5vMRpRWLPa42xVT","requestRef":"263b11a6-7585-4ebb-a1b9-b52c6cd5b2ba","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e11a9f6-dc3d-49d1-bc00-bd0c53f57cdd","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:07:42.611Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a4acf55fce15d0b8f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9e11a9f6-dc3d-49d1-bc00-bd0c53f57cdd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"46a99c82-2069-4d31-b822-5b5effb1145d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzHsRQinM8X2zoAd2F8tzi","type":"tool_result","content":"</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Each configuration mistake now has its own error code, so a script or a person can tell them apart.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- E254 is retired. A bad `publish-to` is E330, `release-trigger` E331, `cascade.mode` E332, `changelog.layout` E333, a registry `kind` E334, `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry E335, `url` on a Cargo registry E336, a registry timeout E337, and an unparsable package `match` E338. Before, all of thes\n- A registry `kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem is E339. Before, it reported E171, which means an internal defect, so it looked like a bug in Callisto.\n- Exit codes are unchanged.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n\nPull request #506\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Error codes now each name one condition, so a script can tell problems apart from the code.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto.toml`: E111 is only a TOML syntax error. An unknown key is E325, and a value of the wrong type or a missing required key is E326.\n- `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327, and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328. Before, both showed E171, which means an internal defect.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n\nPull request #500\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Breaking: eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What changed**\n- `--format json` output never contains `napi-coordination-not-yet-supported`, `pre-major-inference-inert`, `changelog-section-not-found`, `changeset-read-error`, `git-discovery-failed`, `changelog-read-error`, `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` or `publish-target-not-implemented`\n- The `DiagnosticCode` enum in the schema no longer lists them\n\n**Action**\n- Remove any match on these codes from scripts; a schema validator pinned to the old enum should be updated\n\nPull request #489\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. Many project templates give that root a version such as `0.0.0`, and until now Callisto listed it as a package even though it only holds scripts and tooling, is never \n- `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.\n- To version the root anyway, add a `[[package]]` block to `callisto.toml` with `match = \"npm/<name>\"`, where `<name>` is the root's `package.json` name, such as `match = \"npm/monorepo\"`.\n\nPull request #490\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Usage errors now exit 2, as the stability promise says, so a script can tell a mistake in the command from a failure in…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\nUsage errors now exit 2, as the stability promise says, so a script can tell a mistake in the command from a failure in the workspace.\n\n- A bad or missing flag value that Callisto checks after parsing now exits 2, like a clap-level mistake always did. Examples: `add --package a:patch`, `add --package cargo/a:bogus`, `add` without `--summary`, `init` without `--yes` and without a terminal, `snapshot --tag` with a space, and `--dry-ru\n- Also exit 2: an unknown package passed to `--package` on `add`, `matrix` or `release` (E102), an invalid `init --forge-repository` (E187) or `--product-package` (E189), a `release pending --from` that is not a release commit (E328), a repeated `--package` in a release selection (E169), an invalid \n- The rule: exit 2 when a flag value or combination is rejected, exit 1 when a valid flag meets state that cannot support it. Failures about your workspace, config, git, registries or release intent (for example E188, E299, E219, E308) still exit 1, and so does the same value read from `callisto.tom\n- The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n\nAction: a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n\nPull request #502\n\n</details>\n\n#### 🟢 Patch\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto add</code> no longer writes a changeset that Callisto's own tools reject, and <code>status</code> JSON has the same fields for…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n`callisto add` no longer writes a changeset that Callisto's own tools reject, and `status` JSON has the same fields for every package.\n\n- `add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` now fails with E329 and writes nothing. Before, it wrote both lines, and `status --check` then failed on the file.\n- `status --format json`: `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` print `null` when there is none instead of being left out, so every package record has the same keys.\n- The `--strict` help for `snapshot` and `version` now says what the flag does: it turns warnings into errors, and graph errors abort either way.\n\nPull request #503\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>version --emit-preview</code> is faster in large monorepos.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- The check for packages that changed since their last release now asks git once for all packages tagged at the same release, instead of once per package.\n- In a test workspace with 150 changed packages, that went from 151 git calls to 4, and from 3.8 s to 1.0 s.\n\nPull request #494\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A mistyped package name now gets a suggestion, so you can fix it from the error alone.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto add --package cargo/libb:minor` adds ``did you mean `cargo/lib`?`` to the E102 error, with up to three close matches.\n- A wrong ecosystem is caught too: `npm/lib` suggests `cargo/lib`.\n- When nothing is close, the error is unchanged.\n\nPull request #491\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Notes about packages Callisto skips are printed once per run.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- Before, a command that loads the workspace more than once, such as `callisto init`, printed the same note up to three times.\n- This covers the notes for a crate with no version and for an ignored private workspace root.\n\nPull request #496\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto release</code> and the release PR are much faster in very large monorepos.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- With about 1,500 of 1,800 packages releasing at once, `release --dry-run` starts 14 git processes instead of about 3,000: 8.1 s to 1.3 s in a release build, and 7.9 s to 1.6 s on a 20,000-commit history.\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` no longer slows down quadratically as more packages release at once: 12 s to 1.5 s in a debug build at 1,800 packages.\n- The output is unchanged.\n\nPull request #507\n\n</details>\n\n<details>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"967e4f7d-65a0-4fc2-b894-166a321a6403","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:07:43.459Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Each configuration mistake now has its own error code, so a script or a person can tell them apart.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- E254 is retired. A bad `publish-to` is E330, `release-trigger` E331, `cascade.mode` E332, `changelog.layout` E333, a registry `kind` E334, `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry E335, `url` on a Cargo registry E336, a registry timeout E337, and an unparsable package `match` E338. Before, all of thes\n- A registry `kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem is E339. Before, it reported E171, which means an internal defect, so it looked like a bug in Callisto.\n- Exit codes are unchanged.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n\nPull request #506\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Error codes now each name one condition, so a script can tell problems apart from the code.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto.toml`: E111 is only a TOML syntax error. An unknown key is E325, and a value of the wrong type or a missing required key is E326.\n- `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327, and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328. Before, both showed E171, which means an internal defect.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n\nPull request #500\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Breaking: eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What changed**\n- `--format json` output never contains `napi-coordination-not-yet-supported`, `pre-major-inference-inert`, `changelog-section-not-found`, `changeset-read-error`, `git-discovery-failed`, `changelog-read-error`, `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` or `publish-target-not-implemented`\n- The `DiagnosticCode` enum in the schema no longer lists them\n\n**Action**\n- Remove any match on these codes from scripts; a schema validator pinned to the old enum should be updated\n\nPull request #489\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. Many project templates give that root a version such as `0.0.0`, and until now Callisto listed it as a package even though it only holds scripts and tooling, is never \n- `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.\n- To version the root anyway, add a `[[package]]` block to `callisto.toml` with `match = \"npm/<name>\"`, where `<name>` is the root's `package.json` name, such as `match = \"npm/monorepo\"`.\n\nPull request #490\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Usage errors now exit 2, as the stability promise says, so a script can tell a mistake in the command from a failure in…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\nUsage errors now exit 2, as the stability promise says, so a script can tell a mistake in the command from a failure in the workspace.\n\n- A bad or missing flag value that Callisto checks after parsing now exits 2, like a clap-level mistake always did. Examples: `add --package a:patch`, `add --package cargo/a:bogus`, `add` without `--summary`, `init` without `--yes` and without a terminal, `snapshot --tag` with a space, and `--dry-ru\n- Also exit 2: an unknown package passed to `--package` on `add`, `matrix` or `release` (E102), an invalid `init --forge-repository` (E187) or `--product-package` (E189), a `release pending --from` that is not a release commit (E328), a repeated `--package` in a release selection (E169), an invalid \n- The rule: exit 2 when a flag value or combination is rejected, exit 1 when a valid flag meets state that cannot support it. Failures about your workspace, config, git, registries or release intent (for example E188, E299, E219, E308) still exit 1, and so does the same value read from `callisto.tom\n- The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n\nAction: a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n\nPull request #502\n\n</details>\n\n#### 🟢 Patch\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto add</code> no longer writes a changeset that Callisto's own tools reject, and <code>status</code> JSON has the same fields for…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n`callisto add` no longer writes a changeset that Callisto's own tools reject, and `status` JSON has the same fields for every package.\n\n- `add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` now fails with E329 and writes nothing. Before, it wrote both lines, and `status --check` then failed on the file.\n- `status --format json`: `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` print `null` when there is none instead of being left out, so every package record has the same keys.\n- The `--strict` help for `snapshot` and `version` now says what the flag does: it turns warnings into errors, and graph errors abort either way.\n\nPull request #503\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>version --emit-preview</code> is faster in large monorepos.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- The check for packages that changed since their last release now asks git once for all packages tagged at the same release, instead of once per package.\n- In a test workspace with 150 changed packages, that went from 151 git calls to 4, and from 3.8 s to 1.0 s.\n\nPull request #494\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A mistyped package name now gets a suggestion, so you can fix it from the error alone.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto add --package cargo/libb:minor` adds ``did you mean `cargo/lib`?`` to the E102 error, with up to three close matches.\n- A wrong ecosystem is caught too: `npm/lib` suggests `cargo/lib`.\n- When nothing is close, the error is unchanged.\n\nPull request #491\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Notes about packages Callisto skips are printed once per run.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- Before, a command that loads the workspace more than once, such as `callisto init`, printed the same note up to three times.\n- This covers the notes for a crate with no version and for an ignored private workspace root.\n\nPull request #496\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto release</code> and the release PR are much faster in very large monorepos.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- With about 1,500 of 1,800 packages releasing at once, `release --dry-run` starts 14 git processes instead of about 3,000: 8.1 s to 1.3 s in a release build, and 7.9 s to 1.6 s on a 20,000-commit history.\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` no longer slows down quadratically as more packages release at once: 12 s to 1.5 s in a debug build at 1,800 packages.\n- The output is unchanged.\n\nPull request #507\n\n</details>\n\n<details>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d75ab957-0f25-4870-91db-76af9778f469","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a4acf55fce15d0b8f","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a4acf55fce15d0b8f","branch":"refactor/lockfile-refresh-result","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a4acf55fce15d0b8f","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e11a9f6-dc3d-49d1-bc00-bd0c53f57cdd","permissionDecision":