{"parentUuid":"5d449591-eeaf-40b1-990a-95b10d6f4025","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx98BtHK8Q65hThDADB8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S2zdEnwSa36Yreo2a7QwPs","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Golden snapshots of every report schema","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\") and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c test/schema-goldens origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: prefer the smallest mechanism that makes a wrong change impossible to miss; use `insta` (already a dev-dependency; look at how existing snapshot tests are written and where snapshots live); add no scripts, no source-text scanning, no new dependencies; delete before adding. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; re-run workflow-contracts once if it fails). Push `git push -u origin test/schema-goldens`. No PR, no changeset (test-only).\nPROBLEM: docs/stability.md promises that within a `schemaVersion` no JSON report field is removed, renamed or retyped. `crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs` pins only the top-level fields of the status report and some enum variant sets; the generated schemas come from the same types as the output, so a rename passes unnoticed. Reports and their schemaVersion today: add=1, pre=1, release pending=1, errors=1, status/version/snapshot/matrix=2 (check origin/main for the exact list; `callisto schema --help` lists the `--type` values).\nTASK: add ONE test (in schema_guard_test.rs or a sibling) that, for EVERY `callisto schema --type <t>` value (enumerate them from the CLI's own definition, not a hand-copied list, e.g. through the clap enum / the function the schema command uses), runs the real schema generation and asserts an `insta` snapshot of the pretty JSON, so any shape change shows as a reviewable snapshot diff. Prefer calling the library function behind the `schema` command over spawning the binary N times. Include the schemaVersion in what is snapshotted if the schema carries it. Review the snapshots for noise (non-deterministic ordering, absolute paths, version strings that change every release: if present, normalize or exclude them rather than snapshotting churn). Then confirm the guard bites: temporarily rename one field in one report struct, run the test, see it fail, revert. Remove any now-redundant pins in schema_guard_test.rs only if the snapshot strictly covers them.\nREPORT (under 150 words): how many schemas are snapshotted, how the list is enumerated, size of the snapshots, the mutation result, commit signed?, five exit codes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":649704,"output_tokens":3322,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":809},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3322,"cache_read_input_tokens":649704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wir