{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"e4773119-9b0f-4d57-81f2-142460e20852","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:09:29.460Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"061c200486ebc9b0312f567dd75bc581bc0a5e74fd96255fbb8887ebe6350a68","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"b76875e0-1f68-40d5-a6d8-6fc57fb634ec","keep":817,"tail":["2d737db744ebb71c7e55f6d89eac009f4cb5fb99261bf496e72bb38aade99581","95783e6f77272f523a1c09bb13c5de4fece7ba596ec2933c21d0e904e1e0800e","4fa4ebc097db4b6d63e992dfb20edc9eaadafb9213cabeacbc628099e086c527"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",819,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"29b9528a9936372c4b2ac1c62bf4eb063286d3dfddbbf73535feae09b27c9449"}
{"parentUuid":"102e84e9-e53a-47a6-aa1b-2591af4ce0b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx99wh4RpfgAKHGkqZMZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 1.0 blockers report is in, and two small agents are running on its pre-release items.\n\n**Ranked 1.0 blockers (verified by the agent against `main`)**\n1. **No golden for JSON report shapes.** `schema_guard_test.rs` pins only the status report's top-level fields, and the other schemas are generated from the same types as the output, so a rename passes. Running now: an `insta` snapshot of every `callisto schema --type`.\n2. **Exit 1 vs 2 is still a hand-kept list.** `exit_kind` ends in `_ => Runtime`, so a new flag-value error silently exits 1. Two live cases:\n   - `release pending --decision ../x` exits 1 with a raw git error.\n   - `version --emit-decision` accepts paths outside the workspace and writes there. I confirmed this in the code: `ws.root.join(path)` has no check, while `release plan` validates its decision path. Running now: contain both with the existing errors and exit 2, no new codes. The agent will check whether `--emit-preview` legitimately writes outside, since the release action may use a temp dir.\n3. **The `callisto-action` contract is unpinned.** There are 12 inputs and 3 outputs, snake_case in and camelCase out, which freeze on `@v1`. Several look internal (`version_command`, `decision_path`, `setup_callisto`, `release_branch`). That's your call: trim or hide them, or state which are promised.\n4. **`release pending` is unclassified.** It's in `release --help` and used by the workflow but isn't in `stability.md`'s command list. Promise it, or hide it and list it as plumbing.\n5. **ADR 12 is still \"Proposed\"** although it's implemented (E316/E317 enforced). The smallest action is to flip it to Accepted.\n6. **The first `v1` tag has never run for real:** the floating-tag script returns early below 1.0.0. Rehearse it or be ready to fix `v1` by hand.\n\n**Clean:** about 45 spec criteria tested against the binary showed no behavioral drift (two wording gaps). The \"Ready for review\" override is a gap by design and can follow 1.0. Performance: 1,800 packages takes 820 ms (`status`) and 581 ms (`release --dry-run`), with at most 11 git processes per command.\n\n**Stale and done:** the private workspace root, #290, michi (now 0.9), and the 14% spec drift (not reproduced). `gh issue list` shows none open.\n\nneeds input: your decisions on items 3, 4 and 5 (action inputs, `release pending`, ADR 12). They're small, and I can draft the doc changes once you've chosen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7263,"cache_read_input_tokens":650411,"output_tokens":886,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7263,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":886,"cache_read_input_tokens":650411,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7263},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d95d9e00-7eb2-4556-8f8c-0b546ebad269","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx99wKygrbXbDmRPWdXw","requestRef":"e4773119-9b0f-4d57-81f2-142460e20852","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"99d98adf-a3e5-4009-98b0-e5071bdd1c61","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:09:35.323Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/fix-cha