works as before.\n  \n  Action: a script that passes an absolute or `../` decision path to `version --emit-decision` or `release pending --decision` must use a path inside the workspace.\n  ````\n  \n  changeset@3 JSON:\n  \n  ```json\n  [\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Breaking: `version --emit-decision` and `release pending --decision` now reject a decision path outside the workspace, as `release plan` always did.\\n\\n- `version --emit-decision ../x` or an absolute path outside the workspace used to write the decision file there and exit 0. It now exits 2 with E225 (outside the workspace) or E226 (invalid path) and writes nothing.\\n- `release pending --decision ../x` used to fail with exit 1 and a raw git \\\"outside repository\\\" error. It now exits 2 with E225 or E226.\\n- `version --emit-preview` is unchanged, so a preview can still go to a temp file outside the workspace.\\n- A workspace-relative path, such as the release PR action's `--emit-decision \\\"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\\\"`, works as before.\\n\\nAction: a script that passes an absolute or `../` decision path to `version --emit-decision` or `release pending --decision` must use a path inside the workspace.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"new\",\n      \"consumer_impact\": \"behavior-change\",\n      \"semver_impact\": \"major\",\n      \"files_changed\": [\n        \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs\",\n        \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"tests_added\": [\"crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria_met\": [\"unlinked\"],\n      \"breaking_changes\": [\n        \"`version --emit-decision <path>` with an absolute or `../` path outside the workspace: wrote the file there and exited 0 -> exits 2 with E225 or E226 and writes nothing -> pass a path inside the workspace.\",\n        \"`release pending --decision <path>` with a path outside the workspace: exited 1 with a raw git 'outside repository' error -> exits 2 with E225 or E226 -> pass a path inside the workspace.\"\n      ],\n      \"commits\": [\"deaf2b924\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Semver row: 'Changed CLI output, exit code, or default that scripts already depend on' -> major in the shared reference. The repo's sibling unreleased CLI entries (usage-errors-exit-2, catch-bad-input-early) use callisto-cli: minor for similar breaking changes, so the front matter says minor per the caller's instruction. The JSON semver_impact is major per the shared reference; the caller should confirm which convention release tooling reads. New entry, not folded into usage-errors-exit-2: that one is about flag-value exit codes, this one is path containment of the decision file. No spec linked, so no criteria_evidence. Files and commit come from the single commit deaf2b924; all attributed to this one outcome. usage_exit_codes_tests.rs is test-only, listed under tests_added.\"\n    }\n  ]\n  ```\n  \n  If release tooling reads the front matter, not the JSON, then the bump is minor in practice. The JSON says major only because the shared reference says exit-code changes are major. Decide which one governs.\n</agent-message>"}
