"`version --emit-decision <path>` with an absolute or `../` path outside the workspace: wrote the file there and exited 0 -> exits 2 with E225 or E226 and writes nothing -> pass a path inside the workspace.\",\n      \"`release pending --decision <path>` with a path outside the workspace: exited 1 with a raw git 'outside repository' error -> exits 2 with E225 or E226 -> pass a path inside the workspace.\"\n    ],\n    \"commits\": [\"deaf2b924\"],\n    \"reasoning\": \"Semver row: 'Changed CLI output, exit code, or default that scripts already depend on' -> major in the shared reference. The repo's sibling unreleased CLI entries (usage-errors-exit-2, catch-bad-input-early) use callisto-cli: minor for similar breaking changes, so the front matter says minor per the caller's instruction. The JSON semver_impact is major per the shared reference; the caller should confirm which convention release tooling reads. New entry, not folded into usage-errors-exit-2: that one is about flag-value exit codes, this one is path containment of the decision file. No spec linked, so no criteria_evidence. Files and commit come from the single commit deaf2b924; all attributed to this one outcome. usage_exit_codes_tests.rs is test-only, listed under tests_added.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nIf release tooling reads the front matter, not the JSON, then the bump is minor in practice. The JSON says major only because the shared reference says exit-code changes are major. Decide which one governs."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":228,"turnIndex":325},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/fix-changeset-list","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-list-fix","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
