{"parentUuid":"5e339ee2-771b-4942-aeda-a240766b539d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx9ixaJVoTFKe5GLRjNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018W66BRWAg8DrBWavrGr3vC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_goldens.md","content":"## Summary\n- `docs/stability.md` promises that within a `schemaVersion` no JSON report field is removed, renamed or retyped, but `schema_guard_test.rs` pinned only the top-level fields of the status report and some enum variant sets. The schemas are generated from the same types as the output, so a rename passed unnoticed.\n- One test, `every_schema_type_matches_its_snapshot`, now loops over every `callisto schema --type` value and asserts an `insta` snapshot of the pretty JSON schema. A new `--type` value gets a snapshot automatically, because the list comes from clap's `SchemaReportType::value_variants()`. Any shape change is a reviewable snapshot diff.\n- To call the schema without spawning the binary, `schema_of(SchemaReportType)` is extracted from `commands/schema.rs`, and `handle` calls it. Eight schemas are covered (about 95 KB of snapshots in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/snapshots/`), with no paths or version strings in them.\n- Not covered: `add`, `pre`, `release pending` and the error envelope are not `schema --type` values, so they have no schema snapshot. The existing pins in `schema_guard_test.rs` are untouched.\n- If #526 merges first, regenerate the `version` snapshot (it removes `success` and `exitCode`); if this merges first, #526 updates it.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Test only.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: tests only, plus one small internal extraction.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0 locally\n- [x] Mutation check: renaming `StatusReport.has_changesets` through serde made the test fail; reverted\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_read_input_tokens":685104,"output_tokens":732,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1385,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":685104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1385},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018W66BRWAg8DrBWavrGr3vC":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_goldens.md","content":"## Summary\n- `docs/stability.md` promises that within a `schemaVersion` no JSON report field is removed, renamed or retyped, but `schema_guard_test.rs` pinned only the top-level fields of the status report and some enum variant sets. The schemas are generated from the same types as the output, so a rename passed unnoticed.\n- One test, `every_schema_type_matches_its_snapshot`, now loops over every `callisto schema --type` value and asserts an `insta` snapshot of the pretty JSON schema. A new `--type` value gets a snapshot automatically, because the list comes from clap's `SchemaReportType::value_variants()`. Any shape change is a reviewable snapshot diff.\n- To call the schema without spawning the binary, `schema_of(SchemaReportType)` is extracted from `commands/schema.rs`, and `handle` calls it. Eight schemas are covered (about 95 KB of snapshots in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/snapshots/`), with no paths or version strings in them.\n- Not covered: `add`, `pre`, `release pending` and the error envelope are