{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:21:44.740Z","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","content":"And verify the findings for change #136:\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"6d4c\">\n### Medium finding\n\n**Location:** `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs:492`\n\nWhen `.callisto` does not exist yet, `version --emit-decision /workspace/.callisto/release-decision.json` now fails because canonicalizing its parent returns `NotFound`, even though the destination is inside the workspace. This previously worked: the writer creates missing parents (`crates/callisto-model/src/atomic.rs:49`), but the new validation runs first (`crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs:52`). Resolve the nearest existing ancestor and retain the missing components so valid absolute output paths remain supported.\n</pasted_content id=\"6d4c\">"}
