{"parentUuid":"927b1115-52cf-4ab3-87f7-ca56fb525127","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"758e031f-79d9-49e1-a841-bd78b594398c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MA8NZMh772oLkeugW4VHjJ","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 9 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: trails-feature-first\n3\tdescription: \"Entire trails are feature/outcome-shaped, created and linked BEFORE the PR is opened; descriptions state the work; never one per PR, never \\\"audit\\\" framing\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-02T15:08:36.610Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tTrails group work by semantic outcome (for example \"Releases publish exactly what was planned\"), not one per PR and not by how the work started (an audit). The description is the work: problem, outcome, done-when, open decisions; the PR numbers come last as a pointer.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** the owner has guided this more than once. Entire auto-creates a trail per PR titled with the PR title and no intent, so opening PRs first leaves a pile of empty mirror trails. Once the auto-trail owns a branch, the CLI cannot move it: `entire trail unlink` gives 409 \"reparent instead of detaching\" and `entire trail link` gives 409 \"already belongs to another Trail\"; there is no reparent command, so only the web UI could fix it.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:**\n16\t- Before pushing branches for a body of work, create the trail intent-only: `entire trail create --repo gh/orin-dx/callisto --no-branch --title ... --body ...` (group by feature, a handful of PRs each).\n17\t- Push each branch, then `entire trail link <n> --repo gh/orin-dx/callisto --branch <b>` BEFORE `gh pr create`, so no auto-trail is created for it. Tested on #419 (trail #151), and I misread it: linking the branch made ENTIRE open its own PR (\"opened by Entire to back a trail\", titled with the branch name, hidden `entire-shadow-pr` marker, authored as the user's own account, not as orin-dx-pr-bot). My `gh pr create` printed that existing PR's URL and I took it for success because I kept only the last line of output (`| tail -1`). Never trim `gh pr create` output; read it all. The gh shim (`~/.local/bin/gh`) opens PRs in orin-dx repos as orin-dx-pr-bot so a human can approve; an Entire-created PR is user-authored, but the owner confirmed that is fine because they merge through the Entire UI (the trail approval is the gate), so link-first is an accepted flow. After linking, do NOT run `gh pr create` (Entire already opened the PR): edit its title and body instead, keeping the `entire-shadow-pr` marker. Use `--base main` on link.\n18\t- Do not close or create trails without saying so; I closed one unprompted before and was corrected. The Entire Gates check is the trail's approvals gate (reviewers must approve), not a CI failure.\n19\t\n20\tRelated: [[feedback_local_tracking_not_prs]], [[feedback_entire_auto_push_intended]].\n21\t"}]},"uuid":"6e5b754a-6801-4905-93ad-8383792b9329","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:29:44.466Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_trails_feature_first.md","content":"---\nname: trails-feature-first\ndescription: \"Entire trails are feature/outcome-shaped, created and linked BEFORE the PR is opened; descriptions state the work; never one per PR, never \\\"audit\\\" framing\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\n  modified: 2026-11-02T15:08:36.610Z\n---\n\nTrails group work by semantic outcome (for example \"Releases publish exactly what was planned\"), not one per PR and not by how the work started (an audit). The description is the work: problem, outcome, done-when, open decisions; the PR numbers come last as a pointer.\n\n**Why:** the owner has guided this more than once. Entire auto-creates a trail per PR titled with the PR title and no intent, so opening PRs first leaves a pile of empty mirror trails. Once the auto-trail owns a branch, the CLI cannot move it: `entire trail unlink` gives 409 \"reparent instead of detaching\" and `entire trail link` gives 409 \"already belongs to another Trail\"; there is no reparent command, so only the web UI could fix it.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Before pushing branches for a body of work, create the trail intent-only: `entire trail create --repo gh/orin-dx/callisto --no-branch --title ... --body ...` (group by feature, a handful of PRs each).\n- Push each branch, then `entire trail link <n> --repo gh/orin-dx/callisto --branch <b>` BEFORE `gh pr create`, so no auto-trail is created for it. Tested on #419 (trail #151), and I misread it: linking the branch made ENTIRE open its own PR (\"opened by Entire to back a trail\", titled with the branch name, hidden `entire-shadow-pr` marker, authored as the user's own account, not as orin-dx-pr-bot). My `gh pr create` printed that existing PR's URL and I took it for success because I kept only the last line of output (`| tail -1`). Never trim `gh pr create` output; read it all. The gh shim (`~/.local/bin/gh`) opens PRs in orin-dx repos as orin-dx-pr-bot so a human can approve; an Entire-created PR is user-authored, but the owner confirmed that is fine because they merge through the Entire UI (the trail approval is the gate), so link-first is an accepted flow. After linking, do NOT run `gh pr create` (Entire already opened the PR): edit its title and body instead, keeping the `entire-shadow-pr` marker. Use `--base main` on link.\n- Do not close or create trails without saying so; I closed one unprompted before and was corrected. The Entire Gates check is the trail's approvals gate (reviewers must approve), not a CI failure.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_local_tracking_not_prs]], [[feedback_entire_auto_push_intended]].\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"927b1115-52cf-4ab3-87f7-ca56fb525127","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
