{"parentUuid":"9e6fc3ba-b1cc-424f-9bf6-0b632b5c4fa0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxCebzHXebyPepgoQDtR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, the release is ready from our side, pending three steps that are yours.\n\n**Done and verified**\n- **Subdirectory workspace:** `status` and `version --dry-run` give the same results with the workspace at `repo/ws` as at the repo root, including `changedSinceLastTag: true`. The release path itself wasn't run (it needs registry access).\n- **#493 (0.20.0):** regenerated after the last merges. It's out of draft with 17 changes, and the lockfile and decision-path Breaking entries are in the \"Read before merging\" list.\n- **All 27 PRs from this session** are merged or closed. The only PR left open besides the release PR is the older #495. The worktrees for merged PRs are cleaned up (the one for #528 can go now that it's merged).\n\n**Before you merge #493**\n1. **CI on the release branch hasn't run for the current head.** The release PR's CI runs on `callisto/version-packages` all finished as `action_required`, meaning they need approval before they run, and the newest run (01:34) predates the latest regeneration (01:54). Approve the pending run (Actions tab), or re-trigger it, and wait for it to pass. I can't approve workflow runs, and only the Entire Gates check is reporting now.\n2. **Entire Gates on trail 288** shows failing. Per your notes it's the approvals gate and not CI, so it clears when you approve the trail.\n3. **Read the rendered body once more.** It's the user-facing artifact and has about eight Breaking or Action items for a minor bump.\n\n**Deliberately after the release (about 15 lines of docs):** mark the internal Action inputs as internal, list `release pending` as CI plumbing, and flip ADR 12 to Accepted. I'll link that PR to trail #357 first.\n\n**Not release blockers:** the Caliper fix (needs a session in that repo), the 1.0-o