{"parentUuid":"83b2e69a-396a-4670-a7de-825ac3556e55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxD6k1DmA34cR4BQw4CA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_read_input_tokens":744563,"output_tokens":1738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":997},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":744563,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8052,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e586f400-abc3-4abf-8a2d-1748705a11e8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxD6jYwZ1gWer6rJmA4n","requestRef":"d1da7c79-ee79-4983-bee8-0536cd348845","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5956d2af-08e7-4e3a-80ef-aa8f49a875c5","timestamp":"2026-11-12T02:01:22.123Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"5956d2af-08e7-4e3a-80ef-aa8f49a875c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxD6k1DmA34cR4BQw4CA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing I'd hold the release for. What's left is real but either small or about 1.0, and adding to 0.20.0 now only makes an already large release bigger.\n\n**Why ship 0.20.0 as is**\n- It already carries 17 changes and about eight Breaking or Action notes, which is a lot for users to absorb at once.\n- Anything merged to `main` before #493 merges gets added to it, because the release PR regenerates on every push. So new work would have to stay unmerged until after the release anyway.\n- Known user-visible bugs are already in it: the subdirectory-workspace fix, the Python parser fix, and the decision-path containment.\n\n**What I'd put in the next batch (0.21 or the 1.0 candidate)**\n1. **`--dry-run` on read-only commands.** It's a global flag shown on `status`, `matrix` and `release pending`, where it does nothing, and it freezes at 1.0 by accident. It needs a decision (hide it or reject it there), so it's small but breaking.\n2. **A misleading message.** `version` prints \"No pending changesets\" next to a version plan computed from commits. It's a wording bug in a user-visible message, found by the spec check.\n3. **Shared tag or title for a fixed group (E194).** The title part is cheap, and it's one of your open design items.\n4. **OIDC trusted publishing for npm.** This is the one real feature. You raised its priority, and it needs a design pass and a workflow policy change, so it deserves its own plan and not a rush.\n5. **Rehearse the first `v1` tag.** The floating-tag script has never run for real, so before 1.0 someone should run it against a scratch remote.\n6. **The three docs items** (internal Action inputs, `release pending` as plumbing, ADR 12), as decided.\n\n**Also still open and not release-related:** the Caliper `Props<string>` fix, which needs a session in that repo.\n\nI'd release 0.20.0 first. Then I'll link the next batch to trail #357 (or a new trail) before opening any PRs, and start with items 1, 2 and 6, which are small.\n\nneeds input: say \"go\" and I'll prepare items 1, 2 and 6 on branches now but hold their PRs until #493 has merged, so they don't change the release."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_read_input_tokens":744563,"output_tokens":1738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":997},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":744563,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e586f400-abc3-4abf-8a2d-1748705a11e8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgxD6jYwZ1gWer6rJmA4n","requestRef":"d1da7c79-ee79-4983-bee8-0536cd348845","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"52a0c8d7-3d96-4a11-bc5a-727e39b121b8","timestamp":"2026-11-12T02:01:27.701Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
