{"parentUuid":"cc2e7a9e-f85e-4e08-8dac-86eb3050ece5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxT1oX3wnsYogDyuUxW7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F41vxMQPctQLmNrKRadw8u","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Investigate dry-run flag on read-only commands","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), main checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (use `git show origin/main:<path>` after `git fetch origin`; build the binary from a scratch copy only if you need to run it: `git worktree add` is not allowed, so use `cargo run` from an existing worktree only if one exists, else reason from code). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md.\nQUESTION: `--dry-run` is a GLOBAL flag (crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs, GlobalArgs) accepted before or after any subcommand. A 1.0-readiness audit found it shows up in the help of read-only commands (`status`, `matrix`, `release pending`, `help`, `schema`, `completions`) where it is a no-op, and flags freeze at 1.0 by accident. Find: (1) every command and what `--dry-run` actually does there (writes suppressed? output changed? nothing?), from the code (`ApplyPermit::granted_unless_dry_run(global.dry_run)` call sites and any other reads of `.dry_run`); (2) every place the repo itself passes `--dry-run` (grep .github/, docs/, README, tests, benches, the justfile) and to which command, so we know what would break if read-only commands rejected it; (3) what docs/stability.md and docs/specs/*.json promise about `--dry-run`; (4) the cheapest options with consequences for scripts: (a) leave it and document it as 'accepted everywhere, a no-op on read-only commands'; (b) keep it global but hide it from the help of commands where it does nothing (clap `hide` per command is awkward: say whether feasible without per-command arg structs); (c) move it from global to the commands that write, which makes `status --dry-run` a usage error (exit 2): list the breakage. State which you recommend for a CLI with one user pre-1.0 and why, preferring the smallest change that keeps the 1.0 surface honest.\nREPORT (under 350 words): a table of commands vs dry-run behavior, repo call sites passing it, the three options with breakage, and your recommendation. Mark anything unverified."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":746417,"output_tokens":3546,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":227},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3546,"cache_read_input_tokens":746417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01F41vxMQPctQLmNrKRadw8u":{"description":"Investigate dry-run flag on read-only commands","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), main checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (use `git show origin/main:<path>` after `git fetch origin`; build the binary from a scratch copy only if you need to run it: `git worktree add` is not allowed, so use `cargo run` from an existing worktree only if one exists, else reason from code). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md.\nQUESTION: `--dry-run` is a GLOBAL flag (crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs, Glob