t, or reword to say bumps were inferred from commits, whichever the spec/other criteria support); when there truly is nothing to release it must still say so. Fix at the source of the diagnostic (find where the 'No pending changesets' text is produced, likely callisto-graph version/plan code) with the smallest change, keep the diagnostic code/identity unchanged, and add one test in the existing test style that asserts the inferred-bump case and one for the truly-nothing case if no test covers it. Update docs/specs/versioning.json only if the criterion text is wrong. Check `--strict` interplay: `--strict` turns warnings into errors, so a spurious warning could make --strict fail on a valid inferred plan; verify and mention.\nREPORT (under 200 words): the reproduction (before/after output), what changed, the --strict finding, commit signed?, five exit codes."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"41ecd58d-cee2-4c17-8c53-e1ea0bab533f","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgxT1oChG6y1ANW5MwN78","requestRef":"b9c32fc1-f166-47d1-965d-8a7c7c748d42","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed063faa-337b-40ef-9e14-3add788b477c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:03:59.117Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"ed063faa-337b-40ef-9e14-3add788b477c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxT1oX3wnsYogDyuUxW7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K1XFf3Mh8UZ7fmsVUQ2HrG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Docs for internal inputs, plumbing and ADR 12","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto. Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c docs/1-0-contract-clarifications origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links; never hard-wrap prose; terse. Verify by EXIT CODE: `just doc-check`, `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just workflow-contracts` (run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; all exit 0; re-run workflow-contracts once if it fails). Push `git push -u origin docs/1-0-contract-clarifications`. No PR, no changeset (docs only). Do NOT change behavior, flags, action inputs or code.\nTASK (three owner-approved doc clarifications, smallest edits):\n1. `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` has 12 inputs and 3 outputs that freeze on `@v1`. Four are internal plumbing: `version_command`, `decision_path`, `setup_callisto`, `release_branch` (verify each by reading the action and its scripts; if a different input is clearly internal too, include it and say so). Prefix those inputs' `description:` with 'Internal: may change without notice.' (keep the rest of each description). Add one or two sentences to docs/stability.md (in its Action section, or where the Action contract lives; read first) saying only the inputs and outputs documented as supported are promised and the ones marked Internal are not. Do not rename or remove anything. Update docs for the action (docs/*.md, README) only if they list inputs and would now contradict.\n2. `callisto release pending` is shown in `release --help` and used by the release workflow, but docs/stability.md names it neither among the eight commands nor in the CI plumbing list. Add it to the plumbing list with a short note that its JSON output follows the report envelope but its flags are not part of the 1.0 CLI promise (check how the other plumbing commands, e.g. release plan or compose-pr-body, are described and mirror that exactly; verify the claim by reading cli.rs and the docs/specs/release.json criteria; do not promise more than the spec).\n3. docs/adr/ADR 12 (find it via docs/adr/README.md) is still 'Proposed' although implemented: E316 and E317 are enforced and tags follow it. Verify against the code that what the ADR decides is in place (read the ADR's decision section, then grep the code/tests), then set its status to Accepted and update the README index row. ADR 11's selector-promotion half was revised by ADR 12 without a supersede: add one sentence to ADR 11's status or notes saying which half ADR 12 revises, without rewriting ADR 11. If ADR 12 decides something that is NOT implemented, do not flip it: report what is missing.\nREPORT (under 150 words): the edits, anything you could not verify, commit signed?, four exit codes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":746417,"output_tokens":3546,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":227},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3546,"cache_read_input_tokens":746417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"