ed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; if workflow-contracts fails once, re-run it). Push `git push -u origin fix/no-pending-changesets-message`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (from a spec check against the binary): `callisto version` prints the warning \"No pending changesets\" even when it computes a version plan from commit inference (conventional commits), so the message contradicts the plan printed next to it. Spec: docs/specs/versioning.json VER-AGG-06 (read it and its neighbors). Reproduce with the real binary first: build once (`cargo build -q -p callisto-cli` in your worktree), make a temp git repo under $TMPDIR with a cargo workspace (callisto.toml, one package), an annotated tag `a@0.1.0`, then a commit `feat: x` touching the package and NO changeset file, and run `version --dry-run`, `status` and `version --dry-run --format json` and show the message and plan. Decide what the correct behavior is from the spec: when bumps are inferred from commits the warning should not claim there are no changesets (either do not emit it, or reword to say bumps were inferred from commits, whichever the spec/other criteria support); when there truly is nothing to release it must still say so. Fix at the source of the diagnostic (find where the 'No pending changesets' text is produced, likely callisto-graph version/plan code) with the smallest change, keep the diagnostic code/identity unchanged, and add one test in the existing test style that asserts the inferred-bump case and one for the truly-nothing case if no test covers it. Update docs/specs/versioning.json only if the criterion text is wrong. Check `--strict` interplay: `--strict` turns warnings into errors, so a spurious warning could make --strict fail on a valid inferred plan; verify and mention.\nREPORT (under 200 words): the reproduction (before/after output), what changed, the --strict finding, commit signed?, five exit codes.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/acb69fdff4fb3419d.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"41ecd58d-cee2-4c17-8c53-e1ea0bab533f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","branch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed063faa-337b-40ef-9e14-3add788b477c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
