{"parentUuid":"3245b99c-6dc6-41aa-97e8-85f4cb662bc0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35ae637f-ab49-40e2-97c6-91f5a102c985","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L2Ug7Wzxy8AgS5MfVEpWoX","type":"tool_result","content":"-    description: 'Version command; defaults to callisto version, which refreshes lockfiles. Callisto appends --emit-decision <decision_path>. The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a path with spaces.'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Version command; defaults to callisto version, which refreshes lockfiles. Callisto appends --emit-decision <decision_path>. The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a pat\n-    description: 'Path, relative to cwd, where the version command records the exact release decision this PR carries. Committed alongside the manifest and changelog edits; `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` verifies the merged commit against this \n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Path, relative to cwd, where the version command records the exact release decision this PR carries. Committed alongside the manifest and changelog edits; `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` ver\n-    description: 'Branch managed for the release PR'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Branch managed for the release PR'\n-    description: 'Install the Callisto environment before running'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Install the Callisto environment before running'\n+ADR 12 revises the selector-promotion half of this decision: qualified references are canonical slash form. The directory key and default tag stand.\n+\n-Status: Proposed\n+Status: Accepted\n-This proposal revises ADR 11's selector promotion when implemented. ADR 11 remains the current decision, including its default tag; it is not superseded by this documentation change.\n+This revises the selector-promotion half of ADR 11; ADR 11's directory-keyed identity and default tag stand.\n-## Proposed decision\n+## Decision\n-- [12. Canonical distribution references and explicit release ownership](0012-canonical-distribution-release-ownership.md) — proposed v1 model with some behavior already implemented. Separates native distribution identities, version authority and shared effec\n+- [12. Canonical distribution references and explicit release ownership](0012-canonical-distribution-release-ownership.md) — accepted v1 model. Separates native distribution identities, version authority and shared effects while preserving deliberate historic\n-| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n+| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. Only the inputs and outputs documented as supported are promised; those marked Internal are not. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version\n+`release pending` also appears in `release --help` and the release workflow uses it. Its JSON output follows the report envelope, but its flags are not part of the 1.0 CLI promise.\n+","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cb073a9d-7253-4401-aa47-103c46aa2ce8","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:14:27.933Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"-    description: 'Version command; defaults to callisto version, which refreshes lockfiles. Callisto appends --emit-decision <decision_path>. The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a path with spaces.'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Version command; defaults to callisto version, which refreshes lockfiles. Callisto appends --emit-decision <decision_path>. The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a pat\n-    description: 'Path, relative to cwd, where the version command records the exact release decision this PR carries. Committed alongside the manifest and changelog edits; `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` verifies the merged commit against this \n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Path, relative to cwd, where the version command records the exact release decision this PR carries. Committed alongside the manifest and changelog edits; `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` ver\n-    description: 'Branch managed for the release PR'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Branch managed for the release PR'\n-    description: 'Install the Callisto environment before running'\n+    description: 'Internal: may change without notice. Install the Callisto environment before running'\n+ADR 12 revises the selector-promotion half of this decision: qualified references are canonical slash form. The directory key and default tag stand.\n+\n-Status: Proposed\n+Status: Accepted\n-This proposal revises ADR 11's selector promotion when implemented. ADR 11 remains the current decision, including its default tag; it is not superseded by this documentation change.\n+This revises the selector-promotion half of ADR 11; ADR 11's directory-keyed identity and default tag stand.\n-## Proposed decision\n+## Decision\n-- [12. Canonical distribution references and explicit release ownership](0012-canonical-distribution-release-ownership.md) — proposed v1 model with some behavior already implemented. Separates native distribution identities, version authority and shared effec\n+- [12. Canonical distribution references and explicit release ownership](0012-canonical-distribution-release-ownership.md) — accepted v1 model. Separates native distribution identities, version authority and shared effects while preserving deliberate historic\n-| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n+| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of