{"parentUuid":"ad5f8d50-5459-4270-8771-adffd46d757f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35ae637f-ab49-40e2-97c6-91f5a102c985","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbuDg12hH3hAcRQvzZq8RL","type":"tool_result","content":"## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure,\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. `release inspect` prints the intent, manifest or\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli`. The bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. Only the inputs and outputs documented as supported are promised; those marked Internal are not. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work \n\n`release pending` also appears in `release --help` and the release workflow uses it. Its JSON output follows the report envelope, but its flags are not part of the 1.0 CLI promise.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3ab2770f-6e23-40b9-82d8-083a2ab03a05","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:14:34.126Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure,\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. `release inspect` prints the intent, manifest or\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli`. The bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. Only the inputs and outputs documented as supported are promised; those marked Internal are not. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work \n\n`release pending` also appears in `release --help` and the release workflow uses it. Its JSON output follows the report envelope, but its flags are not part of the 1.0 CLI promise.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"838c8a32-8a74-4a46-97ff-75fbbaa92b51","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","branch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad5f8d50-5459-4270-8771-adffd46d757f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/contain-emit-paths","slug":