cess,"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b6f18343-56aa-43de-8fb7-6e69aa761e10","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxTr6ijsQZoY2pj4GgKh","requestRef":"76399400-447f-4067-8e29-5fea88e1a98d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"30bfec6b-a4fa-4013-ad0f-5496193688ff","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:14:39.076Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/1-0-contract-clarifications","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"30bfec6b-a4fa-4013-ad0f-5496193688ff","snapshotMessageId":"68f4e562-fed0-4aef-87e6-1b0b00f1527a","trackingPath":"docs/stability.md","backup":{"backupFileName":"d6c607d22f237dde@v1","version":1,"backupTime":"2026-11-12T05:14:39.212Z","realParentDir":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276/docs"},"timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:14:39.212Z"}
{"parentUuid":"30bfec6b-a4fa-4013-ad0f-5496193688ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35ae637f-ab49-40e2-97c6-91f5a102c985","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011xprTc73hqgripyiWs2B4s","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276/docs/stability.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"8eade6aa-0b47-4fb8-b4aa-a74ff4cf288c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:14:39.271Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276/docs/stability.md","oldString":"| Exit codes | `0` success,","newString":"| `--dry-run` | Accepted by every command, before or after the command name. Commands that write write nothing under it; on read-only commands it does nothing; where it cannot apply (for example `release plan`) it is a usage error. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success,","originalFile":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure, not a usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. `release inspect` prints the intent, manifest or receipt unchanged: its own `schemaVersion`, no `command` or `dryRun`. `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli`. The bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. Only the inputs and outputs documented as supported are promised; those marked Internal are not. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n`release pending` also appears in `release --help` and the release workflow uses it. Its JSON output follows the report envelope, but its flags are not part of the 1.0 CLI promise.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":6,"newStart":7,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Surface | The promise |"," | --- | --- |"," | The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |","+| `--dry-run` | Accepted by every command, before or after the command name. Commands that write write nothing under it; on read-only commands it does nothing; where it cannot apply (for example `release plan`) it is a usage error. |"," | Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure, not a usage error. |"," | `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. `release inspect` prints the intent, manifest or receipt unchanged: its own `schemaVersion`, no `command` or `dryRun`. `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. |"," | `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30bfec6b-a4fa-4013-ad0f-5496193688ff","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/1-0-contract-clarifications","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
