{"parentUuid":"476f2b66-e3d2-48dd-a959-f4c747908bb8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35ae637f-ab49-40e2-97c6-91f5a102c985","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K6LmwswhFGrSBz4n1i48bB","type":"tool_result","content":"Link an existing remote branch to a project trail. --branch defaults to the current branch. --base sets the branch the change merges into, for linked and created branches alike; trail show lists each change's base, and trail retarget changes it later. Use --branch-action create to create remote branch work from --base. Existing work and reviews are preserved; a branch belonging to another trail is rejected.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail link <trail> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --base string              Base branch the change merges into; with --branch-action create, the new branch also starts from it\n      --branch string            Branch to use (defaults to the current feature branch; create derives one from the title on the base branch)\n      --branch-action string     Branch action: link existing remote work, or create a new branch (default \"link\")\n  -h, --help                     help for link\n      --idempotency-key string   Retry key for linking a branch; with intent-only creation, requires project management\n      --json                     Output raw JSON instead of a table\n      --status string            Lifecycle status (open, closed)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a9ecff2e-e871-4a4f-858e-f5aa12a2e17e","timestamp":"2026-11-12T0