{"parentUuid":"aa632593-d299-4a29-bf74-09b1eb2256d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxTvfCxGZb8WhuZnnetG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vkv9yyV7CtqE5p6aN2URWo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Changeset for the no-pending-changesets fix","subagent_type":"courier:changeset-analyzer","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Produce changeset text for orin-dx/callisto branch `fix/no-pending-changesets-message` (base main). Diff: `git diff origin/main...origin/fix/no-pending-changesets-message` (run from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276; do not cd elsewhere). First list the unreleased `.changeset/` files on origin/main (`git ls-tree --name-only origin/main .changeset/`; after the 0.20.0 release most are consumed, so there may be none) and fold in only if the SAME outcome exists; otherwise write a new file. Facts (reproduced with the real binary): with `release-trigger = \"auto\"` and a `feat:` commit after the last tag but no changeset file, `callisto version` printed the plan (cargo/a 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, inferred from the commit) and then the warning \"No pending changesets found in workspace\", contradicting the plan beside it; `callisto version --strict` turned that warning into an error and exited 1 on a valid inferred plan. Now the warning is skipped when the bump was inferred from commits, so `version` prints only the plan, `--strict` exits 0, and the JSON `diagnostics` array no longer carries the `empty-changeset` diagnostic in that case. When there is truly nothing to release (no changesets and no inferred bumps) the warning still appears. `status` is unchanged. Style: say what changed, why it matters, what to do (nothing, unless a script relied on the warning); lead line, short bullets only where they add something, plain language, no AI slop, one line per paragraph; patch-level bug fix: front matter `callisto-cli: patch`. Return ready-to-write file text with a kebab-case file name, plus changeset@3 JSON. Do not write files."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":776968,"output_tokens":945,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":945,"cache_read_input_tokens":776968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Vkv9yyV7CtqE5p6aN2URWo":{"description":"Changeset for the no-pending-changesets fix","subagent_type":"courier:changeset-analyzer","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Produce changeset text for orin-dx/callisto branch `fix/no-pending-changesets-message` (base main). Diff: `git diff origin/main...origin/fix/no-pending-changesets-message` (run from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3331bef90d4c2276; do not cd elsewhere). First list the unreleased `.changeset/` files on origin/main (`git ls-tree --name-only origin/main .changeset/`; after the 0.20.0 release most are consumed, so there may be none) and fold in only if the SAME outcome exists; otherwise write a new file. Facts (reproduced with the real binary): with `release-trigger = \"auto\"` and a `feat:` commit after the last tag but no changeset file, `callisto version` printed the plan (cargo/a 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, inferred from the commit) and then the warning \"No pending changesets found in workspace\", contradicting 