{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:25:01.549Z","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","content":"Change #139 has a finding:\n\n<pasted_content id=\"6d4c\">\n### Medium finding\n\n**Location:** `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:331`\n\nOn a prerelease rerun, an auto package can have a minor commit inference overridden by an already-recorded major changeset (`crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:325–337`); aggregation then removes its bump but leaves `inference_commits` populated (`aggregate.rs:387–391`). This guard consequently suppresses the empty-plan warning and lets `--strict` succeed with nothing to release. Check for a surviving inferred bump, or remove stale inference entries when their bumps are removed.\n</pasted_content id=\"6d4c\">"}
