{"parentUuid":"7f31e749-f52b-4752-9604-f0a8bd12ffa6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxUdj3HrihtewRcr6Nb4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've run out of safe work to launch on my own, and the reason is worth stating plainly.\n\n**Where things stand**\n- **#530 and #531:** CI is 15 passing with 2 still pending (one is the Entire approval gate). They're ready for you to merge.\n- **0.20.0:** published and verified, with nothing left to fix in it.\n\n**What's left is decision-heavy, not build-ready**\n- **OIDC trusted publishing:** `docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md` already holds the plan and marks it \"after v1\". Two things block building it:\n  1. It needs your decisions: the shape of the switch (a `callisto.toml` setting or a generated-workflow option), and whether Callisto's own release workflow may give `execute` the `id-token: write` permission, which the policy check forbids today.\n  2. Its verification needs real scratch packages on npm, crates.io and PyPI, run from a scratch repository with no token set, and you'd have to do that part. Given the release incidents in your history, I'd rather not build it without those answers.\n- **E194 (a fixed group sharing one tag or release title):** E194 still exists as the \"more than one package shares a `v{version}` tag\" error. Letting a group share one tag and release is a design change across tags, registries and release notes (ADRs 9 and 12), not a quick fix. It needs a design pass with you first.\n- **The first `v1` tag rehearsal:** `workflow-contracts` already tests the floating-tag script against a local remote (it creates `v1` at 1.0.0, moves it forward, never backwards). I'd only add value by a real run at 1.0.0, so I'm not building anything for it.\n- **Caliper `Props<string>`:** it needs a session started in the Caliper repo. The prompt is ready.\n\n**What I can do next, if you want**\n1. **Draft decision briefs** for OIDC and E194: options, consequences, my recommendation, one page each, so the decisions are quick.\n2. **Clean up** the worktrees for #530 and #531 once they merge, plus the Caliper prompt.\n\nneeds input: tell me which brief to write first (OIDC or E194), or merge #530 and #531 and I'll clean up after them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":796232,"output_tokens":1099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":362},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":963,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":796232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":963},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0e749c5f-1fac-4d3e-8794-deecdfcd4dcb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgxUdigiAB9AMvzerq72m","requestRef":"5f90f3f2-6b73-4f17-809e-5d1d308524c7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef06a3ce-9d74-4aa7-8920-ac81711f3ffc","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:25:04.812Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
