{"parentUuid":"5e988526-e257-4630-b63c-7c8e15db7d04","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54581314-3dd6-435d-af74-61b3aca3efb3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VKVWwPt8s5YVZZnTVi1mqX","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Safe Rust only.** `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` workspace-wide.\n2. **License boundary.** `callisto-model` is MIT and must never depend on an FSL-1.1-MIT crate. Every other crate is FSL-1.1-MIT. Check with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml`.\n3. **Format-preserving manifest edits.** `Cargo.toml` goes through `toml_edit`'s CST. String-only `package.json` changes replace scanned literal spans in the original text; other changes keep key order and fingerprinted indentation and line endings. No regex or line-based edits to manifests.\n4. **One file-write primitive, capability-gated.** `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write` (`NamedTempFile` in the target's own directory, `fsync`, `persist` via `fs::rename`, then `fsync` the parent directory, and its parent when the call created it; a failed sync is returned unless the filesystem cannot sync a directory) is the\n5. **System Git only.** All VCS reads and writes shell out to the user's `git` binary (`callisto_model::vcs`), so Callisto sees exactly the repository, config, and identity Git itself does. No embedded Git implementation.\n6. **Versioning.** The four published crates version in lockstep (one fixed group). Only `callisto-cli`, its command-line interface and its JSON reports are a compatibility surface; `callisto-model`, `callisto-manifests` and `callisto-graph` are internal and may change in any release.\n7. **User-facing errors are diagnosable.** Every error surfaced to a user derives `miette::Diagnostic` with a stable code and, where the fix isn't obvious from the message, `help` text. A wrapper around another crate's error (for example `GraphError::Config`) is `#[diagnostic(transparent)]` and declares no code of its own, so th\n\nDesign decisions, with the options they rejected and why: [`docs/adr/README.md`](docs/adr/README.md).\n\n## Crate map","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ff695525-bb42-40e9-8339-fb5d9069d979","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:36:34.766Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Safe Rust only.** `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` workspace-wide.\n2. **License boundary.** `callisto-model` is MIT and must never depend on an FSL-1.1-MIT crate. Every other crate is FSL-1.1-MIT. Check with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml`.\n3. **Format-preserving manifest edits.** `Cargo.toml` goes through `toml_edit`'s CST. String-only `package.json` changes replace scanned literal spans in the original text; other changes keep key order and fingerprinted indentation and line endings. No regex or line-based edits to manifests.\n4. **One file-write primitive, capability-gated.** `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write` (`NamedTempFile` in the target's own directory, `fsync`, `persist` via `fs::rename`, then `fsync` the parent directory, and its parent when the call created it; a failed sync is returned unless the filesystem cannot sync a directory) is the\n5. **System Git only.** All VCS reads and writes shell out to the user's `git` binary (`callisto_model::vcs`), so Callisto sees exactly the repository, config, and identity Git itself does. No embedded Git implementation.\n6. **Versioning.** The four published crates version in lockstep (one fixed group). Only `callisto-cli`, its command-line interface and its JSON reports are a compatibility surface; `callisto-model`, `callisto-manifests` and `callisto-graph` are internal and may change in any release.\n7. **User-facing errors are diagnosable.** Every error surfaced to a user derives `miette::Diagnostic` with a stable code and, where the fix isn't obvious from the message, `help` text. A wrapper around another crate's error (for example `GraphError::Config`) is `#[diagnostic(transparent)]` and declares no code of its own, so th\n\nDesign decisions, with the options they rejected and why: [`docs/adr/README.md`](docs/adr/README.md).\n\n## Crate map","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2c85a731-94ed-407d-a271-fcb10ef69daf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","branch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e988526-e257-4630-b63c-7c8e15db7d04","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
