{"parentUuid":"b9f54142-cd3f-4b1c-b41e-75e1fdb5f928","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxVevC9QSpn1ckwGbvuW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C8QoV3WiGwebv18in1dpAe","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit README and guides against current behavior","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c docs/catch-up-with-0-20 origin/main`. Build the binary once (`cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; the sandbox may need dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true) and use `target/debug/callisto` in temp fixture repos under $TMPDIR (a git repo with a cargo workspace, a callisto.toml, an annotated tag `a@0.1.0`, a later commit, and a changeset; never run in the worktree itself, and never commit fixtures).\nCONTEXT: since 0.19.0 (see crates/callisto-cli/CHANGELOG.md 0.20.0 section for the user-visible list) these changed: every JSON field is camelCase; usage errors and errors caused by a flag value exit 2 (docs/stability.md has the rule); new error codes E325-E339 and each condition has its own code; `pre enter` tag validation (SemVer prerelease); unknown keys in group blocks rejected; `pre-major-inference \"false\"` rejected; private npm workspace root no longer a package; `did you mean` suggestions for package names; `callisto add` rejects duplicate packages and writes only valid changesets; `status` JSON prints null fields; reports have schemaVersion 2 (version report lockfile result lost success/exitCode, status/version/snapshot/matrix are schemaVersion 3); decision paths must stay inside the workspace (E225/E226); `version` no longer warns 'No pending changesets' on an inferred bump; subdirectory workspaces now work; Action inputs version_command/decision_path/release_branch/setup_callisto are Internal; `release pending` is CI plumbing; `--dry-run` is accepted everywhere and a no-op on read-only commands; large-monorepo speedups.\nTASK: audit these docs against the CURRENT code and binary and FIX what is wrong, with the smallest edits: README.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/architecture/*.md, docs/releasing.md, docs/publishing.md and any other guide under docs/*.md EXCEPT docs/errors.md, docs/config.md, docs/stability.md and docs/specs/* (those were audited recently) and EXCEPT docs/adr/* (decisions are history; only fix a factual status line if plainly wrong) and docs/projects/* (plans). For each doc check: (1) every command, flag and example invocation actually exists and behaves as the text says (run the ones that can run on the fixture; for ones that need a registry or GitHub, check the code/help text only and say so); (2) every quoted output, JSON field name, key, tag format, error code and exit code is current (grep error codes against docs/errors.md; JSON example keys against `callisto schema --type <t>` and real output); (3) file paths, crate names, module names and function names mentioned still exist (grep the code); (4) numbers (command counts, supported ecosystems, platforms) match the code; (5) claims that a feature is planned/missing but now exists, or the reverse. ALSO add to ARCHITECTURE.md invariants (keep the existing style, one or two sentences each, after invariant 7): (a) exit classification: a failure caused by a flag value exits 2, everything else exits 1, decided per error type by `exit_kind()` with runtime as the default; (b) every `--format json` report goes through the typed `Report` envelope (`emit_report`); untyped JSON output is crate-private. And in docs/specs/versioning.json is OFF-LIMITS, do not touch specs.\nRULES: edit docs only (no code, no behavior); never hard-wrap prose; terse; do not rewrite sections that are merely old-fashioned, only wrong or missing; do not invent behavior, verify each fix by running or reading co