{"parentUuid":"71210096-996c-4b68-bcce-96e330253561","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxVhGgkY2xLYMGfPoNcj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VwSehcj1GAh5RMMGZTJLA1","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae55a48dbafe514c8","summary":"Add a verified features section to README","message":"Addition to your task, same branch docs/catch-up-with-0-20, as its own commit: the README undersells the product. It names Cargo, npm/pnpm and PyPI and says 'tags, GitHub releases and assets' in two lines, and says nothing about attestation/provenance, native-extension packages (napi-rs, maturin), checksums, the reviewable release PR, or safe retries. Add ONE compact section to README.md (place it after the 'A change through Callisto' example and before install; at most 14 lines, bullets, plain claims, no marketing adjectives, no emoji) titled like 'What you get', containing ONLY claims you have verified in code or by running the binary, each with the doc that explains it linked. Candidates to verify and include if true: (1) ecosystems and package managers actually supported: Cargo, npm (which of npm/pnpm/yarn/bun are supported for versioning AND for publishing: check docs/publishing.md and the code), PyPI (build backends: maturin, uv, hatch, setuptools, poetry? which are actually handled), and native-extension platform packages (napi-rs for npm, maturin wheels): say exactly what works. (2) Tags: one tag per package `{name}@{version}` (qualified `ecosystem/name@{version}` only on a name clash), configurable `tag-template`, a floating major tag (`v1`) for the Action from 1.0. (3) GitHub releases with attached assets and generated notes from changesets for the product package. (4) Supply-chain: what is attested and how (grep attest/provenance in .github/workflows, init.rs generated workflows, release_artifacts.rs: are artifact attestations created for release binaries, and can users verify them with `gh attestation verify`? is npm provenance supported via NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE? any checksums file or per-asset sha256?). (5) The release PR: one continuously updated PR holding versions, changelogs and the reviewable publish plan, and that merging it is the approval; a held/draft state when stale. (6) Safe reruns: a failed release can be rerun; already-published versions are adopted not re-published; receipts. (7) Every command has `--dry-run`, JSON output with stable schemaVersion. If a candidate is not true or you cannot verify it, leave it out and list it in your report under 'unverified'. Do not touch the existing sections except to fix wrong facts. Same verification: `just doc-check`, `just pre-push`, `just lint` exit 0; signed commit; push the same branch. In your report add a short 'README feature claims' table: claim, evidence (file or command), verified yes/no.","type":"message","recipient":"ae55a48dbafe514c8","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Addition to your task, same branch docs/catch-up-…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_read_input_tokens":836080,"output_tokens":1882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":905},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1882,"cache_read_input_tokens":836080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1611},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VwSehcj1GAh5RMMGZTJLA1":{"to":"ae55a48dbafe514c8","summary":"Add a verified features section to README","message":"Addition to your task, same branch docs/catch-up-with-0-20, as its own commit: the README undersells the product. It names Cargo, npm/pnpm and PyPI and says 'tags, GitHub releases and assets' in two lines, and says nothing about attestation/provenance, native-extension packages (napi-rs, maturin), checksums, the reviewable release PR, or safe retries. Add ONE compact section to README.md (place it after the 'A change through Callisto' example and before install; at most 14 lines, bullets, plain claims, no marketing adjectives, no emoji) titled like 'What you get', containing ONLY claims you have verified in code or by running the binary, each with the doc that explains it linked. Candidates to verify and include if true: (1) ecosystems and package managers actually supported: Cargo, npm (which of npm/pnpm/yarn/bun are supported for versioning AND for publishing: check docs/publishing.md and the code), PyPI (build backends: maturin, uv, hatch, setuptools, poetry? which are actually handled), and native-extension platform packages (napi-rs for npm, maturin wheels): say exactly what works. (2) Tags: one tag per package `{name}@{version}` (qualified `ecosystem/name@{version}` only on a name clash), configurable `tag-template`, a floating major tag (`v1`) for the Action from 1.0. (3) GitHub releases with attached assets and generated notes from changesets for the product package. (4) Supply-chain: what is attested and how (grep attest/provenance in .github/workflows, init.rs generated workflows, release_artifacts.rs: are artifact attestations created for release binaries, and can users verify them with `gh attestation verify`? is npm provenance supported via NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE? any checksums file or per-asset sha256?). (5) The release PR: one continuously updated PR holding versions, changelogs and the reviewable publish plan, and that merging it is the approval; a held/draft state when stale. (6) Safe reruns: a failed release can be rerun; already-published versions are adopted not re-published; receipts. (7) Every command has `--dry-run`, JSON output with stable schemaVersion. If a candidate is not true or you cannot verify it, leave it out and list it in your report under 'unverified'. Do not touch the existing sections except to fix wrong facts. Same verification: `just doc-check`, `just pre-push`, `just lint` exit 0; signed commit; push the same branch. In your report add a short 'README feature claims' table: claim, evidence (file or command), verified yes/no."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"685715da-b55d-490b-81dd-d1d37c10b1fc","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgxVhGJgg7yMAbHv1TJxY","requestRef":"da973120-e1e2-44a0-a59a-c0a6701f9545","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d7934fc-09b8-4dca-89a3-a27ee5d4f9a8","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:39:06.622Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/catch-up-with-0-20","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
