{"parentUuid":"b3c28afe-b47e-4aaf-a624-865a8514de7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxWQyaXYNuiTJp4hvyk8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H9yzJoHiXBwWRhw7gMxDYU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs_catchup.md","content":"## Summary\n- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).\n- ARCHITECTURE.md: two invariants. A failure caused by a flag value exits 2 and everything else exits 1, decided per error type by `exit_kind()` with runtime as the default. Every `--format json` report goes through the typed `Report` envelope (`emit_report`), and untyped JSON output is crate-private.\n- Ten stale or missing statements fixed in `docs/architecture/{versioning,wire-compat,identity,release}.md`, `docs/how-callisto-works.md` (yarn and bun are supported) and `docs/publishing.md` (yarn registry advice, E168 and `npmPublishRegistry`). Worst ones: `versioning.md` said `uncovered_changes` was not wired into the CLI or PR body (it feeds `ReleasePreview.unreleased`), and `wire-compat.md` called `schema --type snapshot` the status report.\n- `docs/releasing.md` and `docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md` were checked and needed nothing. Left out of the README on purpose: the floating `v1` tag and the \"Hold release PR\" draft state (this repo's own workflow, not generated for users) and a checksum file (none is generated).\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Documentation only\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: docs only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] README, ARCHITECTURE.md and the architecture and guide pages above. `docs/errors.md`, `config.md`, `stability.md` and `docs/specs/*` were audited and updated in earlier PRs.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just doc-check`, `just pre-push` and `just lint` exit 0. Quick start, `status`, `version --dry-run`, `release --dry-run`, the dirty-tree error (E267), `--package` (E102, exit 2), `pre enter` (E324), `release pending --from` (E327), the `--emit-decision` path rules, `--format json` and `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` were run on a fixture.\n- [x] I re-checked the supply-chain claims in code: the generated matrix workflow uses `actions/attest-build-provenance`, `release_artifacts.rs` compares SHA-256 and size and then runs `gh attestation verify` against a recorded repository and workflow policy, and generated workflows set `NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE`.\n- [ ] Not verified (left as written): the four-attempt retry in `releasing.md` (checked in the action script only); a yarn or bun publish (not run); Python build-backend breadth beyond `python -m build`; npm provenance end to end (code read only); `gh attestation verify` against a real release. Anything needing a registry or GitHub was checked in code and help text only.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":851949,"output_tokens":1364,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":79},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":851949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":