{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","prNumber":532,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/532","prRepository":"orin-dx/callisto","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:48:42.135Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1328c2d2-daf2-4c4f-a325-a8079d642502","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxWSqTRJiY8VXG6y732Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #532 is open and ready for review. It adds a verified \"What you get\" section to the README and fixes the stale docs you suspected.\n\n**README: \"What you get\"**\n- **Ecosystems:** Cargo, npm with npm, pnpm, yarn or bun, and Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry (`python -m build` with Twine).\n- **Native extensions:** napi-rs platform packages.\n- **Release pipeline:** tags, GitHub releases, one release PR, safe reruns, and `--dry-run` with stable JSON and exit 2.\n- **Supply chain:** I verified this one myself in code.\n  - The generated matrix workflow attests each Cargo binary with `actions/attest-build-provenance`.\n  - `release execute` compares each asset's SHA-256 and size and then runs `gh attestation verify` against a recorded repository and workflow policy.\n  - Generated workflows set `NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE` for npm.\n\n**Stale docs fixed:** ten statements in the architecture pages and guides. Examples:\n- `versioning.md` said a function wasn't wired into the CLI when it is.\n- `wire-compat.md` called the snapshot schema \"the status report\".\n- `how-callisto-works.md` said npm and pnpm only, but yarn and bun are supported.\n\nARCHITECTURE.md also gets the two invariants (exit classification and the typed report envelope).\n\n**What I couldn't verify**, left as written and listed in the PR:\n- the four-attempt retry in `releasing.md` (checked in the action script only);\n- a yarn or bun publish, which wasn't run;\n- Python build-backend breadth beyond `python -m build`;\n- npm provenance end to end;\n- `gh attestation verify` against a real release.\n\nI deliberately left three things out of the README: the floating `v1` tag and the \"Hold release PR\" state (this repo's own workflow, not generated for users), and a checksum file (none is generated).\n\n**Trail:** I created trail #374 \"Docs describe what Callisto does today\" and linked the branch to it before the PR existed, so it didn't spawn a mirror trail. That's a new trail I created without asking.\n\nCI hasn't run on the branch yet.\n\nneeds input: merge #530, #531 and #532 when CI passes. Say if you want the README section reworded, especially the attestation line."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":853956,"output_tokens":783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":853956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"aac33305-3278-4d3c-87bf-e8973d2469ff","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxWSq8Ksu6fCfeu4ZW3L","requestRef":"4e83d978-3fab-47da-b4b2-17694adb4164","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e1d1bcd-8556-43c3-ae96-9e73505ee714","timestamp":"2026-11-12T05:48:47.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/catch-up-with-0-20","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
