te actions `callisto-action`, `setup-callisto`, `callisto-validate` and what each does (read .github/actions/*/action.yml, mention only the documented-as-supported inputs, not the ones marked Internal); how a repo adopts it. (6) Scripting and stability: `--format json` on every command, `schemaVersion`, camelCase, exit codes 0/1/2, error codes documented in docs/errors.md, `callisto schema`, stability promises in docs/stability.md; performance only if you measure it yourself on a generated fixture (state the size and the time you got). (7) Platform and install: operating systems and architectures the release binaries cover (read the README install section and the release workflow matrix), and any unsupported platform. THEN add a short honest 'Limits' list (max 8 bullets) of what Callisto does not do or only partly does, each verified: e.g. cross-language dependencies are not inferred; maturin gets no generated workflow; Python versions must be static (PEP 621) or Poetry; Windows; only Cargo/npm/PyPI; OIDC trusted publishing is planned not built (docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md); nuget appears in publish-to enums (check whether it is actually implemented or only reserved, and say so). Do not claim comparisons with other tools. Update the hero line/lead paragraph only if a sentence there is now wrong. Verification as before: `just doc-check`, `just pre-push`, `just lint` exit 0, signed commit(s) (retry with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true if gpg fails in the sandbox), push the same branch. REPORT (under 300 words): the claim table (claim, evidence, verified yes/no) for the NEW claims only, the list of unverified items, and any README statement you found wrong."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c41bd6e3-fdf8-4348-8496-96b49ef295f2","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgxXQEKtCYALv3hCbS11c","requestRef":"a9611f62-097d-4527-86c3-56e2e6d18083","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa691e55-61d6-4aea-b9d2-447f44d448af","timestamp":"2026-11-