{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":11704,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"8acef268-e787-429c-a5a7-e2f71bbd8016","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxXRgncyc82EedFa8qzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right that it's anemic, and the docs agent is writing the fuller version now. I capped the first section at eight bullets, and the real surface is much larger.\n\n**What's missing from the README today** (from the CLI help and `docs/config.md`)\n- **Versioning control:** the dependency-aware cascade and its knobs (`out-of-range` or `always`, bump severity, peer escalation, npm range preservation), lock-step `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]`, per-package and glob overrides, and did-you-mean suggestions.\n- **Beyond plain changesets:** `release-trigger = \"auto\"` inferring bumps from conventional commits (with the pre-1.0 `pre-major-inference` policy), prerelease mode, throwaway `snapshot` versions, and grouped or flat changelogs with compare links.\n- **Releasing:** private and alternate registries with publish timeouts, product binaries declared with target triples, platform-package ordering, and confirming a published version is visible before tagging.\n- **CI:** `callisto init` scaffolding the workflows and the three composite actions (`callisto-action`, `setup-callisto`, `callisto-validate`).\n- **Scripting and stability:** `status --check` as a CI gate, JSON on every command, error codes, `callisto schema`, and the stability promises.\n\n**What I asked for:** seven grouped sections of roughly 40–70 lines, each claim verified in code, the help text or a fixture run and linked to its doc. Performance is only to appear if the agent measures it itself.\n\n**A \"Limits\" list:** up to eight verified bullets of what Callisto doesn't do, such as cross-language dependencies not being inferred, no generated workflow for maturin, static versions only for Python, and OIDC publishing planned but not built. I also asked it to check whether `nuget` in the `publish-to` options is implemented or only reserved. A README that states its limits is more credible to adopters, and it saves them finding out later.\n\nIt adds commits to #532 (no force-push), and I'll read the result myself before anything is merged, especially claims that can't be run here, like registry publishing. I'm not asking for competitor comparisons, because I can't verify those.\n\nneeds input: none yet. I'll bring back the new section and its claim table for your review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5621,"cache_read_input_tokens":858837,"output_tokens":755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5621,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":858837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5621},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ae308cc2-c002-4101-bff4-15def8ea933e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxXRgRJL7Pa4fHDnRAok","requestRef":"08c9020d-34c5-43eb-b818-d53c8c378fa6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0c3ca326-cde9-4c43-9be6-4e684c3d5d4d","timestamp":"2026-11-12T06:01:38.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/catch-up-with-0-20","slug":"mossy-snacki