ignores them | ran it; `status` warns | yes |\n  | `pre-major-inference` policies | `aggregate.rs::apply_pre_major` | code read only |\n  | Snapshot `0.0.0-<tag>-<sha>` (Cargo only) | ran it | yes |\n  | `--format json` on every command except `completions` | ran 11 commands; `completions` prints a raw script | yes |\n  | Exit 0/1/2, E325, E324, E327 | ran it | yes |\n  | `nuget` accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher | E119 on a cargo package; `config.md` | yes |\n  | OIDC trusted publishing planned, not built | `docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md` | yes |\n  | Platforms: 5 targets, no Windows | release workflow matrix, `proto/callisto.toml`, `stability.md` | yes |\n  \n  **Unverified or left out**\n  - Performance: not measured, not claimed.\n  - `confirm-timeout` waiting and safe reruns: only the docs, since they need a registry or GitHub.\n  - Whether `conservative-feat` downgrades a feat on a 0.1.0 package. In my run it stayed minor, because the code skips packages at `0.0.x`/`0.y` with y=0 or no prior release. I only stated the policy.\n  - No real `gh attestation verify` or npm provenance run.\n  \n  **Anything wrong in the README?** Nothing wrong in the old text. The four internal action inputs are not mentioned.\n  \n  **Oddity for you:** `callisto-validate/action.yml` and `callisto-ci.yml` line 261 contain `uses: $/.github/actions/...`, which is not a valid local action reference. I did not touch it.\n  \n  **Your brief vs. the code:** `version --dry-run` still printed \"No pending changesets found\" for an inferred bump in my fixture.\n</agent-message>"}
