{"parentUuid":"8a15057f-785a-430b-89ff-d86f0837bcca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxXotFobAWwQQjjWCUm4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQWwLcvQKtNbf2HZmmThB9","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs_catchup.md","old_string":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).","new_string":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section (about 60 lines, six groups) and a \"Limits\" list, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Groups: versioning from changesets (cascade policy, `status --check`, did-you-mean), control over what moves together (fixed and linked groups, per-package and glob rules, private registries), beyond changesets (commit inference, prerelease mode, snapshots, changelog layouts), releasing (publish order, tags, GitHub releases, product binaries, the single release PR, safe reruns, build provenance attestation with SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify`, npm provenance), CI and automation (what `init` generates and the three composite actions), and scripting and stability (JSON, exit codes, platforms). Limits: Cargo, npm and PyPI only (`nuget` is accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher), no cross-language dependency inference, Python needs static or Poetry versions, no generated maturin workflow, GitHub Actions only, inference-only releases get no managed release PR, releases across registries are not atomic, OIDC trusted publishing is planned, no Windows."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":880279,"output_tokens":1782,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1059},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":880279,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JQWwLcvQKtNbf2HZmmThB9":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs_catchup.md","old_string":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).","new_string":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section (about 60 lines, six groups) and a \"Limits\" list, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Groups: versioning from changesets (cascade policy, `status --check`, did-you-mean), control over what moves together (fixed and linked groups, per-package and glob rules, private registries), beyond changesets (commit inference, prerelease mode, snapshots, changelog layouts), releasing (publish order, tags, GitHub releases, product binaries, the single release PR, safe reruns, build provenance attestation with SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify`, npm provenance), CI and automation (what `init` generates and the three composite actions), and scripting and stability (JSON, exit codes, platforms). Limits: Cargo, npm and PyPI only (`nuget` is accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher), no cross-language dependency inference, Python needs static or Poetry versions, no generated maturin workflow, GitHub Actions only, inference-only releases get no managed release PR, releases across registries are not atomic, OIDC trusted publishing is planned, no Windows."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"087de9ed-33eb-43a3-bd74-2c6c843b8ca8","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgxXostyWTejNRxGpvSzD","requestRef":"845bcc2f-a3d2-4e75-9599-5dba3a382723","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8446be5c-88d4-4ca3-bb3e-a97553badad2","timestamp":"2026-11-12T06:06:47.254Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/catch-up-with-0-20","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"8446be5c-88d4-4ca3-bb3e-a97553badad2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37a6d940-ad15-4126-9323-e42ac0035d05","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQWwLcvQKtNbf2HZmmThB9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs_catchup.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"47bb64eb-1a6d-47ed-b447-c0d8a62a3d7a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T06:06:47.397Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs_catchup.md","oldString":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).","newString":"- README: a new \"What you get\" section (about 60 lines, six groups) and a \"Limits\" list, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Groups: versioning from changesets (cascade policy, `status --check`, did-you-mean), control over what moves together (fixed and linked groups, per-package and glob rules, private registries), beyond changesets (commit inference, prerelease mode, snapshots, changelog layouts), releasing (publish order, tags, GitHub releases, product binaries, the single release PR, safe reruns, build provenance attestation with SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify`, npm provenance), CI and automation (what `init` generates and the three composite actions), and scripting and stability (JSON, exit codes, platforms). Limits: Cargo, npm and PyPI only (`nuget` is accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher), no cross-language dependency inference, Python needs static or Poetry versions, no generated maturin workflow, GitHub Actions only, inference-only releases get no managed release PR, releases across registries are not atomic, OIDC trusted publishing is planned, no Windows.","originalFile":"## Summary\n- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).\n- ARCHITECTURE.md: two invariants. A failure caused by a flag value exits 2 and everything else exits 1, decided per error type by `exit_kind()` with runtime as the default. Every `--format json` report goes through the typed `Report` envelope (`emit_report`), and untyped JSON output is crate-private.\n- Ten stale or missing statements fixed in `docs/architecture/{versioning,wire-compat,identity,release}.md`, `docs/how-callisto-works.md` (yarn and bun are supported) and `docs/publishing.md` (yarn registry advice, E168 and `npmPublishRegistry`). Worst ones: `versioning.md` said `uncovered_changes` was not wired into the CLI or PR body (it feeds `ReleasePreview.unreleased`), and `wire-compat.md` called `schema --type snapshot` the status report.\n- `docs/releasing.md` and `docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md` were checked and needed nothing. Left out of the README on purpose: the floating `v1` tag and the \"Hold release PR\" draft state (this repo's own workflow, not generated for users) and a checksum file (none is generated).\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Documentation only\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: docs only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] README, ARCHITECTURE.md and the architecture and guide pages above. `docs/errors.md`, `config.md`, `stability.md` and `docs/specs/*` were audited and updated in earlier PRs.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just doc-check`, `just pre-push` and `just lint` exit 0. Quick start, `status`, `version --dry-run`, `release --dry-run`, the dirty-tree error (E267), `--package` (E102, exit 2), `pre enter` (E324), `release pending --from` (E327), the `--emit-decision` path rules, `--format json` and `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` were run on a fixture.\n- [x] I re-checked the supply-chain claims in code: the generated matrix workflow uses `actions/attest-build-provenance`, `release_artifacts.rs` compares SHA-256 and size and then runs `gh attestation verify` against a recorded repository and workflow policy, and generated workflows set `NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE`.\n- [ ] Not verified (left as written): the four-attempt retry in `releasing.md` (checked in the action script only); a yarn or bun publish (not run); Python build-backend breadth beyond `python -m build`; npm provenance end to end (code read only); `gh attestation verify` against a real release. Anything needing a registry or GitHub was checked in code and help text only.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":5,"lines":[" ## Summary","-- README: a new \"What you get\" section states what Callisto ships, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Ecosystems and package managers (Cargo; npm, pnpm, yarn, bun; Python via static PEP 621 or Poetry, `python -m build` and Twine), napi-rs platform packages, tags, GitHub releases, supply chain (build provenance attestation of each Cargo binary asset, SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify` before upload, npm provenance), the single release PR, safe reruns, and scripting (`--dry-run`, `schemaVersion`, exit 2).","+- README: a new \"What you get\" section (about 60 lines, six groups) and a \"Limits\" list, with each claim linked to the doc that explains it. Groups: versioning from changesets (cascade policy, `status --check`, did-you-mean), control over what moves together (fixed and linked groups, per-package and glob rules, private registries), beyond changesets (commit inference, prerelease mode, snapshots, changelog layouts), releasing (publish order, tags, GitHub releases, product binaries, the single release PR, safe reruns, build provenance attestation with SHA-256 and `gh attestation verify`, npm provenance), CI and automation (what `init` generates and the three composite actions), and scripting and stability (JSON, exit codes, platforms). Limits: Cargo, npm and PyPI only (`nuget` is accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher), no cross-language dependency inference, Python needs static or Poetry versions, no generated maturin workflow, GitHub Actions only, inference-only releases get no managed release PR, releases across registries are not atomic, OIDC trusted publishing is planned, no Windows."," - ARCHITECTURE.md: two invariants. A failure caused by a flag value exits 2 and everything else exits 1, decided per error type by `exit_kind()` with runtime as the default. Every `--format json` report goes through the typed `Report` envelope (`emit_report`), and untyped JSON output is crate-private."," - Ten stale or missing statements fixed in `docs/architecture/{versioning,wire-compat,identity,release}.md`, `docs/how-callisto-works.md` (yarn and bun are supported) and `docs/publishing.md` (yarn registry advice, E168 and `npmPublishRegistry`). Worst ones: `versioning.md` said `uncovered_changes` was not wired into the CLI or PR body (it feeds `ReleasePreview.unreleased`), and `wire-compat.md` called `schema --type snapshot` the status report."," - `docs/releasing.md` and `docs/architecture/polyglot-v1.md` were checked and needed nothing. Left out of the README on purpose: the floating `v1` tag and the \"Hold release PR\" draft state (this repo's own workflow, not generated for users) and a checksum file (none is generated)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"087de9ed-33eb-43a3-bd74-2c6c843b8ca8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","branch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8446be5c-88d4-4ca3-bb3e-a97553badad2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/catch-up-with-0-20","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
