{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"5d548444-7fd2-4101-8db9-881e0a259e54","timestamp":"2026-11-12T06:06:56.955Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"061c200486ebc9b0312f567dd75bc581bc0a5e74fd96255fbb8887ebe6350a68","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"ff10572f-834c-4250-a5d1-c24cb3fe5fb8","keep":1267,"tail":["4dfa2129772c141bfee99682c10208bb6e9c9e609f440eb495c49eec5d4ef2c1","f9b4ec99cadb50ff1c12a0ac7f10cf75ec1a00d7b0628e1593422301c07458d5","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1269,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"bbbc6e5a0e92d4742137096a66187613522d21d66ddd84b06f28df64a1f12d87"}
{"parentUuid":"d0f70817-dade-42e4-ad0a-b92a7cf36d52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxXqZYiwnGs9C92rQieK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The README section is now substantial. It's pushed to #532, all four commits show `valid` on GitHub, and the description is updated to match.\n\n**What it covers now** (about 60 lines in 6 groups, every bullet linked to the doc that explains it)\n- **Versioning from changesets:** the `@changesets/cli`-compatible format, `status --check` as a CI gate, the cascade policy, lockfile refresh, and did-you-mean.\n- **Control over what moves together:** fixed and linked groups, per-package and glob rules, and private registries with their own timeouts.\n- **Beyond changesets:** commit inference with `pre-major-inference`, prerelease mode, snapshots, and changelog layouts.\n- **Releasing:** publish order, tags, GitHub releases, product binaries, the single release PR, safe reruns, and the attestation and provenance facts.\n- **CI and automation:** what `init` generates (simple and matrix) and the three composite actions.\n- **Scripting and stability:** JSON on every command, exit codes, and the five supported platforms.\n\n**Limits list** (8 verified bullets), including some you might not have wanted in public: inference-only releases get no managed release PR, `nuget` is accepted in `publish-to` with no publisher, releases across registries aren't atomic, there's no generated maturin workflow, and OIDC publishing is planned, not built. I'd keep them, because a README that states its limits is more credible. Say if you'd rather soften any.\n\n**Not verified, so read these:** the agent couldn't run anything needing a registry or GitHub, so `confirm-timeout` waiting, safe reruns, npm provenance and `gh attestation verify` against a real release are doc or code reads. Performance isn't claimed, because it wasn't measured.\n\n**One oddity I couldn't explain:** the repo's workflows and `callisto-validate/action.yml` reference local actions as `uses: $/.github/actions/...`. I confirmed the bytes (`24 2f 2e`, a literal `$`, in both git and GitHub's copy), and a test pins that exact string. The release run's log still shows GitHub executing `orin-dx/callisto/.github/actions/setup-callisto@<sha>`. Releases and CI work, so I didn't change anything, but I don't understand the mechanism and don't want to guess.\n\nneeds input: read the README section on the branch (I'd focus on the attestation line and the Limits list), then merge #530, #531 and #532 when CI passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":883158,"output_tokens":822,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":883158,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bfeba50a-1973-453a-8776-a3675d040282","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxXqZ9QtfSmycsFmHBvb","requestRef":"5d548444-7fd2-4101-8db9-881e0a259e54","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6b978d65-b259-4c8f-9aed-3126f2fb52e5","timestamp":"2026-11-12T06:07:02.970Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4