{"parentUuid":"517a46c0-d35a-4dc5-a206-8fbe74e20a70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxcMLmZxZv13bFm7kBa4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":896216,"output_tokens":1986,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1017},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1986,"cache_read_input_tokens":896216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13660,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ba78d14b-830a-4b2c-9a16-a594b3881d03","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxcMLMGLd4djgpxCjFUb","requestRef":"883577b0-8c04-4418-9b37-d8c2d9593def","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"00a7d86e-ba23-49ef-ad18-57df0332623a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:06:22.641Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"00a7d86e-ba23-49ef-ad18-57df0332623a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxcMLmZxZv13bFm7kBa4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The agents are still running, so I'm keeping them going. While I wait, here are the two decision briefs I offered. E194 turned out to be narrower than my notes made it sound.\n\n**E194, shared `v{version}` tags**\n- **What it is:** an `init` guard. When a repo already has several packages sharing one `v1.2.3`-style tag (a lock-step monorepo convention), `init` refuses to scaffold, because Callisto tags each package on its own and the old tags would be adopted wrongly. Its help already says how to proceed: give each package its own `[[package]]` `tag-template`, with `previous-tag-templates` for the old shared tags. Those keys exist today.\n- **The real gap:** a lock-step group still gets one tag and one GitHub release per package, never a single `v1.2.3` release. That's what migrating adopters would miss.\n- **Options:**\n  1. **Do nothing and keep the guidance.** Zero new surface.\n  2. **Add a `release-title` template** for the product's GitHub release. Small, but one more permanent key at 1.0.\n  3. **Let a fixed group share one tag and one release.** This changes tag identity (ADR 9) and ownership (ADR 12), plus the release notes and the receipt. It's a large design change.\n- **Recommendation:** option 1 now. Revisit option 2 only when a real adopter needs it, since you've asked for fewer permanent keys. Option 3 only if migrations turn out to be common.\n\n**OIDC trusted publishing** (the plan in `docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md`, targeted after v1)\n- **Decision 1: should Callisto's own workflow allow `id-token: write` on `execute`?** I'd say yes, but only on `execute`, which already holds the registry secrets, and only when the OIDC publishing exists and you've verified it. The policy check forbids it today, so it's your call.\n- **Decision 2: the shape of the switch.** I'd choose a generated-workflow option and not a `callisto.toml` key, because Callisto doesn't mint tokens (ADR 4). That adds no config surface. Callisto's own changes would be small: stop writing the temporary npm config's `NPM_TOKEN` entry when OIDC is chosen, add a diagnostic hint for npm's misleading E404 on a trusted-publisher mismatch, and generate the crates.io auth step.\n- **The unverified risk that decides the effort:** whether an empty `NPM_TOKEN` entry stops npm falling back to OIDC. It needs a scratch package on each registry, which only you can set up. I'd do that spike before any code.\n\nThe hunt for regressions in the 0.20 code is still running. I'll bring back its verified findings.\n\nneeds input: your calls on E194 (I'd leave it) and the OIDC decisions (the `execute` permission and the generated-workflow shape), whenever convenient."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":896216,"output_tokens":1986,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1017},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1986,"cache_read_input_tokens":896216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ba78d14b-830a-4b2c-9a16-a594b3881d03","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgxcMLMGLd4djgpxCjFUb","requestRef":"883577b0-8c04-4418-9b37-d8c2d9593def","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"653e0d71-fe05-485f-8c55-2a4ac7dac58c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:06:24.690Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
