{"parentUuid":"3f739df3-89e9-42b0-ba0c-dd64f4f253bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxd4putRXWvXLw2ATS5L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011KiN5QDJwbL1N5CkexW1s7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix subdirectory workspace sibling bugs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\", \"Fixing bugs\": grep for structurally identical code) and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change, prefer reusing one helper over copies, add NO error code/flag/key; one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`, one commit per numbered bug; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after the last commit: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nBACKGROUND: #511 fixed object specs (`rev:./path`) for a workspace in a SUBDIRECTORY of the git repo (repo/ws). A regression hunt found two siblings that still break there (git paths are repo-top-relative unless told otherwise; Callisto compares them with workspace-relative paths):\nBUG 1: `release plan --from-release-commit <sha> --decision .callisto/release-decision.json` fails with E165 ('release-decision file was not written by this commit') when the workspace is `repo/ws`. Cause: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs ~439-447 runs `git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-status -r --no-renames <parent> <commit>` without `--relative`, so paths are `ws/.callisto/...` while `decision_path` and the changeset dir are workspace-relative (~460 `require_version_commit_shape`). IMPORTANT: that function is also a SAFETY check ('touched only the paths a version commit may touch'); do NOT weaken it by hiding edits outside the workspace. Prefer converting in one direction while keeping out-of-workspace paths visible (for example prefix the expected workspace-relative paths with `git rev-parse --show-prefix` output, or strip the prefix from in-workspace paths and leave others untouched so they are still flagged). Reuse any existing helper that already knows the workspace's prefix inside the repo (grep `show-prefix`, `relative`, `prefix` in crates/callisto-model/src/vcs).\nBUG 2: the interrupted-version guard (E121) goes blind for subdirectory workspaces: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs ~660 (`SourceChanges::since`) runs `git diff --name-only` and `git diff --cached --name-only` without `--relative`, so the staged-path match never hits; and ~629 `manifest_blob_in_index` uses `format!(\":{path}\")` which resolves from the repo top (should be `:./{path}`, the index-lookup sibling of `object_at` in release_decision.rs). Repro: workspace at repo/ws, run `version` (stages the bump), `git restore --worktree --source=HEAD ws/p/Cargo.toml` so disk matches HEAD but the index holds the bump, run `version` again: expected E121 rc 1 (as when the workspace is the repo root), actual rc 0.\nTASK for EACH bug: (a) reproduce with the REAL binary first (build once: `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; fixtures under $TMPDIR; a git repo `r/` with the callisto workspace in `r/ws`, a cargo package, changeset, tag as needed; compare against the same layout at the repo root where it works), show the failing output; (b) write the regression test in the existing real-git test style (see the `a_workspace_below_the_repository_root_...` tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs and commands/version/tests.rs from #511, and crates/callisto-cli/tests) so it fails before and passes after; (c) fix; (d) grep for any OTHER `git diff`, `git diff-tree`, `git ls-files`, `git status`, `git show :path`/`git cat-file` call that feeds workspace-relative comparisons without `--relative` or `:./` (crates/callisto-graph/src, crates/callisto-model/src/vcs, crates/callisto-cli/src) and report each with 'affected / not affected and why'; fix any that are affected the same way (extra commit).\nREPORT (under 250 words): the repro output before/after for each bug, the sweep table, what you changed, commits signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"output_tokens":5763,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":638},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5763,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011KiN5QDJwbL1N5CkexW1s7":{"description":"Fix subdirectory workspace sibling bugs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"high","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true