_version_commit_shape`). IMPORTANT: that function is also a SAFETY check ('touched only the paths a version commit may touch'); do NOT weaken it by hiding edits outside the workspace. Prefer converting in one direction while keeping out-of-workspace paths visible (for example prefix the expected workspace-relative paths with `git rev-parse --show-prefix` output, or strip the prefix from in-workspace paths and leave others untouched so they are still flagged). Reuse any existing helper that already knows the workspace's prefix inside the repo (grep `show-prefix`, `relative`, `prefix` in crates/callisto-model/src/vcs).\nBUG 2: the interrupted-version guard (E121) goes blind for subdirectory workspaces: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs ~660 (`SourceChanges::since`) runs `git diff --name-only` and `git diff --cached --name-only` without `--relative`, so the staged-path match never hits; and ~629 `manifest_blob_in_index` uses `format!(\":{path}\")` which resolves from the repo top (should be `:./{path}`, the index-lookup sibling of `object_at` in release_decision.rs). Repro: workspace at repo/ws, run `version` (stages the bump), `git restore --worktree --source=HEAD ws/p/Cargo.toml` so disk matches HEAD but the index holds the bump, run `version` again: expected E121 rc 1 (as when the workspace is the repo root), actual rc 0.\nTASK for EACH bug: (a) reproduce with the REAL binary first (build once: `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; fixtures under $TMPDIR; a git repo `r/` with the callisto workspace in `r/ws`, a cargo package, changeset, tag as needed; compare against the same layout at the repo root where it works), show the failing output; (b) write the regression test in the existing real-git test style (see the `a_workspace_below_the_repository_root_...` tests in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs and commands/version/tests.rs from #511, and crates/callisto-cli/tests) so it fails before and passes after; (c) fix; (d) grep for any OTHER `git diff`, `git diff-tree`, `git ls-files`, `git status`, `git show :path`/`git cat-file` call that feeds workspace-relative comparisons without `--relative` or `:./` (crates/callisto-graph/src, crates/callisto-model/src/vcs, crates/callisto-cli/src) and report each with 'affected / not affected and why'; fix any that are affected the same way (extra commit).\nREPORT (under 250 words): the repro output before/after for each bug, the sweep table, what you changed, commits signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3971138a-aaaf-4e46-ae0c-9d4ffcbb1554","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgxd4pZnuNm4FoNrNYvFn","requestRef":"2093630e-5b6b-4a4b-8912-39f31531a1ee","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f944d203-8977-4d7d-9b7c-c0bfd85d1866","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:15:49.174Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"f944d203-8977-4d7d-9b7c-c0bfd85d1866","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxd4putRXWvXLw2ATS5L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012VZujCtdRrKCrMZwXPuDVL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Validate emit-decision before version mutates","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\") and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change, reuse existing validation, add NO error code/flag/key (reuse E225/E226 or the existing error for an invalid path); one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (found by a hunt, all reproduced with the binary): `callisto version --emit-decision <path>` validates only the SHAPE of the path (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs `workspace_decision_path`, ~480-530, added in #528; called from crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs ~50-55) but the file is written only AFTER the plan is applied. So `--emit-decision .changeset`, `--emit-decision .`, or an absolute path equal to the workspace root bump and stage manifests, delete the changeset, and then fail with E213 'Is a directory' (rc 1), leaving the workspace half-versioned (a rerun then fails E121 until the user resets by hand). Also in the same function: (a) a RELATIVE path is never canonicalized, so `link/d.json` through an in-workspace symlink `link -> /outside` writes outside the workspace root while the absolute spelling of the same file is rejected (E225); (b) `out/` (trailing slash) silently writes a file named `out`; (c) `.git/d.json` is accepted; (d) an absolute path with `..` after a missing component gives a misleading E213 (before any mutation, lower priority).\nTASK: reproduce (a few lines each, real binary built once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`, fixtures in $TMPDIR; a repo with a cargo workspace, a changeset) then fix so the target is validated BEFORE anything mutates: reject a path that resolves to an existing directory or to the workspace root, a trailing-slash path, any path whose resolved location (canonicalizing the nearest existing ancestor, for RELATIVE paths as well as absolute, following in-workspace symlinks) is outside the workspace root, and anything inside `.git`; all with the existing E225 (outside) or E226 (invalid path) at exit 2, and nothing written or mutated. Keep a valid new file under not-yet-existing directories working (`.callisto/nested/release-decision.json`, relative and absolute: see the test added in #528 `version_emit_decision_to_an_absolute_path_whose_directories_do_not_exist_yet_still_writes_it`), and keep the release PR action's use working (`--emit-decision \"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\"` with a relative default; see .github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/). Share one helper between `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision`, `release pending --decision`. Add real-binary tests to crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (one invocation per rejected spelling, asserting exit 2, the error code, and that Cargo.toml and the changeset are untouched); watch each fail before the fix.\nREPORT (under 200 words): reproduction results, what changed, tests added (and that they failed before), commit signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"output_tokens":5763,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":638},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5763,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012VZujCtdRrKCrMZwXPuDVL":{"description":"Validate emit-decision before version mutates","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\") and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change, reuse existing validation, add NO error code/flag/key (reuse E225/E226 or the existing error for an invalid path); one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (found by a hunt, all reproduced with the binary): `callisto version --emit-decision <path>` validates only the SHAPE of the path (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs `workspace_decision_path`, ~480-530, added in #528; called from crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs ~50-55) but the file is written only AFTER the plan is applied. So `--emit-decision .changeset`, `--emit-decision .`, or an absolute path equal to the workspace root bump and stage manifests, delete the changeset, and then fail with E213 'Is a directory' (rc 1), leaving the workspace half-versioned (a rerun then fails E121 until the user resets by hand). Also in the same function: (a) a RELATIVE path is never canonicalized, so `link/d.json` through an in-workspace symlink `link -> /outside` writes outside the workspace root while the absolute spelling of the same file is rejected (E225); (b) `out/` (trailing slash) silently writes a file named `out`; (c) `.git/d.json` is accepted; (d) an absolute path with `..` after a missing component gives a misleading E213 (before any mutation, lower priority).\nTASK: reproduce (a few lines each, real binary built once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`, fixtures in $TMPDIR; a repo with a cargo workspace, a changeset) then fix so the target is validated BEFORE anything mutates: reject a path that resolves to an existing directory or to the workspace root, a trailing-slash path, any path whose resolved location (canonicalizing the nearest existing ancestor, for RELATIVE paths as well as absolute, following in-workspace symlinks) is outside the workspace root, and anything inside `.git`; all with the existing E225 (outside) or E226 (invalid path) at exit 2, and nothing written or mutated. Keep a valid new file under not-yet-existing directories working (`.callisto/nested/release-decision.json`, relative and absolute: see the test added in #528 `version_emit_decision_to_an_absolute_path_whose_directories_do_not_exist_yet_still_writes_it`), and keep the release PR action's use working (`--emit-decision \"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\"` with a relative default; see .github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/). Share one helper between `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision`, `release pending --decision`. Add real-binary tests to crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (one invocation per rejected spelling, asserting exit 2, the error code, and that Cargo.toml and the changeset are untouched); watch each fail before the fix.\nREPORT (under 200 words): reproduction results, what changed, tests added (and that they failed before), commit signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3971138a-aaaf-4e46-ae0c-9d4ffcbb1554","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgxd4pZnuNm4FoNrNYvFn","requestRef":"2093630e-5b6b-4a4b-8912-39f31531a1ee","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b464eb91-d99a-4a2a-90ad-fa9a0df0dda6","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:15:59.141Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b464eb91-d99a-4a2a-90ad-fa9a0df0dda6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxd4putRXWvXLw2ATS5L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VEzbuKy8VXpMTez4nUpf9s","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Parenthesized PEP 508 requirements","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\": prefer a crate already in Cargo.lock over a hand-written grammar) . `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/python-parenthesized-requirements origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change; add no error code/flag/key; one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/python-parenthesized-requirements`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (reproduced by a hunt with the real binary): a Python dependency written with the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized specifier, `dependencies = [\"core (==1.0.0)\"]`, is not recognized as a dependency on `core`. In a pypi workspace where `app` depends on `core (==1.0.0)`, bumping core to 2.0.0 does not cascade to app and app's pin stays `core (==1.0.0)`, while the same pin written `core==1.0.0` is rewritten correctly. Cause: `Requirement::parse` in crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs (~146-170) splits the name at the first operator character, so the name becomes `core (`. A related risk read from the code (not run): a requirement of the form `core[extra] @ https://...` renders with a stray `]` appended to the URL.\nTASK: (1) reproduce the parenthesized case through the real binary (build once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; fixture under $TMPDIR with two pypi packages (PEP 621 `pyproject.toml`), one depending on the other with parentheses; a changeset bumping the dependency) and show the missing cascade/rewrite; also run the `name[extra] @ url` case and report whether it is really broken. (2) Fix the parser so the name ends at the first of whitespace, `(`, `[`, `;`, `@`, a comparison operator or `,`, per the PEP 508 grammar, and a parenthesized specifier is read as the version spec (and rendered back in the form it was written, so a rewrite of the pin keeps the user's parentheses style). Check whether the `pep440_rs` crate already used by this crate (crates/callisto-manifests, grep `pep440_rs`) or another crate in Cargo.lock parses PEP 508 requirement strings (pep508_rs is NOT necessarily present: do not add a dependency; only reuse what is already a dependency); if one already fits, prefer it over extending the hand-written parser, otherwise extend the parser minimally. Keep the earlier one-bracket-pair extras behavior and the proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passing; run it with a high case count once (PROPTEST_CASES=20000) and report. (3) Tests: a deterministic test on the parenthesized case (fails before, passes after), one for the URL-with-extras case if it is real, and make sure a rewritten pin retains its form. Check the dependency-graph side too: the cascade must find the dependent (grep where Requirement names are matched against package names).\nREPORT (under 200 words): reproduction before/after, what changed, whether an existing crate was reused, proptest result, commit signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"output_tokens":5763,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":638},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5763,"cache_read_input_tokens":903920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VEzbuKy8VXpMTez4nUpf9s":{"description":"Parenthesized PEP 508 requirements","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\": prefer a crate already in Cargo.lock over a hand-written grammar) . `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/python-parenthesized-requirements origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change; add no error code/flag/key; one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/python-parenthesized-requirements`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (reproduced by a hunt with the real binary): a Python dependency written with the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized specifier, `dependencies = [\"core (==1.0.0)\"]`, is not recognized as a dependency on `core`. In a pypi workspace where `app` depends on `core (==1.0.0)`, bumping core to 2.0.0 does not cascade to app and app's pin stays `core (==1.0.0)`, while the same pin written `core==1.0.0` is rewritten correctly. Cause: `Requirement::parse` in crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs (~146-170) splits the name at the first operator character, so the name becomes `core (`. A related risk read from the code (not run): a requirement of the form `core[extra] @ https://...` renders with a stray `]` appended to the URL.\nTASK: (1) reproduce the parenthesized case through the real binary (build once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; fixture under $TMPDIR with two pypi packages (PEP 621 `pyproject.toml`), one depending on the other with parentheses; a changeset bumping the dependency) and show the missing cascade/rewrite; also run the `name[extra] @ url` case and report whether it is really broken. (2) Fix the parser so the name ends at the first of whitespace, `(`, `[`, `;`, `@`, a comparison operator or `,`, per the PEP 508 grammar, and a parenthesized specifier is read as the version spec (and rendered back in the form it was written, so a rewrite of the pin keeps the user's parentheses style). Check whether the `pep440_rs` crate already used by this crate (crates/callisto-manifests, grep `pep440_rs`) or another crate in Cargo.lock parses PEP 508 requirement strings (pep508_rs is NOT necessarily present: do not add a dependency; only reuse what is already