{"parentUuid":"b464eb91-d99a-4a2a-90ad-fa9a0df0dda6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54b26ed8-b071-4ecb-982a-8303d963cdc1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012VZujCtdRrKCrMZwXPuDVL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a60b96e3da64503b6 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a60b96e3da64503b6', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a60b96e3da64503b6.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"7781054b-658d-4c20-8613-71038d548b45","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:16:09.797Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a60b96e3da64503b6","description":"Validate emit-decision before version mutates","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\") and docs/stability.md. `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change, reuse existing validation, add NO error code/flag/key (reuse E225/E226 or the existing error for an invalid path); one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/validate-decision-target-before-apply`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (found by a hunt, all reproduced with the binary): `callisto version --emit-decision <path>` validates only the SHAPE of the path (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs `workspace_decision_path`, ~480-530, added in #528; called from crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/version.rs ~50-55) but the file is written only AFTER the plan is applied. So `--emit-decision .changeset`, `--emit-decision .`, or an absolute path equal to the workspace root bump and stage manifests, delete the changeset, and then fail with E213 'Is a directory' (rc 1), leaving the workspace half-versioned (a rerun then fails E121 until the user resets by hand). Also in the same function: (a) a RELATIVE path is never canonicalized, so `link/d.json` through an in-workspace symlink `link -> /outside` writes outside the workspace root while the absolute spelling of the same file is rejected (E225); (b) `out/` (trailing slash) silently writes a file named `out`; (c) `.git/d.json` is accepted; (d) an absolute path with `..` after a missing component gives a misleading E213 (before any mutation, lower priority).\nTASK: reproduce (a few lines each, real binary built once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`, fixtures in $TMPDIR; a repo with a cargo workspace, a changeset) then fix so the target is validated BEFORE anything mutates: reject a path that resolves to an existing directory or to the workspace root, a trailing-slash path, any path whose resolved location (canonicalizing the nearest existing ancestor, for RELATIVE paths as well as absolute, following in-workspace symlinks) is outside the workspace root, and anything inside `.git`; all with the existing E225 (outside) or E226 (invalid path) at exit 2, and nothing written or mutated. Keep a valid new file under not-yet-existing directories working (`.callisto/nested/release-decision.json`, relative and absolute: see the test added in #528 `version_emit_decision_to_an_absolute_path_whose_directories_do_not_exist_yet_still_writes_it`), and keep the release PR action's use working (`--emit-decision \"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\"` with a relative default; see .github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/). Share one helper between `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision`, `release pending --decision`. Add real-binary tests to crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (one invocation per rejected spelling, asserting exit 2, the error code, and that Cargo.toml and the changeset are untouched); watch each fail before the fix.\nREPORT (under 200 words): reproduction results, what changed, tests added (and that they failed before), commit signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a60b96e3da64503b6.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3971138a-aaaf-4e46-ae0c-9d4ffcbb1554","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","branch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","default