{"parentUuid":"03fbf9a1-ea6a-4f88-b965-523a220ebe06","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"54b26ed8-b071-4ecb-982a-8303d963cdc1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VEzbuKy8VXpMTez4nUpf9s","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a3253dad6be025c8c (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a3253dad6be025c8c', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3253dad6be025c8c.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"c5dc99b4-9dc9-4656-a9cf-b69afdfee2b2","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:16:09.811Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a3253dad6be025c8c","description":"Parenthesized PEP 508 requirements","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). Read AGENTS.md (\"Enforcing an invariant\": prefer a crate already in Cargo.lock over a hand-written grammar) . `git fetch origin` then `git switch -c fix/python-parenthesized-requirements origin/main`.\nHOUSE RULES: smallest correct change; add no error code/flag/key; one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY. Commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links. Verify by EXIT CODE with the repo's recipes, one at a time, run with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true after committing: `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts` (all exit 0; `just test` has one known environment failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` (needs registry tools; passes in CI): report it, do not fix it; re-run workflow-contracts once if it flakes). Push `git push -u origin fix/python-parenthesized-requirements`. No PR, no changeset (the caller writes it).\nPROBLEM (reproduced by a hunt with the real binary): a Python dependency written with the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized specifier, `dependencies = [\"core (==1.0.0)\"]`, is not recognized as a dependency on `core`. In a pypi workspace where `app` depends on `core (==1.0.0)`, bumping core to 2.0.0 does not cascade to app and app's pin stays `core (==1.0.0)`, while the same pin written `core==1.0.0` is rewritten correctly. Cause: `Requirement::parse` in crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs (~146-170) splits the name at the first operator character, so the name becomes `core (`. A related risk read from the code (not run): a requirement of the form `core[extra] @ https://...` renders with a stray `]` appended to the URL.\nTASK: (1) reproduce the parenthesized case through the real binary (build once with `cargo build -q -p callisto-cli`; fixture under $TMPDIR with two pypi packages (PEP 621 `pyproject.toml`), one depending on the other with parentheses; a changeset bumping the dependency) and show the missing cascade/rewrite; also run the `name[extra] @ url` case and report whether it is really broken. (2) Fix the parser so the name ends at the first of whitespace, `(`, `[`, `;`, `@`, a comparison operator or `,`, per the PEP 508 grammar, and a parenthesized specifier is read as the version spec (and rendered back in the form it was written, so a rewrite of the pin keeps the user's parentheses style). Check whether the `pep440_rs` crate already used by this crate (crates/callisto-manifests, grep `pep440_rs`) or another crate in Cargo.lock parses PEP 508 requirement strings (pep508_rs is NOT necessarily present: do not add a dependency; only reuse what is already a dependency); if one already fits, prefer it over extending the hand-written parser, otherwise extend the parser minimally. Keep the earlier one-bracket-pair extras behavior and the proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passing; run it with a high case count once (PROPTEST_CASES=20000) and report. (3) Tests: a deterministic test on the parenthesized case (fails before, passes after), one for the URL-with-extras case if it is real, and make sure a rewritten pin retains its form. Check the dependency-graph side too: the cascade must find the dependent (grep where Requirement names are matched against package names).\nREPORT (under 200 words): reproduction before/after, what changed, whether an existing crate was reused, proptest result, commit signed?, five exit codes (and the known failing test).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3253dad6be025c8c.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3971138a-aaaf-4e46-ae0c-9d4ffcbb1554","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d","branch":"fix/no-pending-changesets-message","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto