ack":true,"handbackReportText":"`git fetch origin` failed (sandbox blocked github.com:22), so I used the existing local origin refs. Their tips may be stale. Both branch diffs and the `.changeset/` listing came from those refs.\n\n**Unreleased `.changeset/` on origin/main:** only `version-no-empty-warning-on-inferred-bump.md`, which is unrelated. There is no `contain-decision-paths` file. The \"decision paths must stay inside the workspace\" changeset (commit 1504d3364) was already consumed by `8b4102afe chore(release): version packages`, and `crates/callisto-cli/CHANGELOG.md` mentions it. So neither outcome folds in, and both are `disposition: new`. Decision (2) is not folded into `contain-decision-paths`, because that entry is already released. It is a separate patch for the released check.\n\nNote: the facts brief called the entry unreleased, but main shows it released. Re-check after a successful fetch. If main has since moved and the file is back unreleased, switch (2) to `update-existing`.\n\n## File 1: `.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md`\n\n```markdown\n---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\nPython dependencies written as `name (==1.0.0)` are now recognized, so bumping that dependency releases its dependents and updates the pin.\n\n- Before, the legacy parenthesized form was not seen as a dependency: the dependent was not released and its pin stayed old. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n- Now a bump of `name` to 2.0.0 patch-releases the dependent and rewrites the pin to `name (==2.0.0)`, keeping the parentheses.\n- A requirement like `name[extra] @ https://...` is now read with the URL kept out of the extras.\n- You do not need to do anything. If you had worked around this by rewriting pins to `name==1.0.0`, you can leave them.\n```\n\n## File 2: `.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md`\n\n```markdown\n---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\n`callisto version --emit-decision <path>` now rejects a bad path before it changes anything, instead of failing after the workspace is already half-versioned.\n\n- Before, only the shape of the path was checked up front, and the file was written at the end. A path that was a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root), had a trailing slash, or was inside `.git` failed late with `E213` (\"Is a directory\", exit 1). By then manifests were bumped and staged and changesets deleted, and a rerun failed with `E121`.\n- A relative path through an in-workspace symlink that points outside the workspace wrote the file outside the workspace.\n- Now one check runs first, and it also covers `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. All rejections exit 2 with nothing written:\n  - `E225`: the path resolves outside the workspace.\n  - `E226`: the workspace root, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, or a path that cannot be resolved.\n- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works.\n- If a script expected the late `E213` (exit 1) for these paths, expect `E225` or `E226` with exit 2 instead, and nothing is changed.\n```\n\n## changeset@3 JSON\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"summary\": \"Python dependencies written as `name (==1.0.0)` are now recognized, so bumping that dependency releases its dependents and updates the pin.\\n\\n- Before, the legacy parenthesized form was not seen as a dependency: the dependent was not released and its pin stayed old. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\\n- Now a bump of `name` to 2.0.0 patch-releases the dependent and rewrites the pin to `name (==2.0.0)`, keeping the parentheses.\\n- A requirement like `name[extra] @ https://...` is now read with the URL kept out of the extras.\\n- You do not need to do anything. If you had worked around this by rewriting pins to `name==1.0.0`, you can leave them.\",\n    \"disposition\": \"new\",\n    \"consumer_impact\": \"behavior-change\",\n    \"semver_impact\": \"patch\",\n    \"files_changed\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/python/tests.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-manifests/proptest-regressions/python/tests.txt\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/python_dependency_tables_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"tests_added\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-manifests/src/python/tests.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/python_dependency_tables_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance_criteria_met\": [\"unlinked\"],\n    \"breaking_changes\": [],\n    \"commits\": [\"590249b7d\"],\n    \"reasoning\": \"Semver row: bug fix in runtime behavior -> patch. consumer_impact is behavior-change because existing observable output changes (a missed cascade and pin rewrite now happen). The tests file path for the CLI test is inferred from the stat's truncated path (.../tests/python_dependency_tables_tests.rs) and assumed under crates/callisto-cli; verify. The extras/URL parsing change is the same parser rewrite and the same reader outcome (Python requirement parsing), so it is a bullet, not a separate entry. No spec linked, so no criteria_evidence.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"summary\": \"`callisto version --emit-decision <path>` now rejects a bad path before it changes anything, instead of failing after the workspace is already half-versioned.\\n\\n- Before, only the shape of the path was checked up front, and the file was written at the end. A path that was a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root), had a trailing slash, or was inside `.git` failed late with `E213` (\\\"Is a directory\\\", exit 1). By then manifests were bumped and staged and changesets deleted, and a rerun failed with `E121`.\\n- A relative path through an in-workspace symlink that points outside the workspace wrote the file outside the workspace.\\n- Now one check runs first, and it also covers `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. All rejections exit 2 with nothing written:\\n  - `E225`: the path resolves outside the workspace.\\n  - `E226`: the workspace root, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, or a path that cannot be resolved.\\n- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works.\\n- If a script expected the late `E213` (exit 1) for these paths, expect `E225` or `E226` with exit 2 instead, and nothing is changed.\",\n    \"disposition\": \"new\",\n    \"consumer_impact\": \"behavior-change\",\n    \"semver_impact\": \"patch\",\n    \"files_changed\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/partial_run_tests.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"tests_added\": [\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs\",\n      \"crates/callisto-cli/tests/partial_run_tests.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance_criteria_met\": [\"unlinked\"],\n    \"breaking_changes\": [],\n    \"commits\": [\"aa3cb30a8\", \"2bd1d6f18\"],\n    \"reasoning\": \"Semver: a literal reading of the table (changed exit code scripts depend on -> major) was rejected. The affected paths previously produced a half-applied failure or an out-of-workspace write, and the check being tightened shipped in the 0.20.0 release that is already in CHANGELOG. This is a bug fix to that behavior, so patch, as the requester specified. Disposition new, not update-existing: .changeset/ on origin/main holds only version-no-empty-warning-on-inferred-bump.md and the contain-decision-paths entry was consumed by 8b4102afe; I couldn't re-fetch, so local origin/main may be stale. Commit attribution: two commits listed for this branch, one is likely the test adjustment in partial_run_tests.rs; which commit touched which file is unresolved. No spec linked, so no criteria_evidence.\"\n  }\n]\n```"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":246,"turnIndex":350},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","ent