{"parentUuid":"406596fb-ac6f-4b26-a9d4-d5909c651e55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxdj4E8saN4N5ZobsHJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019kPFQqVxBKdeHCwS1Foi52","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefName --jq '.[] | \"#\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"'","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":948505,"output_tokens":1045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1045,"cache_read_input_tokens":948505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019kPFQqVxBKdeHCwS1Foi52":{"command":"gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefName --jq '.[] | \"#\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"'","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a66be3a-d31a-411f-90a5-d3b475424efa","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgxdj3soKA7SmvvhF3Uwh","requestRef":"a929d012-ed1f-4b1e-adb8-50a9ea481ba7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"66e35213-a88d-4c86-ab8a-4f1be851bf75","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:24:11.268Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"66e35213-a88d-4c86-ab8a-4f1be851bf75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxdj4E8saN4N5ZobsHJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LnkGFyc5kSkhdVPZSRLfJa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md","content":"## Summary\n- A Python dependency written in the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized form `name (==1.0.0)` was not recognized as a dependency, so bumping that dependency did not cascade to the dependent and its pin stayed old. `Requirement::parse` split the name at the first operator character, so the name became `core (`. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n- `Requirement::parse` now ends the name at whitespace, `(`, `[`, `@`, `,` or a comparison operator. `Requirement` gains a `parenthesized` flag carried through both rewrite sites, so a rewritten pin keeps the user's form (`name (==2.0.0)`).\n- `name[extra] @ https://...` is parsed with the URL kept out of the extras (before, the extras absorbed `] @ url`, which would have rendered a stray `]` on a rewrite). The `;` marker split still comes first. Text after the name that is not a clause is dropped.\n- No new dependency: `pep440_rs` only parses version specifiers, and no crate in `Cargo.lock` parses PEP 508 requirement strings, so the hand parser was extended.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary through an end-to-end test: before the fix `app` stayed at 0.1.0 with its pin unchanged; after it is patch-released to 0.1.1 and the pin is `lib-py (==0.2.0)`. A second end-to-end test covers the URL-with-extras case, and two unit tests cover the parser.\n- [x] The proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passes at 20,000 cases; it caught a `\"(\"` edge case, which is fixed and added to the regression seeds.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":948505,"output_tokens":1045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1045,"cache_read_input_tokens":948505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LnkGFyc5kSkhdVPZSRLfJa":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md","content":"## Summary\n- A Python dependency written in the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized form `name (==1.0.0)` was not recognized as a dependency, so bumping that dependency did not cascade to the dependent and its pin stayed old. `Requirement::parse` split the name at the first operator character, so the name became `core (`. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n- `Requirement::parse` now ends the name at whitespace, `(`, `[`, `@`, `,` or a comparison operator. `Requirement` gains a `parenthesized` flag carried through both rewrite sites, so a rewritten pin keeps the user's form (`name (==2.0.0)`).\n- `name[extra] @ https://...` is parsed with the URL kept out of the extras (before, the extras absorbed `] @ url`, which would have rendered a stray `]` on a rewrite). The `;` marker split still comes first. Text after the name that is not a clause is dropped.\n- No new dependency: `pep440_rs` only parses version specifiers, and no crate in `Cargo.lock` parses PEP 508 requirement strings, so the hand parser was extended.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary through an end-to-end test: before the fix `app` stayed at 0.1.0 with its pin unchanged; after it is patch-released to 0.1.1 and the pin is `lib-py (==0.2.0)`. A second end-to-end test covers the URL-with-extras case, and two unit tests cover the parser.\n- [x] The proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passes at 20,000 cases; it caught a `\"(\"` edge case, which is fixed and added to the regression seeds.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a66be3a-d31a-411f-90a5-d3b475424efa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgxdj3soKA7SmvvhF3Uwh","requestRef":"a929d012-ed1f-4b1e-adb8-50a9ea481ba7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91b95dd2-fccb-4b4d-9cfe-3a58140fae27","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:24:16.223Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"