{"parentUuid":"29835157-053c-470d-a928-f7b90c1ba8e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxe2y4LKhNFKvb3eAimo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GCqM8YWAARTjbuGbZ3JvVM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Changeset for subdirectory workspace fixes","subagent_type":"courier:changeset-analyzer","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Produce ONE changeset file for orin-dx/callisto branch `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`. Diff (run from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6; do not cd elsewhere; `git fetch origin` first): `git diff origin/main...origin/fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`. List the unreleased `.changeset/` files on origin/main (`git ls-tree --name-only origin/main .changeset/`) and fold in only if the SAME outcome exists (the earlier subdirectory fix #511 is released: its entry is in crates/callisto-cli/CHANGELOG.md, do not edit released text). FACTS: when the callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repository (repo/ws), two more places compared repo-top-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones. (1) The interrupted-version guard (E121) went blind: after `callisto version` staged a bump and the working tree was then restored to HEAD (disk matches HEAD, index holds the bump), a second `version` ran with exit 0 and a misleading 'No pending changesets' warning instead of refusing with E121; it now refuses with E121 (exit 1), as it does when the workspace is at the repository root. (2) `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` in such a workspace failed with E165 'release-decision file was not written by this commit' because the commit's changed paths carried the `ws/` prefix; the commit check now compares workspace-relative paths (edits outside the workspace are still refused). That command still cannot succeed from a subdirectory workspace: `release` requires the git repository root to equal the workspace root (E170), which is by design, and it now reports E170 correctly instead of the misleading E165. Doc changes on this branch (mention the limit as a bullet only if it fits): README Limits and docs/releasing.md now say release needs the workspace at the repository root. Style: say what changed, why it matters, what to do (nothing, unless the user hit these); lead line, short bullets only where they add something, plain language, no AI slop, one line per paragraph. Front matter `callisto-cli: patch`. Return the ready-to-write file text with a kebab-case name, plus changeset@3 JSON. Do not write files."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":960448,"output_tokens":1354,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":402},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":709,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1354,"cache_read_input_tokens":960448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":709},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GCqM8YWAARTjbuGbZ3JvVM":{"description":"Changeset for subdirectory workspace fixes","subagent_type":"courier:changeset-analyzer","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Produce ONE changeset file for orin-dx/callisto branch `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`. Diff (run from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6; do not cd elsewhere; `git fetch origin` first): `git diff origin/main...origin/fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`. List the unreleased `.changeset/` files on origin/main (`git ls-tree --name-only origin/main .changeset/`) and fold in only if the SAME outcome exists (the earlier subdirectory fix #511 is released: its entry is in crates/callisto-cli/CHANGELOG.md, do not edit released text). FACTS: when the callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repository (repo/ws), two more places compared repo-top-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones. (1) The interrupted-version guard (E121) went blind: after `callisto version` staged a bump and the working tree was then restored to HEAD (disk matches HEAD, index holds the bump), a second `version` ran with exit 0 and a misleading 'No pending changesets' warning instead of refusing with E121; it now refuses with E121 (exit 1), as it does when the workspace is at the repository root. (2) `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` in such a workspace failed with E165 'release-decision file was not written by this commit' because the commit's changed paths carried the `ws/` prefix; the commit check now compares workspace-relative paths (edits outside the workspace are still refused). That command still cannot succeed from a subdirectory workspace: `release` requires the git repository root to equal the workspace root (E170), which is by design, and it now reports E170 correctly instead of the misleading E165. Doc changes on this branch (mention the limit as a bullet only if it fits): README Limits and docs/releasing.md now say release needs the workspace at the repository root. Style: say what changed, why it matters, what to do (nothing, unless the user hit these); lead line, short bullets only where they add something, plain language, no AI slop, one line per paragraph. Front matter `callisto-cli: patch`. Return the ready-to-write file text with a kebab-case name, plus changeset@3 JSON. Do not write files."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a280ece8-b671-4b3e-9049-b493b666a009","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgxe2xhGT4SgdkJJQCNfw","requestRef":"0703f14b-c41e-46e5-8066-e4