{"parentUuid":"3e8dd34d-9535-4d0f-a289-5e72748a6a0c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"51bf2e4a-aaab-45ba-a926-376f645f0712","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Artifact, Bash, Edit, EnterWorktree, Grep, ListAgents, Monitor, Read, SendFeedback, SendMessage, SubagentHandback, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Ongoing, open-ended: \"Keep going on our work please\", \"We don't need to stop\", \"Keep these going\". Continue improving Callisto (release PR/changelog quality, 1.0 stability, performance, docs, bug fixing) with agent teams at controlled cost.\n   - Specific recent requests:\n     - Verify review findings on specific PR changes (#136 on #528, #139 on #531).\n     - \"Does this have a merge conflict?\" (#531: no conflict; `MERGEABLE`, merge-tree clean; `BLOCKED` was the Entire approval gate).\n     - \"Should we update docs, readme, architecture? etc\", then \"Are you sure? ... I feel like the readme, etc are not keeping up\", then \"Do we tout all our features? GH releases, tagging, attestation? Language support?\", then \"Is that all we can add? Seems anemic for our users\".\n     - \"Anything we want to tackle before the next release?\", then \"Release PR is merged, let's work on the next set of work please\".\n     - \"I like your recommendation on e194\" (leave E194 alone).\n     - \"Are we overengineering again with sh and py scripts???\".\n     - \"Do we really need snapshots of the schemas??? WTF seems over-engineering again\" (closed #529).\n     - \"Let's cleanup what we can\".\n     - \"Our trails are now just PR wrappers...\".\n     - A Caliper finding (change #224: `Props<string>` loses `HTMLAttributes` in `crates/semantic/src/convert.rs`). It needs a session in the Caliper repo; the prompt was given. Not done.\n   - Standing directives (preserve): always sign commits (never `gpgsign=false`); one PR per independent topic off `origin/main`, no stacks; link branch to a feature trail BEFORE the PR; never put claude.ai session links or Claude-Session trailers in commits or PRs; judge checks by exit code; PR/commit text succinct, one line per paragraph; use courier agents for changesets and PR text; Entire auto-push is intended; never edit global CLAUDE.md without approval; no Claude hooks; lean over engineered.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `exit_kind()` per error type (`ExitKind::Usage`/`Runtime`, `_ => Runtime`); flag-caused errors exit 2, state/config errors exit 1 (docs/stability.md).\n   - Typed JSON envelope (`emit_report`, `Report` trait, `write_document` crate-private, `write_error_json`); `PACKAGE_REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION` = 3 (status/version/snapshot/matrix).\n   - git path semantics in subdirectory workspaces: `rev:./path` (`object_at`), `--relative`, `git rev-parse --show-prefix`, repo-top vs workspace-relative paths.\n   - `workspace_decision_path` + `canonicalize_through_missing` (E225 outside workspace, E226 invalid), shared by `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision`, `release pending --decision`; `--emit-preview` intentionally unconstrained (the action uses a temp file).\n   - `named_by == NamedBy::Inference` guard for the \"No pending changesets\" warning.\n   - Python PEP 508 `Requirement::parse` (one bracket pair, `parenthesized` flag, `@ url`).\n   - globset with `literal_separator(true)` for ignore patterns; unscoped `git diff --name-only` per tag commit mapped through `SpecIndex`.\n   - Entire trails: `entire trail create --no-branch`, `entire trail link <n> --repo gh/orin-dx/callisto --project gh/orin-dx --branch <b> --base main` (Entire then opens the PR; edit its title/body; keep the shadow-PR marker; `gh pr ready`).\n   - Supply chain facts verified: generated matrix workflow uses `actions/attest-build-provenance`; `release_artifacts.rs` compares SHA-256/size then `gh attestation verify` against a recorded repo/workflow policy; generated workflows set `NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE`.\n   - Release PR flow: generated `callisto/version-packages` branch; CI on it ends `action_required` (needs approval); Entire Gates is the trail approval gate; release requires git repo root == workspace root (E170 via `CanonicalRootMatchesWorkspace` in `release/capability.rs observe_git_trust`).\n   - Brain memories: `entire brain remember \"...\" --path <category.sub.type>` (valid paths like `preferences.coding.style`, `preferences.architecture.compatibility`).\n   - Michi (sibling repo: michi-core FSL, michi-pipeline async FSL, michi-graph MIT) offers nothing to swap into Callisto.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs`: `workspace_decision_path`, `canonicalize_through_missing` (#528 fix; extended in #535 to resolve relative paths, reject directory/root/trailing separator/`.git`, canonicalize through nearest existing ancestor).\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs`: guard `!agg.named_by.values().any(|n| *n == crate::aggregate::NamedBy::Inference)` (#531); subdirectory fixes pending in branch `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths` (`SourceChanges::since` `--relative`; `manifest_blob_in_index` `:./{path}`).\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release_decision.rs`: `commit_delta` in branch `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths` (show-prefix stripping, `../` rewrite for outside paths); `object_at(rev, path)` = `format!(\"{rev}:./{path}\")`.\n   - `crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs`: `Requirement::parse` rewritten (name ends at whitespace/`(`/`[`/`@`/`,`/operator; `;` marker split first; `parenthesized` flag; `@ url` spec) in #534.\n   - `crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`: real-binary tests for containment and validation (#528, #535).\n   - `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version/tests.rs`: tests `plan_version_inferred_bump_does_not_warn_no_pending_changesets`, `plan_version_nothing_to_release_warns_no_pending_changesets`, `plan_version_recorded_changeset_overriding_an_inferred_bump_still_warns_nothing_pending`.\n   - `README.md`: \"What you get\" (6 groups) and Limits list (8 bullets; line 118 `### Limits`, line 127 `- Windows is not supported`), merged in #532. Needs a new Limits bullet: release requires the workspace at the repository root.\n   - `docs/releasing.md` (sections: Local release: `callisto release` at line 9; Generated workflows 34; Release PR and approval 67; ...) and `docs/errors.md` row E170 (line 219: \"Release precondition is unmet (e.g. detached HEAD, missing GitHub remote)\"; Fix column must stay equal to the code's help text, so only the When column should change).\n   - `docs/stability.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` (invariants 8 and 9 added), `docs/adr/0011/0012/README.md`, `action.yml` (four inputs marked Internal).\n   - `.changeset/*`: `catch-bad-input-early.md` (bullet for `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` removal), `usage-errors-exit-2.md`, `lockfile-refresh-drop-success.md`, `contain-decision-paths.md`, `version-no-empty-warning-on-inferred-bump.md`, `python-parenthesized-requirements.md`, `validate-decision-target-before-apply.md`.\n   - Memory: `/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md` (updated twice with session lessons).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Subdirectory workspace regression siblings missed in #511: `git diff-tree`/`git diff` without `--relative` and bare `:{path}`. Found by the bug hunt; fixed in `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`.\n   - #528 regression: absolute decision path with missing parent failed; fixed with `canonicalize_through_missing` (test red before, green after, signed).\n   - #531 stale-inference guard flaw: replaced `inference_commits.is_empty()` with `named_by == Inference`.\n   - Schema goldens (#529) over-engineering: closed on user feedback; memory updated.\n   - Courier changeset suggested `major` semver in JSON; front matter kept `minor`/`patch` per repo convention.\n   - Agent slip: a repro script overwrote `Cargo.toml` and `callisto.toml` in a worktree because `mktemp` was sandbox-denied; the pre-commit hook blocked the commit and files were restored.\n   - Local `just test` failure `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` is environmental (`cargo info` CommandFailed without registry tools); same on main.\n   - Worktree guard rejections (compound git commands, loops with gh) led to single-command or script-file use; bash `sed -i` into `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs` was sandbox-denied, so Edit/Write were used.\n   - A guessed PR number in a trail body (#532) matched the real PR.\n   - `$/.github/actions/...` in workflow `uses:` lines: confirmed literal in git and GitHub (`24 2f 2e`); unexplained but works in production (GitHub logs show `orin-dx/callisto/.github/actions/...@sha`); left alone.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Release 0.20.0 published and verified.\n   - Docs now current: README feature list, architecture pages, `stability.md`, ADR 12, `--dry-run` clarified.\n   - Regression hunt findings: fixed or in progress (parenthesized PEP 508 #534, decision-target validation #535, subdirectory siblings). Findings deliberately not acted on: exit-code judgment calls (`compose-pr-body --preview` E281 rc 2, `release plan --package` nothing-pending E169 rc 1, `--cwd /nonexistent` E213 rc 1), `br{a}ce` member directory, `release pending --limit 0` message and `--emit-preview` relative-path wording (batch later).\n   - Decisions: E194 leave; OIDC pending the user (generated-workflow option vs config key; allow `id-token: write` on `execute`); `--dry-run` stays global; exit-2 rule applied; #526 merged as is; the first `v1` tag rehearsal is covered by existing `workflow-contracts` tests.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Ready for release? If not finish everything we need to tackle please\"\n   - \"No features, fixes, etc before the next release?\"\n   - \"Release PR is merged, let's work on the next set of work please\"\n   - \"Keep going on our work please\"\n   - \"We don't need to stop\"\n   - \"Keep these going\"\n   - \"I like your recommendation on e194\"\n   - \"Should we update docs, readme, architecture? etc\"\n   - \"Are you sure? We've made  A LOT of changes and I feel like the readme, etc are not keeping up\"\n   - \"Do we tout all our features? GH releases, tagging, attestation? Language support?\"\n   - \"Is that all we can add? Seems anemic for our users\"\n   - \"Does this have a merge conflict? - Confirmed: inference_commits is filled w\" (garbled; interpreted as #531)\n   - Pasted findings: change #139 on #531 (prerelease stale inference guard); change #136 on #528 (absolute path with missing parent); Caliper change #224 (`Props<string>` loses `HTMLAttributes`).\n   - \"Are we overengineering again with sh and py scripts???\"\n   - \"Do we really need snapshots of the schemas??? WTF seems over-engineering again\"\n   - \"Let's cleanup what we can\"\n   - \"Our trails are now just PR wrappers and we've lost the feature and semantic grouping meaning right?\"\n   - \"Can we update to latest branch?\" (read as updating the Caliper checkout; fetched refs only)\n   - \"Do we need to cleanup worktrees and branches?\" then \"cleanup please\"\n   - \"help me with a recommendation on the decisions pending\", then \"Let's follow your recommendations\"\n   - \"Why did this PR fail? https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/516\" (explained pin mismatch and Python proptest flake)\n   - \"What work do we tackle next?\", \"Let's do all of it\", \"What else should we honestly tackle before the release?\"\n   - \"Merged all of the previous PRs, what's next?\" and earlier \"Everything is merged...\" style messages; \"All merged\"; \"Release PR is merged...\"\n   - Earlier in this segment (from the prior summary): the over-engineering critique \"That is exactly what I'm thinking. Rust is structure for compiler checks, that's why the compile is slow...\", \"What kind of prompt and guidance would you give to another agent to look for similar patterns of issues?\", \"we should definitely look for bugs with bug-hunter\", \"Let's verify these and think big picture...\", \"Can we look at things like wait-timeout, duct, etc? are those things that should be in michi?\", \"Take a look at what we have in michi, latest version locally in ~/projects\", \"Updated local mich to latest main\".\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths` (worktree `agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a`, which I had just entered):\n     - add the release-needs-workspace-at-repo-root limit to `README.md` Limits (after the \"Windows is not supported\" bullet region), `docs/releasing.md`, and the E170 row's When column in `docs/errors.md` (do not change its Fix column);\n     - write the changeset (courier agent `a0c449a5fd2cd5ce8` was producing `callisto-cli: patch` text for the two fixes);\n     - commit signed, run `just doc-check`/`pre-push`/`lint`, push;\n     - link to trail #357;\n     - edit the Entire-opened PR title and body (template: Summary, Type of change, Changeset, Docs, Test Plan; shadow-PR marker; known failing test note; sweep table);\n     - `gh pr ready`;\n     - confirm signatures on GitHub.\n   - Then re-read release PR #533 (patch release containing #531, #534, #535 and the subdirectory-fix changesets); merge is the user's (needs CI approval and Entire Gates).\n   - Batch low-priority hunt items: `release pending --limit 0` message, `--emit-preview` cwd-relative wording vs `action.yml`.\n   - Clean up merged worktrees and branches: agent worktrees for #534 (`agent-a3253dad6be025c8c`), #535 (`agent-a60b96e3da64503b6`), the `fix/subdir...` worktree, `agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d` (cwd earlier, #531 merged), after their PRs merge.\n   - User-side decisions still open: OIDC trusted publishing (execute permission, generated-workflow shape; plan in `docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md`); Caliper change #224 fix needs a session in `~/Projects/caliper` on `feat/checker-supplies-facts`.\n   - PR #495 (older docs PR) remains open.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I was in worktree `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a` (branch `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`), about to make the documentation edits for the \"release needs the workspace at the repository root\" limit. I had just grepped and found: README `### Limits` at line 118 and `- Windows is not supported` at line 127; `docs/releasing.md` sections (Local release at line 9, Generated workflows at 34, etc.); `docs/errors.md` line 219 `| E170 | Release precondition is unmet (e.g. detached HEAD, missing GitHub remote) | Satisfy the reported precondition (for example a detached HEAD or a configured GitHub remote) before retrying. |`. The agent's two fixes on this branch (two signed commits, `just test` only fails the known environment test) were reviewed; the sweep found no other affected git calls.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Make those doc edits on `fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths`, then write the changeset from the courier agent's output, push, link to trail #357, and edit and ready the Entire-opened PR. This follows directly from my last message to the user: \"I'm adding that limit to the docs on this same branch (README Limits list, `releasing.md`, and the E170 row), and getting a changeset for the two fixes.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto--claude-worktrees-agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"abb1bfb6-b999-4857-8a14-6da20dcf187d","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.806Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":246,"turnIndex":351},"turnOrigin":"peer","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"abb1bfb6-b999-4857-8a14-6da20dcf187d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_decision_target.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_decision_target.md","content":"## Summary\n- `callisto version --emit-decision <path>` checked only the shape of the path (the helper added in #528) but wrote the file after the plan was applied. A path that resolved to a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root) bumped and staged manifests and deleted changesets, then failed with E213 \"Is a directory\" (exit 1), leaving the workspace half-versioned, and a rerun then failed with E121. A relative path through an in-workspace symlink to the outside wrote outside the workspace, while the absolute spelling was rejected.\n- `workspace_decision_path` in `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs` is now the one check shared by `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. It resolves relative paths against the workspace root, canonicalizes through the nearest existing ancestor (following symlinks), and rejects before anything changes: a path outside the root is E225; the root itself, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, and an unresolvable path such as `missing/..` are E226. All exit 2 with nothing written. No new error code.\n- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works, as does the release PR action's workspace-relative `--emit-decision \"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\"`.\n- One existing test, `partial_run_tests::decision_write_failure_leaves_staged_evidence...`, relied on a file-as-parent failing late, which is now rejected early. It now uses a read-only (0o555) directory and is unix-only.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: `docs/specs/release.json` and `docs/stability.md` already describe the decision path as workspace-relative.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [x] Real-binary tests in `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` for the directory and root, trailing-slash, `.git`, `missing/..` and symlink-escape spellings, each asserting exit 2, the error code, and that `Cargo.toml` and `.changeset` are untouched. Before the fix, three of the four reject tests failed; the fourth (a valid relative path under new directories) passes before and after as the guard.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_decision_target.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7ae3d4fc-73c6-4cb1-9c45-30db388ac781","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_decision_target.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t## Summary\n2\t- `callisto version --emit-decision <path>` checked only the shape of the path (the helper added in #528) but wrote the file after the plan was applied. A path that resolved to a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root) bumped and staged manifests and deleted changesets, then failed with E213 \"Is a directory\" (exit 1), leaving the workspace half-versioned, and a rerun then failed with E121. A relative path through an in-workspace symlink to the outside wrote outside the workspace, while the absolute spelling was rejected.\n3\t- `workspace_decision_path` in `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs` is now the one check shared by `version --emit-decision`, `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. It resolves relative paths against the workspace root, canonicalizes through the nearest existing ancestor (following symlinks), and rejects before anything changes: a path outside the root is E225; the root itself, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, and an unresolvable path such as `missing/..` are E226. All exit 2 with nothing written. No new error code.\n4\t- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works, as does the release PR action's workspace-relative `--emit-decision \"$INPUT_DECISION_PATH\"`.\n5\t- One existing test, `partial_run_tests::decision_write_failure_leaves_staged_evidence...`, relied on a file-as-parent failing late, which is now rejected early. It now uses a read-only (0o555) directory and is unix-only.\n6\t- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n7\t\n8\t## Type of change\n9\t- [x] Bug fix\n10\t\n11\t## Changeset\n12\t- [x] Added `.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md` (patch).\n13\t\n14\t## Docs\n15\t- [x] None apply: `docs/specs/release.json` and `docs/stability.md` already describe the decision path as workspace-relative.\n16\t\n17\t## Test Plan\n18\t- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n19\t- [x] Real-binary tests in `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` for the directory and root, trailing-slash, `.git`, `missing/..` and symlink-escape spellings, each asserting exit 2, the error code, and that `Cargo.toml` and `.changeset` are untouched. Before the fix, three of the four reject tests failed; the fourth (a valid relative path under new directories) passes before and after as the guard.\n20\t- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n21\t- [ ] Not run: CI\n22\t\n23\t<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n24\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"7ae3d4fc-73c6-4cb1-9c45-30db388ac781","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md","content":"## Summary\n- A Python dependency written in the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized form `name (==1.0.0)` was not recognized as a dependency, so bumping that dependency did not cascade to the dependent and its pin stayed old. `Requirement::parse` split the name at the first operator character, so the name became `core (`. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n- `Requirement::parse` now ends the name at whitespace, `(`, `[`, `@`, `,` or a comparison operator. `Requirement` gains a `parenthesized` flag carried through both rewrite sites, so a rewritten pin keeps the user's form (`name (==2.0.0)`).\n- `name[extra] @ https://...` is parsed with the URL kept out of the extras (before, the extras absorbed `] @ url`, which would have rendered a stray `]` on a rewrite). The `;` marker split still comes first. Text after the name that is not a clause is dropped.\n- No new dependency: `pep440_rs` only parses version specifiers, and no crate in `Cargo.lock` parses PEP 508 requirement strings, so the hand parser was extended.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary through an end-to-end test: before the fix `app` stayed at 0.1.0 with its pin unchanged; after it is patch-released to 0.1.1 and the pin is `lib-py (==0.2.0)`. A second end-to-end test covers the URL-with-extras case, and two unit tests cover the parser.\n- [x] The proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passes at 20,000 cases; it caught a `\"(\"` edge case, which is fixed and added to the regression seeds.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"69042f92-12f1-446b-95e0-1172fbaf8573","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_pep508.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t## Summary\n2\t- A Python dependency written in the legacy PEP 508 parenthesized form `name (==1.0.0)` was not recognized as a dependency, so bumping that dependency did not cascade to the dependent and its pin stayed old. `Requirement::parse` split the name at the first operator character, so the name became `core (`. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n3\t- `Requirement::parse` now ends the name at whitespace, `(`, `[`, `@`, `,` or a comparison operator. `Requirement` gains a `parenthesized` flag carried through both rewrite sites, so a rewritten pin keeps the user's form (`name (==2.0.0)`).\n4\t- `name[extra] @ https://...` is parsed with the URL kept out of the extras (before, the extras absorbed `] @ url`, which would have rendered a stray `]` on a rewrite). The `;` marker split still comes first. Text after the name that is not a clause is dropped.\n5\t- No new dependency: `pep440_rs` only parses version specifiers, and no crate in `Cargo.lock` parses PEP 508 requirement strings, so the hand parser was extended.\n6\t- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n7\t\n8\t## Type of change\n9\t- [x] Bug fix\n10\t\n11\t## Changeset\n12\t- [x] Added `.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md` (patch).\n13\t\n14\t## Docs\n15\t- [x] None apply.\n16\t\n17\t## Test Plan\n18\t- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n19\t- [x] Reproduced with the real binary through an end-to-end test: before the fix `app` stayed at 0.1.0 with its pin unchanged; after it is patch-released to 0.1.1 and the pin is `lib-py (==0.2.0)`. A second end-to-end test covers the URL-with-extras case, and two unit tests cover the parser.\n20\t- [x] The proptest `requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` passes at 20,000 cases; it caught a `\"(\"` edge case, which is fixed and added to the regression seeds.\n21\t- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n22\t- [ ] Not run: CI\n23\t\n24\t<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n25\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"69042f92-12f1-446b-95e0-1172fbaf8573","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6/.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6/.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\n`callisto version --emit-decision <path>` now rejects a bad path before it changes anything, instead of failing after the workspace is already half-versioned.\n\n- Before, only the shape of the path was checked up front, and the file was written at the end. A path that was a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root), had a trailing slash, or was inside `.git` failed late with `E213` (\"Is a directory\", exit 1). By then manifests were bumped and staged and changesets deleted, and a rerun failed with `E121`.\n- A relative path through an in-workspace symlink that points outside the workspace wrote the file outside the workspace.\n- Now one check runs first, and it also covers `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. All rejections exit 2 with nothing written:\n  - `E225`: the path resolves outside the workspace.\n  - `E226`: the workspace root, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, or a path that cannot be resolved.\n- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works.\n- If a script expected the late `E213` (exit 1) for these paths, expect `E225` or `E226` with exit 2 instead, and nothing is changed.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"displayPath":"../agent-a60b96e3da64503b6/.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9e827881-57c2-449c-b6c2-9b81206e3800","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60b96e3da64503b6/.changeset/validate-decision-target-before-apply.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tcallisto-cli: patch\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t`callisto version --emit-decision <path>` now rejects a bad path before it changes anything, instead of failing after the workspace is already half-versioned.\n6\t\n7\t- Before, only the shape of the path was checked up front, and the file was written at the end. A path that was a directory or the workspace root (`.changeset`, `.`, the root), had a trailing slash, or was inside `.git` failed late with `E213` (\"Is a directory\", exit 1). By then manifests were bumped and staged and changesets deleted, and a rerun failed with `E121`.\n8\t- A relative path through an in-workspace symlink that points outside the workspace wrote the file outside the workspace.\n9\t- Now one check runs first, and it also covers `release plan --decision` and `release pending --decision`. All rejections exit 2 with nothing written:\n10\t  - `E225`: the path resolves outside the workspace.\n11\t  - `E226`: the workspace root, an existing directory, a trailing separator, anything under `.git`, or a path that cannot be resolved.\n12\t- A new file under directories that do not exist yet still works.\n13\t- If a script expected the late `E213` (exit 1) for these paths, expect `E225` or `E226` with exit 2 instead, and nothing is changed.\n14\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9e827881-57c2-449c-b6c2-9b81206e3800","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3253dad6be025c8c/.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3253dad6be025c8c/.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\nPython dependencies written as `name (==1.0.0)` are now recognized, so bumping that dependency releases its dependents and updates the pin.\n\n- Before, the legacy parenthesized form was not seen as a dependency: the dependent was not released and its pin stayed old. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n- Now a bump of `name` to 2.0.0 patch-releases the dependent and rewrites the pin to `name (==2.0.0)`, keeping the parentheses.\n- A requirement like `name[extra] @ https://...` is now read with the URL kept out of the extras.\n- You do not need to do anything. If you had worked around this by rewriting pins to `name==1.0.0`, you can leave them.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}},"displayPath":"../agent-a3253dad6be025c8c/.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7c4b35c1-be59-4d4c-8acd-b798148527c4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3253dad6be025c8c/.changeset/python-parenthesized-requirements.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tcallisto-cli: patch\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\tPython dependencies written as `name (==1.0.0)` are now recognized, so bumping that dependency releases its dependents and updates the pin.\n6\t\n7\t- Before, the legacy parenthesized form was not seen as a dependency: the dependent was not released and its pin stayed old. The same pin written `name==1.0.0` already worked.\n8\t- Now a bump of `name` to 2.0.0 patch-releases the dependent and rewrites the pin to `name (==2.0.0)`, keeping the parentheses.\n9\t- A requirement like `name[extra] @ https://...` is now read with the URL kept out of the extras.\n10\t- You do not need to do anything. If you had worked around this by rewriting pins to `name==1.0.0`, you can leave them.\n11\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"7c4b35c1-be59-4d4c-8acd-b798148527c4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/wt_remove4.sh","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/wt_remove4.sh","content":"#!/bin/sh\n# Remove clean, fully pushed worktrees whose PR merged, then their local branches. Keep agent-acb69 (current directory).\nbase=/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees\ncd \"$base/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d\" || exit 2\nfor d in agent-a3331bef90d4c2276 agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889 agent-ae55a48dbafe514c8; do\n  p=\"$base/$d\"\n  [ -d \"$p\" ] || { echo \"$d missing\"; continue; }\n  br=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" branch --show-current)\n  dirty=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\n  if /usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" rev-parse -q --verify \"origin/$br\" >/dev/null; then\n    ahead=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" rev-list --count \"origin/$br..HEAD\")\n  else\n    ahead=remote-deleted\n  fi\n  echo \"$d $br dirty=$dirty ahead=$ahead\"\n  if [ \"$dirty\" = 0 ] && { [ \"$ahead\" = 0 ] || [ \"$ahead\" = remote-deleted ]; }; then\n    /usr/bin/git worktree unlock \"$p\" 2>/dev/null\n    /usr/bin/git worktree remove \"$p\" && echo \"  removed\" && { [ -n \"$br\" ] && /usr/bin/git branch -D \"$br\" 2>&1 | sed 's/^/  /'; }\n  else\n    echo \"  KEPT (not clean or has unpushed commits)\"\n  fi\ndone\necho \"--- local branches\"\n/usr/bin/git branch --format='%(refname:short)' | tr '\\n' ' '\necho\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/wt_remove4.sh"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b90a68ff-0ea0-4ada-9e3f-167b3be3916b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:24.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/wt_remove4.sh\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t#!/bin/sh\n2\t# Remove clean, fully pushed worktrees whose PR merged, then their local branches. Keep agent-acb69 (current directory).\n3\tbase=/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees\n4\tcd \"$base/agent-acb69fdff4fb3419d\" || exit 2\n5\tfor d in agent-a3331bef90d4c2276 agent-ac9ece27b6e55b889 agent-ae55a48dbafe514c8; do\n6\t  p=\"$base/$d\"\n7\t  [ -d \"$p\" ] || { echo \"$d missing\"; continue; }\n8\t  br=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" branch --show-current)\n9\t  dirty=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\n10\t  if /usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" rev-parse -q --verify \"origin/$br\" >/dev/null; then\n11\t    ahead=$(/usr/bin/git -C \"$p\" rev-list --count \"origin/$br..HEAD\")\n12\t  else\n13\t    ahead=remote-deleted\n14\t  fi\n15\t  echo \"$d $br dirty=$dirty ahead=$ahead\"\n16\t  if [ \"$dirty\" = 0 ] && { [ \"$ahead\" = 0 ] || [ \"$ahead\" = remote-deleted ]; }; then\n17\t    /usr/bin/git worktree unlock \"$p\" 2>/dev/null\n18\t    /usr/bin/git worktree remove \"$p\" && echo \"  removed\" && { [ -n \"$br\" ] && /usr/bin/git branch -D \"$br\" 2>&1 | sed 's/^/  /'; }\n19\t  else\n20\t    echo \"  KEPT (not clean or has unpushed commits)\"\n21\t  fi\n22\tdone\n23\techo \"--- local branches\"\n24\t/usr/bin/git branch --format='%(refname:short)' | tr '\\n' ' '\n25\techo\n26\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
