{"parentUuid":"13bcd4b3-2a0c-4cac-8281-b40f74d28c72","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxe8cDcw1gqJQXssFXvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3128,"cache_read_input_tokens":72370,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":72370,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3128},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":444,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"328b7236-4441-4840-9bca-209ca5edca87","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgxe8bhNtMwDWfsFTVF8A","requestRef":"fd8b1486-19bd-4d27-b41a-98a8ed5a047a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"327bffe1-e636-42de-b16b-720bd3ea60a1","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:30.203Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"327bffe1-e636-42de-b16b-720bd3ea60a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxe8cDcw1gqJQXssFXvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FPuU93VTqxc6ymKL1LwYUN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a/.changeset/subdir-workspace-interrupted-version-and-release-commit.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\nFixes two checks that misbehaved when the Callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repository (`repo/ws`). Both compared repository-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones.\n\n- `callisto version` now refuses to run again with E121 (exit 1) after an interrupted run. If a first `version` staged a bump and you then restored the working tree to HEAD, the second run used to exit 0 with a misleading \"No pending changesets\" warning. This matches the behavior when the workspace is at the repository root.\n- `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` no longer fails with E165 \"release-decision file was not written by this commit\" for a valid release commit. Edits outside the workspace are still refused.\n- That command still cannot succeed from a subdirectory workspace. `release` requires the repository root to be the workspace root (E170), and it now reports E170 instead of the misleading E165.\n- You do not need to do anything, unless you hit either problem. If you want to release, move the workspace to the repository root.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3128,"cache_read_input_tokens":72370,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":27},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":72370,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3128},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FPuU93VTqxc6ymKL1LwYUN":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a/.changeset/subdir-workspace-interrupted-version-and-release-commit.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\nFixes two checks that misbehaved when the Callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repository (`repo/ws`). Both compared repository-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones.\n\n- `callisto version` now refuses to run again with E121 (exit 1) after an interrupted run. If a first `version` staged a bump and you then restored the working tree to HEAD, the second run used to exit 0 with a misleading \"No pending changesets\" warning. This matches the behavior when the workspace is at the repository root.\n- `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` no longer fails with E165 \"release-decision file was not written by this commit\" for a valid release commit. Edits outside the workspace are still refused.\n- That command still cannot succeed from a subdirectory workspace. `release` requires the repository root to be the workspace root (E170), and it now reports E170 instead of the misleading E165.\n- You do not need to do anything, unless you hit either problem. If you want to release, move the workspace to the repository root.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"328b7236-4441-4840-9bca-209ca5edca87","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgxe8bhNtMwDWfsFTVF8A","requestRef":"fd8b1486-19bd-4d27-b41a-98a8ed5a047a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e63e7a86-c92b-40e0-b8ab-7b3a1d118779","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:29:32.269Z","advisorModel":"claude