{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"b7ad9a4e-4263-4bb7-a782-e27de4b71b93","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:30:27.627Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"061c200486ebc9b0312f567dd75bc581bc0a5e74fd96255fbb8887ebe6350a68","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"f77f8b31-7e0f-48b3-a0ab-19abf2db07b1","keep":23,"tail":["a464e3b2da9ad040eae11a55af459a2e463a22f90d33b34fffbd105fc90d4548","46cf00dc86ef4ac09fb4e74c124d700fc97b81cbdf84866091106ef04a985255","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",25,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f654a270bc1d465a443a6e038d410ca7f6616abf94549ced54503cf9085d0990"}
{"parentUuid":"4253657f-1e2e-4771-8111-2cb7b02171d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxeCv62WKm8ExQGmx8aG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SrKm6SpmpUDnr4u3pWLy6W","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_subdir.md","content":"## Summary\n- Two checks compared repository-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones, so they misbehaved when the workspace is a subdirectory of the repository (`repo/ws`). Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0, as siblings of the fix in #511.\n- `callisto version` after an interrupted run: the staged-manifest check used a bare `:{path}` and the source diff lacked `--relative`, so a restored working tree gave exit 0 and a misleading \"No pending changesets\" warning. It now refuses with E121 as it does at the repository root.\n- `callisto release plan --from-release-commit`: the commit delta kept repository-relative paths, so a valid release commit failed with E165. Paths are now mapped to the workspace, and edits outside it are still refused.\n- `release` still requires the repository root to be the workspace root (E170). That limit is now in the README Limits list, `docs/releasing.md` and the E170 row of `docs/errors.md`.\n- A sweep of the other git calls found no further affected sites.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/subdir-workspace-interrupted-version-and-release-commit.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] README Limits, `docs/releasing.md` and `docs/errors.md` (E170 When column).\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just doc-check` and `just lint` exit 0\n- [x] Real-binary tests for both fixes in a `repo/ws` layout, red before and green after.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":78972,"output_tokens":736,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":78972,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":218},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SrKm6SpmpUDnr4u3pWLy6W":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_subdir.md","content":"## Summary\n- Two checks compared repository-relative git paths with workspace-relative ones, so they misbehaved when the workspace is a subdirectory of the repository (`repo/ws`). Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0, as siblings of the fix in #511.\n- `callisto version` after an interrupted run: the staged-manifest check used a bare `:{path}` and the source diff lacked `--relative`, so a restored working tree gave exit 0 and a misleading \"No pending changesets\" warning. It now refuses with E121 as it does at the repository root.\n- `callisto release plan --from-release-commit`: the commit delta kept repository-relative paths, so a valid release commit failed with E165. Paths are now mapped to the workspace, and edits outside it are still refused.\n- `release` still requires the repository root to be the workspace root (E170). That limit is now in the README Limits list, `docs/releasing.md` and the E170 row of `docs/errors.md`.\n- A sweep of the other git calls found no further affected sites.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/subdir-workspace-interrupted-version-and-release-commit.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] README Limits, `docs/releasing.md` and `docs/errors.md` (E170 When column).\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just doc-check` and `just lint` exit 0\n- [x] Real-binary tests for both fixes in a `repo/ws` layout, red before and green after.\n- [ ] `just test` exits 100 in the agent's sandbox on one test, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4425cc92-fa8d-4c6e-8702-91025984b811","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxeCuqPtAWg8d6izBCc9","requestRef":"b7ad9a4e-4263-4bb7-a782-e27de4b71b93","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6184a9c1-271c-47a6-a7e9-b41a72d37ed4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:30:32.377Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-af481f5a6fc7e809a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-workspace-git-paths","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
