{"parentUuid":"00ebf7e4-d6b9-49d6-bfa8-98e31c323ac0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyU32srvppTau6Cf5dR3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Release PR #533 is the next step, and it's waiting on you. It now includes #531, #534, #535 and #536. Its only check is \"Entire Gates\", which shows `fail`. That is the approval gate, not a code failure. CI on that branch also needs approval before it runs. Approve in Entire (trail 375), then approve CI and merge.\n\nAfter that:\n\n1. **Worktree cleanup.** The #531, #534, #535 and #536 worktrees and branches are merged and can go. I'll run the removal script on your word.\n2. **OIDC trusted publishing.** This is the main open design item. It needs your choice between a generated-workflow option and a config key, and whether to allow `id-token: write` on `execute`. The plan is in `docs/projects/OIDC-TRUSTED-PUBLISHING.md`.\n3. **Small batch.** Two low-priority hunt items are left: the `release pending --limit 0` message and the `--emit-preview` relative-path wording against `action.yml`. Both would be one small PR.\n4. **Caliper change #224.** The `Props<string>` loses `HTMLAttributes` finding needs a session in `~/Projects/caliper`. That is outside this repo.\n5. **Docs PR #495.** It is still an open draft, and I can review whether it is stale.\n\nMy suggestion is to merge the release, let me clean up the worktrees, then decide on OIDC. The small batch can follow."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":82354,"output_tokens":470,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":313,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":470,"