{"parentUuid":"36dfe202-f67d-4fd9-ba0f-7a79b6ea9981","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyUZ99V3gcFwDZ3s8MJW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Worktrees and branches are cleaned up, and PR #537 is open and ready for review.\n\n**Cleanup**\n- I removed the four merged agent worktrees and their `fix/*` branches, plus the four stub `worktree-agent-*` branches. Everything was clean and fully pushed first.\n- The `callisto-fixtures` worktrees (`clean-cleanup`, `wt-cleanup-1` to `-3`) and their `chore/callisto-*` branches are untouched, since they weren't part of this work.\n\n**Small batch**\n- **`--limit 0` fix:** `callisto release pending --limit 0` is now a usage error with exit 2. Before, it silently reported nothing pending. PR #537 is linked to trail #357. The commit shows `valid` on GitHub, and a patch changeset is included.\n- **Checks:** `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. I did not run the full `just test`, and CI hasn't run yet.\n- **Dropped item:** the `--emit-preview` wording item turned out to be a non-issue. The flag's help text already says \"A relative path is relative to `--cwd`\", which is correct, so there was nothing to change.\n\nCaliper is dropped.\n\nThe release PR #533 is still waiting on your approval in Entire (trail 375) and CI. Merging #537 afterwards will queue a follow-up patch release.\n\nresult: Merged worktrees and branches are cleaned up, and PR #537 (reject `release pending --limit 0` with exit 2) is open, signed and ready for review; the `--emit-preview` item was dropped because its wording is already correct."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":99981,"output_tokens":551,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":