{"parentUuid":"c7fece4d-f151-45bf-b403-55a6a8f95205","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzBS8Su8gxLyP7h2DDMt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B9bRNPfauUA9gqAFjqiUQj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_cl.md","content":"## Summary\n- A changelog's \"Dependency updates\" for a cascaded package was built from one recorded reason, so it listed only the first dependency that raised the bump. With two bumped dependencies the second was missing, and a package that also had its own changeset got no dependency line even though its pins were rewritten (`docs/specs/versioning.json` says cascaded bumps appear under \"Dependency updates\").\n- The recorded dependency version could also be stale: with a fixed group, the line said `b → 1.0.1` while the manifest pin said `=1.1.0`.\n- The cascade now records, per consumer, every bumped dependency it was updated for (`CascadeOutcome::dependency_updates`). The changelog writes one entry per dependency, at the version the dependency finally reached (`outcome.targets`). The single-reason `Cascade` mapping is removed, so nothing is listed twice.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/changelog-lists-every-dependency-update.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `a` depends on `b` and `c` (exact pins); changeset `b: minor, c: patch` listed only `b`, and `a: patch, b: minor` listed no dependency line. After the fix both list every dependency. A plan-level test covers the two-dependency case.\n- [ ] `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli` has one failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":158215,"output_tokens":918,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":158215,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B9bRNPfauUA9gqAFjqiUQj":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_cl.md","content":"## Summary\n- A changelog's \"Dependency updates\" for a cascaded package was built from one recorded reason, so it listed only the first dependency that raised the bump. With two bumped dependencies the second was missing, and a package that also had its own changeset got no dependency line even though its pins were rewritten (`docs/specs/versioning.json` says cascaded bumps appear under \"Dependency updates\").\n- The recorded dependency version could also be stale: with a fixed group, the line said `b → 1.0.1` while the manifest pin said `=1.1.0`.\n- The cascade now records, per consumer, every bumped dependency it was updated for (`CascadeOutcome::dependency_updates`). The changelog writes one entry per dependency, at the version the dependency finally reached (`outcome.targets`). The single-reason `Cascade` mapping is removed, so nothing is listed twice.\n- Found by a regression hunt after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/changelog-lists-every-dependency-update.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `a` depends on `b` and `c` (exact pins); changeset `b: minor, c: patch` listed only `b`, and `a: patch, b: minor` listed no dependency line. After the fix both list every dependency. A plan-level test covers the two-dependency case.\n- [ ] `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli` has one failure, `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which needs the registry test tools CI installs and fails the same way on `main`. Everything else passed.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e5f2945d-0b30-4607-8d80-a941c2d24e69","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgzBS8D18PXQNiiv633Yj","requestRef":"8830e515-e517-48a1-a19d-976913aa19c4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e1fff5d-9347-4b51-8ddf-c3bb04144d45","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:00:38.855Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/small-batch-limit-and-preview","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/changelog-dependency-updates","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
