{"parentUuid":"17e4b63f-1bdc-4562-a0dc-e67623b2e795","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzLRs8TMPqQbPbBULSyY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VzB7DQEU45jdoXLxzRZEPk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit.md","content":"## Summary\n- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`. Rust 1.100 marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code now fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` (and the test builds). Every open PR failed Clippy, coverage and the test suites for this reason.\n- Each of those calls is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`, so the tests check the code instead of dropping it. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.\n- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Chore (CI)\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None apply: test-only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0 on the default toolchain\n- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli` has no failures, so every call returns success\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":179908,"output_tokens":701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":179908,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":358},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VzB7DQEU45jdoXLxzRZEPk":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit.md","content":"## Summary\n- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`. Rust 1.100 marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code now fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` (and the test builds). Every open PR failed Clippy, coverage and the test suites for this reason.\n- Each of those calls is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`, so the tests check the code instead of dropping it. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.\n- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Chore (CI)\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None apply: test-only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0 on the default toolchain\n- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli` has no failures, so every call returns success\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cffd5785-72b9-4f94-9b6a-c233674d8241","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgzLRrobkpTTFpsN2bH48","requestRef":"cde5f949-a4ee-4e8d-a5ba-1196b29ce851","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d6bb5a18-108d-4bc3-b567-240a3383d96e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T04:58:35.857Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gab