{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":11704,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"bdc899ad-dd71-4849-8483-f62a20b01e77","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzLT5U8nzwqCT1bYSAPk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #540 fixes the CI failures and is ready for review. It's the only open PR that goes red for this reason, but the others stay blocked until it merges.\n\nCI uses `channel = \"stable\"`, so it moved to Rust 1.100. That version marks `ExitCode` as `#[must_use]`. As a result, 91 test calls that dropped a command's exit code now fail clippy and the test builds. This failed Clippy, coverage and the test suites on #538, and it will fail every PR on a fresh run. #538's ubuntu test suite shows the same compile error, and I assume the macOS test and preflight failures share it. I didn't read their logs.\n\n- **The fix:** each of those calls is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), ExitCode::SUCCESS)`. It's test code only, so there's no behaviour change and no changeset. The repo's lints reject `let _ =` on must-use values, so I assert the code instead.\n- **Verification:** I installed 1.100.0 as a side toolchain, and your default is unchanged. `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` was clean, where it reported 91 errors before. `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0, and `cargo test -p callisto-cli` shows no failures. The only failure in the wider run is the known `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` test. The commit is signed, and the PR is linked to trail #357.\n- **Not yet run:** CI and `just workflow-contracts`.\n\n**Branch sync:** #537, #538 and #539 are each one commit on top of `main` and don't conflict with each other. I haven't rebased them. Once you merge #540, I'll merge `main` into each, which avoids rewriting signed commits. Their CI will rerun after that. Release PR #533 regenerates on its own once #540 merges.\n\nEntire Gates still shows `fail` on all four PRs. The 15 to 23 minute durations suggest those results came from before your fix, so they may need a rerun.\n\nresult: PR #540 fixes the CI breakage (Rust 1.100 made `ExitCode` must-use; 91 test calls now assert success) and is signed, checked locally on 1.100.0 and ready for review; #537, #538 and #539 get synced with `main` once it merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":181156,"output_tokens":792,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":181156,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f4cb44f5-cc89-4a88-9ef7-de32702fa18f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgzLT5Dk2XYW8cgGsNTYz","requestRef":"b37ce84c-ab39-48ea-a25d-bd60679a415f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b232b942-7ff2-4516-a3d2-bf45673544d2","timestamp":"2026-11-13T04:58:54.449Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/small-batch-limit-and-preview","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/ci-unused-exitcode","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
