{"parentUuid":"ab9150c1-72ef-44b6-b40e-93148719d20f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"84b075a1-0564-423a-86f1-0c369759409e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7Gaq8LFsyG6f3spQr9zV1","type":"tool_result","content":"Manage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add          Create a finding on a trail\n  apply        Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  delete-reply Delete your reply to a finding\n  dismiss      Dismiss a finding\n  edit-reply   Edit your reply to a finding\n  list         List findings for a trail\n  reopen       Reopen a finding\n  reply        Reply to a finding\n  resolve      Resolve a finding\n  show         Show a finding\n  update       Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string                    Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string                    Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string                 Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed[=true|false]   Include dismissed findings\n      --json[=true|false]                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int                        Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string                  Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string                    Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string                     Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"59060717-35e5-4e1b-a277-d4a607262e53","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:37:20.261Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Manage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add          Create a finding on a trail\n  apply        Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  delete-reply Delete your reply to a finding\n  dismiss      Dismiss a finding\n  edit-reply   Edit your reply to a finding\n  list         List findings for a trail\n  reopen       Reopen a finding\n  reply        Reply to a finding\n  resolve      Resolve a finding\n  show         Show a finding\n  update       Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string                    Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string                    Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string                 Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed[=true|false]   Include dismissed findings\n      --json[=true|false]                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int                        Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string                  Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string                    Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string                     Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"546c22aa-b413-4806-b440-c6e608abd567","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/small-batch-limit-and-preview","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/small-batch-limit-and-preview","branch":"fix/ci-unused-exitcode","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","ho