{"parentUuid":"beb24075-f197-4619-b245-f7b930246048","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzWGqZcQKjJm8waTdz5S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015cWJPDMfdToRG28jBcund8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit.md","content":"## Summary\n- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`, which is now Rust 1.100. It marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` and the test builds. Each is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.\n- The same toolchain moved `callisto-manifests` line coverage to 89.71%, under the 90% per-crate floor, with no change to that crate. Added three tests for code that had none: Flit version read and write, the bare-`[project]` write fallback, and an invalid PEP 440 version. That is 15 more covered lines.\n- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset. Every open PR fails on these two checks until this merges.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Chore (CI)\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None apply: test-only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 llvm-cov` reproduced CI's 2249 covered lines in `callisto-manifests`; with the new tests it is 2264\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0 on the default toolchain\n- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli -p callisto-graph` has only the known registry-tools failure `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which CI's Test Suite job covers\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":215666,"output_tokens":924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":57},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":336,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":215666,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":336},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015cWJPDMfdToRG28jBcund8":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exit.md","content":"## Summary\n- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`, which is now Rust 1.100. It marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` and the test builds. Each is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.\n- The same toolchain moved `callisto-manifests` line coverage to 89.71%, under the 90% per-crate floor, with no change to that crate. Added three tests for code that had none: Flit version read and write, the bare-`[project]` write fallback, and an invalid PEP 440 version. That is 15 more covered lines.\n- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset. Every open PR fails on these two checks until this merges.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Chore (CI)\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None apply: test-only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 llvm-cov` reproduced CI's 2249 covered lines in 