he_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which CI's Test Suite job covers\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Summary","-- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`. Rust 1.100 marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code now fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` (and the test builds). Every open PR failed Clippy, coverage and the test suites for this reason.","-- Each of those calls is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`, so the tests check the code instead of dropping it. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.","-- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset.","+- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`, which is now Rust 1.100. It marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` and the test builds. Each is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.","+- The same toolchain moved `callisto-manifests` line coverage to 89.71%, under the 90% per-crate floor, with no change to that crate. Added three tests for code that had none: Flit version read and write, the bare-`[project]` write fallback, and an invalid PEP 440 version. That is 15 more covered lines.","+- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset. Every open PR fails on these two checks until this merges."," "," ## Type of change"," - [x] Chore (CI)"]},{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":8,"newStart":14,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," ## Test Plan"," - [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)","+- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 llvm-cov` reproduced CI's 2249 covered lines in `callisto-manifests`; with the new tests it is 2264"," - [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0 on the default toolchain","-- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli` has no failures, so every call returns success","+- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli -p callisto-graph` has only the known registry-tools failure `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim`, which CI's Test Suite job covers"," - [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI"," "," <!-- entire-shadow-pr -->"]}],"originalFile":"## Summary\n- CI builds with `channel = \"stable\"`. Rust 1.100 marks `std::process::ExitCode` `#[must_use]`, so 91 test calls that discarded a command handler's exit code now fail `cargo clippy -D warnings` (and the test builds). Every open PR failed Clippy, coverage and the test suites for this reason.\n- Each of those calls is now `assert_eq!(<call>.unwrap(), std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS)`, so the tests check the code instead of dropping it. `let _ =` is not used because the repo's lints reject non-binding `let` on must-use values.\n- Test code only; no behaviour change and no changeset.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Chore (CI)\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None apply: test-only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` reports no errors (it reported 91 before)\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint` and `just doc-check` exit 0 on the default toolchain\n- [x] `cargo test -p callisto-cli` has no failures, so every call returns success\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f53bde7b-e134-4df0-8f19-ff411efacc88","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/small-batch-limit-and-prev