{"parentUuid":"d0950ff6-fe50-4661-b415-476080a7c7ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21D5Zz1TondW4MUKVTg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_read_input_tokens":228371,"output_tokens":1249,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":228371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3569,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"75695bfd-d14d-4036-a696-113da39fb1e3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21D5LbtJTDfxG5HchFi","requestRef":"089fe549-3294-4aa5-9ff6-a676bc3b96ff","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1b185ed-cf99-4781-a1c9-e930dc6e4a42","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:07:44.135Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"e1b185ed-cf99-4781-a1c9-e930dc6e4a42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21D5Zz1TondW4MUKVTg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, sharding by crate would miss them. Per-shard agents are good at local defects but blind to anything that lives between shards. The real bugs we've found recently were mostly of that kind:\n\n- Subdirectory paths were handled differently in `version`, `release_decision` and `release`.\n- Fixed groups interacted with pre mode.\n- The changelog read cascade state that a later group pass had changed.\n\nThe fix is a second pass organised by flow and invariant rather than by crate:\n\n1. **Shard pass.** The six local shards, as proposed. Each agent also writes \"boundary notes\": assumptions it relies on from another shard that it could not verify. Those become the second pass's starting leads.\n2. **Cross-cutting pass.** Four agents, each owning one flow or invariant set across all crates:\n   - **Plan to publish:** `version` plan, apply, persist, decision file, `release pending`, then release execution. They check that state written by one step is read correctly by the next, including after a partial failure or a rerun.\n   - **Manifest and cascade:** the rewrites the cascade plans against what the manifest writers actually do for each ecosystem, grammar and spec form, and the resulting changelog.\n   - **Config and generated workflows:** config keys, `action.yml` and generated workflow behaviour, against what the code enforces.\n   - **Semantic model and spec drift:** `ARCHITECTURE.md` invariants, `docs/architecture/`, `docs/specs/*.json`, `docs/stability.md` and the error table. Each documented claim is checked against code, and the reverse. This is where \"broken invariant\" gets tested, and it's the pass that covers the semantic models.\n3. **My verification.** I reproduce each finding before fixing anything. I also check the claims that cite a guard or caller, since those are the ones agents most often get wrong.\n\nEntire Brain's graph tools (`entire brain inspect impact` and `trace-path`) give the cross-cutting agents the call graph across crates, so they don't have to rediscover it by grepping. I'd tell them to use it.\n\nThe limits: agents can still miss a cross-flow defect that needs a specific state combination, and nothing here executes code, so races and ordering bugs get found only when they're visible in the source. Running selected scenarios against the real binary afterwards (pre mode with groups, subdirectory workspaces, partial failures) is the best backstop. I'd do that as a third stage for whatever the first two surface.\n\nThe cost is about ten agents in two waves. Want me to run it that way, or run the cross-cutting pass first? The cross-cutting pass has more value per agent for this codebase."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_read_input_tokens":228371,"output_tokens":1249,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":228371,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"75695bfd-d14d-4036-a696-113da39fb1e3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21D5LbtJTDfxG5HchFi","requestRef":"089fe549-3294-4aa5-9ff6-a676bc3b96ff","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f3de793-9bba-463a-b288-da23226963be","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:07:51.328Z","advisorModel":"cl