{"parentUuid":"b4204d9f-6237-4392-b5df-d5d24943311d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21FpELbvxSmUxg1uWFX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_read_input_tokens":229699,"output_tokens":1148,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":229699,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":889,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"eff5a748-91f6-4200-9c7e-87e44bb93de4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21FozTKZK3XBaH3YYBY","requestRef":"bdaa88f0-9dc5-4510-b11b-54cb0a575a73","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7a41c87-8de0-4d2a-8c18-67fd26b2b6e7","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:08:18.615Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"f7a41c87-8de0-4d2a-8c18-67fd26b2b6e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21FpELbvxSmUxg1uWFX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Some of the prompt needs to change for this use, and some of what we've learned from the hunts belongs in it.\n\n**Changes for whole-codebase and cross-flow review**\n- **Remove the diff clauses.** Delete \"this Change introduced it\", the diff base and the Trail-description exemption. Replace them with \"a defect in current code that you can trigger\".\n- **Give each agent a charter, not a file list.** Shards get a subsystem. Cross-cutting agents get a flow or an invariant, for example \"state written by step N must be read correctly by step N+1, including after a partial failure or a rerun\".\n- **Require boundary notes.** Each agent lists assumptions it relies on from outside its scope and could not verify. These feed the second pass.\n- **Seed with invariants.** Point agents at `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/architecture/`, `docs/specs/*.json` and `docs/stability.md`. For each documented invariant they ask \"what in the code could violate this?\" instead of reading code and hoping to notice.\n- **Add a spec-versus-code step.** Check every documented claim against code and every code behaviour against the docs, in both directions. The changelog bug was found that way (`versioning.json` said one thing and the code did another).\n\n**What we've learned about agent reviews**\n- **Agents report \"confirmed\" without proof.** I have to reproduce each one. So the prompt asks for a runnable repro: commands, observed versus expected, `file:line`. A finding without one is labelled \"plausible\". That matches the 0.5 to 0.9 confidence bands.\n- **Tests can encode the bug.** The pre-mode fix had to change an existing test that asserted the downgrade. Tell agents that a test asserting the behaviour is not evidence it's intended, and to check git history and recorded decisions (`entire brain recall`) for intent before dismissing.\n- **Don't report settled decisions.** Our memory records choices that look like bugs but aren't: the emoji in the release PR body, E194, exit-code judgment calls, Entire auto-push. Put a short \"settled, do not flag\" list in the prompt.\n- **Hunt by defect class.** Our best finds came from classes: fixpoint staleness, silent fallback, sibling call sites of an earlier fix, and path-base mismatches. List those classes. For any fix pattern, require \"search for siblings\" as a step. That is how the subdirectory regression was caught.\n- **Cap the output.** Ask for at most 8 findings per agent, ranked. Unbounded reports fill with low-value items.\n- **Keep them off tests and builds.** You already state this, and it's right. They can't reproduce, so the repro step is mine, which is why the prompt should make that handoff explicit.\n- **Rerun on fixes.** \"Fixed only when the code at its location changed\" is a good rule. I'd add \"and a regression test names the case\".\n\n**What stays as is**\nThe disprove-before-reporting step, the severity and confidence bands, the one-finding-per-defect rule, and \"don't report style, missing tests or anything CI enforces\".\n\nI can write the adapted shard prompt and the cross-cutting prompt as two short templates, and you can review them before anything runs. Want that?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_read_input_tokens":229699,"output_tokens":1148,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":229699,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"eff5a748-91f6-4200-9c7e-87e44bb93de4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21FozTKZK3XBaH3YYBY","requestRef":"bdaa88f0-9dc5-4510-b11b-54cb0a575a73","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aef3afc7-9062-4d0e-b5df-9d91abb3f57a","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:08:27.769Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
