{"parentUuid":"0e6c0192-11e3-4abd-b3b0-c07520397399","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21LZ3RWDDzVtQ5mJDvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":231052,"output_tokens":1180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":215},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":231052,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2049,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"38f883df-b403-4c16-8f75-032000578e50","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21LY9LtvGvoJYQe35MP","requestRef":"e791caeb-d4d0-4060-9718-2cc3460ab22b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2bb458c1-011f-4245-9b3b-8f17620c069f","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:09:24.083Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"2bb458c1-011f-4245-9b3b-8f17620c069f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21LZ3RWDDzVtQ5mJDvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ten-agent plan I proposed is a human org chart, and the process around it is the same. Shards are teams, boundary notes are handoff documents, phases are stage gates, and the prompt templates are procedures. That structure exists for humans because people have limited memory and can't see the whole system at once, so work is split and then coordinated. Models are in a different position, and imposing that structure costs tokens and loses information at every handoff.\n\n**What models are good at, and what I should use**\n- **Holding a lot in context.** One agent with the whole flow can see a cross-crate interaction directly. A shard agent can only guess at it and write a note. Splitting by crate creates the cross-shard blind spot I then proposed a second pass to patch.\n- **Running things.** The best results in this session came from executing: the real binary, a repro, a compiler. The bug hunt found the pre-mode downgrade, and I confirmed it in four commands. Reading code and arguing about it found far less.\n- **Following a goal.** \"Find ways the release flow loses or corrupts state, and prove each with the binary\" gets a model to pick its own route. It doesn't need a charter, a ledger or a boundary-notes format.\n\n**Where I added process that wasn't needed**\n- Per-finding templates, confidence bands and report formats, when what I need is a repro I can run.\n- Multi-wave agent pipelines, where one or two agents with a clear goal and permission to execute would do.\n- Scripts for things a single command does, a habit I explained earlier. Most of the scripts were a workaround for the worktree guard, not a need of the work.\n- Heavy PR and trail ceremony per small fix. Some of it is yours (trails, signed commits), and I follow it. But I also added steps: courier agents for text I could write directly, and long PR bodies for one-line fixes.\n\n**What I'd do instead**\n1. Give one to three agents a goal and the invariants, and let them explore. For example: \"Break the plan-to-publish flow. Try partial failures, reruns, subdirectory workspaces, pre mode with groups. Prove each defect with the real binary or a failing test.\"\n2. Let them execute freely in a scratch directory. The earlier read-only restriction came from caution, and it makes agents less capable, because proof is the most useful thing they can produce.\n3. Have them return only reproduced defects. Unproven suspicion is noise, so don't ask for it.\n4. Fix and verify in the same loop, with a regression test, then move on.\n\nI'd keep the parts that carry real meaning: signed commits, the one-PR-per-topic rule, running the repo's own checks, and reproducing before fixing. Those protect the repo. The rest was me following a process pattern out of habit.\n\nMy suggestion is to run two agents, one on plan-to-publish and one on manifest rewrites plus cascade plus changelog. Both get the goal, the invariants and permission to run the binary, and both report only what they've reproduced. Want that?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":231052,"output_tokens":1180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":215},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":231052,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"38f883df-b403-4c16-8f75-032000578e50","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21LY9LtvGvoJYQe35MP","requestRef":"e791caeb-d4d0-4060-9718-2cc3460ab22b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cec361b7-b908-411d-9231-82edd30c6c11","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:09:33.219Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
