{"parentUuid":"a8d933de-7415-4b1f-85b8-23a2ac0ae188","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21R94AvbhCKF1y7eRLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91,"cache_read_input_tokens":232320,"output_tokens":1312,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":232320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1052,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"acce4c84-eb40-46bf-b51a-4d6502386731","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21R8VC12bmBiwKNYwb2","requestRef":"36f3274f-673e-45aa-b8f6-52dbda6624b9","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"26a96a28-4843-4b65-88f5-bb8a27e8335c","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:10:25.637Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"26a96a28-4843-4b65-88f5-bb8a27e8335c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21R94AvbhCKF1y7eRLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the prompt say what to achieve and what counts as proof, and have the agent discover everything about the repo itself. Nothing in it should name a language, crate or tool.\n\n**The principles**\n1. **Goal first, method never.** State the outcome, \"find defects that are real and can be shown\", and leave out the steps. The model chooses how to explore.\n2. **Discovery replaces configuration.** The agent should find the repo's rules, build and test commands, and documented invariants itself. It reads `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README`, CI config and the task runner file, and the docs that describe behaviour. No per-repo prompt edits are needed.\n3. **Proof is the product.** A defect only counts when the agent has shown it with the repo's own tooling: a failing test, a command with observed and expected output, or a compile error. Anything it can't demonstrate is dropped or labelled \"unproven\". This is the one rule that works in any language.\n4. **Scope by risk, not by directory.** Tell the agent to start from where damage is largest: state changes, data written, parsing of external input, permission boundaries, cross-module contracts. It decides where that is in each repo.\n5. **A small output contract.** Only what the reader needs: where it is, how to reproduce it, observed versus expected, and impact. No severity ladder and no confidence scores.\n6. **Hard safety bounds, short.** Work in a scratch copy or worktree, don't touch real secrets or remotes, don't change tracked files unless asked.\n\n**A skeleton**\n```\nFind real defects in this repository and prove each one.\n\nOrient first. Read the repo's own rules and docs (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README,\nCI and task-runner config) and learn how to build, test and run it. Work out\nwhat the system promises: documented behaviour, invariants, error contracts.\n\nThen hunt where being wrong costs most: places that change or persist state,\nparse outside input, cross a module or process boundary, or handle failure\nhalfway through. Compare what the docs promise with what the code does, and\nlook for sibling code that shares a flaw you find.\n\nProve every defect using the repo's own tooling or by running the program:\na failing test, or exact commands with observed versus expected output.\nDrop anything you can't demonstrate. Check git history and recorded\ndecisions before calling surprising behaviour a bug. A test that asserts\na behaviour does not make it intended.\n\nWork in a scratch copy. Don't edit tracked files, push, or touch secrets.\n\nReport only proven defects, ranked by impact: where it is, the repro,\nobserved versus expected, and the consequence.\n```\n\n**What changes per repo**\nNothing in the prompt. Per-repo knowledge lives in the repo's own docs and in a short \"settled decisions\" file, if one exists, which the agent reads as part of orientation. For us, that is where the emoji in release PR bodies and the E194 decision would go. That keeps the prompt portable and the repo-specific facts where the repo keeps them.\n\n**Limits**\n- Repos without runnable tests or a documented build get weaker proof, so the agent will report less. That's correct, not a prompt problem.\n- A model can still miss defects that need unusual states. Running more agents doesn't fix that, but adding a \"think about partial failure and reruns\" line costs nothing and has helped here.\n- Big repos need a focus hint from you, such as \"the release flow\". Without one the agent spreads thin. One sentence does it, so the prompt takes the target as an input.\n\nFor our own use, I'd drop the skeleton in as the base and add only the focus line per run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91,"cache_read_input_tokens":232320,"output_tokens":1312,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":232320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"acce4c84-eb40-46bf-b51a-4d6502386731","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21R8VC12bmBiwKNYwb2","requestRef":"36f3274f-673e-45aa-b8f6-52dbda6624b9","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d0893a3-df13-411f-a2f1-00574d98cccc","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:10:36.498Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
