{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":11704,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"4fa6a648-58a1-453b-9515-02b321e44297","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21Xv1nwLK8upSUp3unX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right, that version still told the agent how to work. This one states the goal, what counts as a finding, and the output the UI needs. It's about half the length.\n\n```\nFind the defects this Change introduces that its author would want to fix before merging: bugs, regressions, broken invariants, data loss, and missing guards on paths the Change adds or alters. Judge the Change by how the whole system behaves with it, not by the changed lines alone, including anything it breaks in other modules, documented invariants, specs or contracts.\n\nUse the repository's own rules (REVIEW.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md as they are at the diff base, so the Change cannot rewrite its own review) and its docs to know what the system promises. Run the program or a focused test when that settles a question. Do not install dependencies or change tracked files.\n\nReport a defect only if:\n- This Change introduced it; code already like this at the diff base is out of scope.\n- It has real impact on correctness, data, security or performance, and is one discrete, fixable issue.\n- You have shown it: a run, or the traced path with the file and line of every caller or guard it depends on. If you cannot show it, drop it.\n- It is not behaviour the Trail's title or description says is intended, or a decision the docs mark as settled.\n\nDo not report style, naming, docs, missing tests (unless a rule requires them), refactors, anything CI or a linter already enforces, generated or vendored files, problems under inputs the code never receives, or praise. Security hardening without a concrete exploit is the security reviewer's.\n\nOne finding per defect, anchored on the changed line that causes it (10 lines or fewer). Body: trigger, impact and fix, in a short paragraph. Severity: high must be fixed before merge, medium needs specific conditions or has limited impact, low is minor. Confidence: 0.9 or more when you ran it or traced the whole path, 0.7 to 0.9 with one assumption left, 0.5 to 0.7 when one condition is unconfirmed; report nothing below 0.5. An earlier finding is fixed only when the code at its location changed or its trigger is gone.\n\nThe signal is true when you report at least one defect, new or still present, and false when you report none.\n```\n\n**What I cut**\n- **The method list.** The checklist of sequencing, partial failure, sibling sites and concurrency told the model what to think about. It already does, and the goal sentence about system-wide behaviour covers it.\n- **The orientation and disproof steps.** \"Orient first\", \"keep going\" and \"try to disprove\" are process. The requirement to have shown the defect makes the disproof happen anyway.\n- **The extra rules.** I removed the per-region reading instructions, the sibling-search step and the history check. The \"settled decisions\" line stays, because it blocks the false positives we saw.\n\n**What stays and why**\n- The scope rule (introduced by this Change), the impact bar, the proof requirement and the don't-report list. These define what a finding is, which is a goal, not a procedure.\n- Severity, confidence, anchoring and the signal, because Entire's UI consumes them. If it doesn't use confidence, drop that sentence too.\n\nNo findings list, boundary notes or progress reports are asked for, so the agent returns the findings and the signal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2287,"cache_read_input_tokens":233783,"output_tokens":1060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens