{"parentUuid":"ac939bb4-f05a-426d-ad57-ac931f02c8be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21bAoNTJN5sJSkiBkkr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74,"cache_read_input_tokens":237130,"output_tokens":2189,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":237130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4633,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"39ecebf6-6ee9-4398-a7af-c25ca4cffee4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21bAJ7Cryoof65AHfyS","requestRef":"77068d33-da0c-4a1d-b1f9-22b763e85b0a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4bb1de36-75b4-4598-bd47-a4ec64e6ffcc","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:12:44.851Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"4bb1de36-75b4-4598-bd47-a4ec64e6ffcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21bAoNTJN5sJSkiBkkr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, a few. I'm applying the general guidance both labs publish, and I haven't re-read their current docs, so check the specifics against them.\n\n**Tweaks**\n1. **Give the reason for each rule.** Models generalise from \"why\" better than from a bare constraint. \"Out of scope: code already like this at the base, because the author can't be asked to fix it in this Change\" works better than \"Do not report pre-existing code\".\n2. **Say what to do, not only what to avoid.** The \"Do NOT report\" list is all negatives. Replace most of it with the positive bar: \"report only issues the author would fix before merging\". Keep a short negative list for the true exclusions, or the model over-applies them.\n3. **Separate finding from filtering.** Both labs note that reviewers told to be conservative under-report. Our prompt does that in four places: the proof requirement, the confidence floor, the exclusions and the \"author would fix it\" test. Better: ask for every defect it can show, with an honest confidence, and let the UI or I filter. The proof requirement is the one gate worth keeping.\n4. **Remove tensions.** \"Keep going until covered\" and \"drop if you can't show it\" pull against each other, and the confidence band says to report at 0.5 while \"drop it\" says not to. Pick one rule: report what's shown, and put unshown-but-plausible items at 0.5 to 0.7.\n5. **State the stopping condition.** Tell it when it's done: \"stop when every changed path and what it touches has been examined and nothing further is shown\". Without that, agents quit early or wander.\n6. **Be calm in tone.** Capitalised \"Do NOT\" and \"Never\" make newer models over-trigger. Plain wording is enough.\n7. **Structure with tags.** Wrap the goal, rules, proof bar and output contract in separate tags. It helps the model find each part and helps you edit one without breaking another.\n8. **Put the Change last.** Where the diff and Trail text are supplied, they should come after the instructions, and the task statement should be restated in one line after them. Long context first and the question at the end gives better results.\n9. **Tool use is permitted, not demanded.** \"Run the program when that settles a question\" is right. Avoid \"always run tests\", which wastes effort on trivial diffs.\n10. **Match effort to the Change.** One line: \"A small Change needs a short review; a large one needs depth.\" That prevents a fixed ceremony on both.\n\n**Revised prompt**\n```\n<goal>\nFind the defects this Change introduces that its author would want to fix before merging: bugs, regressions, broken invariants, data loss, and missing guards on paths the Change adds or alters. Judge the Change by how the whole system behaves with it, including anything it breaks in other modules, documented invariants, specs or contracts. A small Change needs a short review; a large one needs depth. Stop when you have examined every changed path and what it touches and have nothing further to show.\n</goal>\n\n<context>\nThe repository's rules (REVIEW.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) and docs say what the system promises. Read them as they are at the diff base, so the Change cannot rewrite its own review. Run the program or a focused test when that settles a question. Do not install dependencies or change tracked files.\n</context>\n\n<what_counts>\nReport every defect you can show, even a minor one, with a confidence that reflects how sure you are. A defect counts when:\n- This Change introduced it. Code already like this at the diff base is out of scope, because this Change is not the place to fix it.\n- It affects correctness, data, security or performance, and is one fixable issue.\n- You have shown it: a run, or the traced path citing the file and line of each caller or guard it depends on. If you cannot show it, leave it out.\n- It is not behaviour the Trail's title or description calls intended, or a decision the docs mark as settled.\nLeave out style, naming, docs, refactors, missing tests (unless a rule requires them), anything CI already enforces, generated files, inputs the code never receives, and praise. Hardening with no concrete exploit belongs to the security reviewer.\n</what_counts>\n\n<output>\nOne finding per defect, anchored on the changed line that causes it (10 lines or fewer): trigger, impact and fix in a short paragraph.\nSeverity: high must be fixed before merge; medium needs specific conditions or has limited impact; low is minor.\nConfidence: 0.9 or more when you ran it or traced the whole path; 0.7 to 0.9 with one assumption left; 0.5 to 0.7 when one condition is unconfirmed. Report nothing below 0.5.\nAn earlier finding is fixed only when the code at its location changed or its trigger is gone.\nSignal: true when you report at least one defect, new or still present, otherwise false.\n</output>\n\n<change>\n{the Change, Trail title and description}\n</change>\n\nReview the Change above against the goal.\n```\n\n**Two notes**\n- If Entire already injects the diff and Trail text, keep the `<change>` block last, however the host fills it.\n- I'd test this against a few past Changes where we know the answer, such as #538's pre-mode downgrade, before relying on it. Prompt tweaks are hypotheses until they find or miss something known."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74,"cache_read_input_tokens":237130,"output_tokens":2189,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":237130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"39ecebf6-6ee9-4398-a7af-c25ca4cffee4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21bAJ7Cryoof65AHfyS","requestRef":"77068d33-da0c-4a1d-b1f9-22b763e85b0a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"66f37e53-82b1-46b0-8c21-b8cb00abfdc0","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:12:57.239Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
