{"parentUuid":"7e133f07-2441-4006-9759-149f1e737602","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21fNEa1Yt7qVqWhhKbo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60,"cache_read_input_tokens":239393,"output_tokens":864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":158},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":239393,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1307,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"feb796ca-a423-4454-b79c-6a024c5ae702","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch21fMxhPnvgWKiG9dxu5","requestRef":"1bbb8ff5-26cc-4a54-8350-2129b3990c99","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f6091ab-3f11-4f93-93f4-369ba88a5512","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:13:38.465Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"8f6091ab-3f11-4f93-93f4-369ba88a5512","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21fNEa1Yt7qVqWhhKbo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't judge \"gpt sol medium\" because I don't know that model, and I'm Claude, so I have a bias toward Claude models. I'd settle it with a test on our own history, not on my opinion.\n\n**How I'd decide**\n1. **Build a small answer key.** Use past Changes where we know what a good review finds:\n   - #538: the pre-mode downgrade.\n   - #539: the incomplete changelog dependency lines.\n   - #535: a decision path written after the workspace was already half-versioned.\n   - #528: the absolute path with a missing parent.\n   - #531: the stale-inference guard.\n   - Two or three clean Changes, to measure false positives.\n2. **Run each candidate model and effort level on the same prompt.** Score three things: defects found, false positives, and cost per review. A sample of 5 to 8 Changes is enough to see big differences.\n3. **Pick by results.** A finding only counts if it can be reproduced, as in our own hunts.\n\n**What I'd expect, as hypotheses to test**\n- **Effort matters more than model for this task.** Review is reasoning-heavy, and tracing a path across modules is where low effort misses things. Medium may be fine for small diffs and thin for ones that cross modules. I'd test high on the larger Changes.\n- **Cost gap between sizes.** A smaller model at high effort may match a larger one at medium for a fraction of the price on small diffs. Only the test shows whether that holds here.\n- **Two different models can beat one.** Reviewers from different model families miss different things. If the budget allows, run a second model only on large or high-risk Changes, such as release, versioning or manifest-writing code, and take the union of their findings.\n\n**If you want a starting point without testing first**\nKeep what you have for small Changes, and raise the effort or move up a model for any Change that touches state, parsing or release flow. That's where our real bugs were. Confirm it with the answer key before making it permanent.\n\nIf it helps, I can assemble the answer key: the PR numbers, the commit before each fix, and what each review should have caught. That's about an hour of setup, and you'd have a repeatable way to compare any model or prompt change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60,"cache_read_input_tokens":239393,"output_tokens":864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":158},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":239393,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"feb796ca-a423-4454-b79c-6a024c5ae702","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21fMxhPnvgWKiG9dxu5","requestRef":"1bbb8ff5-26cc-4a54-8350-2129b3990c99","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3486302c-bba4-4e73-bf93-ce9555fed161","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:13:44.944Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
