{"parentUuid":"6d3e981f-17ec-43a3-8a03-94a9ce5f42f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21iHQggh4LduuzaXVA7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Launching two agents with a goal each, free to run the real binary in their own worktrees, and reporting only defects they've reproduced."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"output_tokens":2456,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2456,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a4632c64-4c87-43ce-a3b9-81827ef2d1bc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch21iH5bjaLDAjSN5xQw5","requestRef":"af6eb75a-3980-4337-be89-6bdb85cfb00a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a4f1f98b-44f4-45ac-a54e-acc441ef54da","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:14:20.639Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"a4f1f98b-44f4-45ac-a54e-acc441ef54da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21iHQggh4LduuzaXVA7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Tp954CvziVZRHGXpcjjq7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hunt plan-to-publish flow defects","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Find real defects in Callisto (a Rust release tool for Cargo/npm/PyPI monorepos) and prove each one.\n\nFocus: the plan-to-publish flow. `callisto version` (plan, apply, persist, changelogs, pre mode, groups), the release decision file, `release plan` / `release pending` / `release`, release execution and recovery after a partial failure or rerun. Anything where one step writes state that a later step reads is where defects hide.\n\nOrient yourself first from AGENTS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md (read its invariants), docs/architecture/, docs/stability.md, docs/errors.md, docs/specs/*.json and docs/releasing.md. Work out what the system promises, then try to break those promises: reruns, interrupted runs, workspaces below the repo root, pre-release mode, fixed/linked groups, several ecosystems in one workspace, odd but valid configs. Where a documented claim and the code disagree, that is a lead. When you find a flaw, look for sibling code with the same flaw.\n\nProve each defect by running the real binary (`cargo build -p callisto-cli`, then target/debug/callisto) in throwaway repos under $TMPDIR, or with a failing test. A test that asserts a behaviour does not make it intended; check git history before calling something a bug. You may run commands and builds freely, but do not edit tracked files, push, or touch the network or any real remote. Commit signing is off in scratch repos: use `-c commit.gpgsign=false` only there.\n\nAlready fixed, do not report: subdirectory-workspace git paths, parenthesized PEP 508 requirements, decision-file path containment, pre-mode version downgrade, changelog dependency-update lines, `release pending --limit 0`. Settled, do not report: the emoji in the release PR body, error code E194, the exit codes of `compose-pr-body --preview`, `release plan --package` with nothing pending, and `--cwd` to a missing directory, the literal `$/.github/actions/...` in generated workflow `uses:` lines, and the registry-tools test `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` failing without network tools.\n\nReport only defects you reproduced, ranked by impact: where it is (file:line), the exact commands, observed versus expected, and the consequence. No suspicions, no progress notes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"output_tokens":2456,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2456,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016Tp954CvziVZRHGXpcjjq7":{"description":"Hunt plan-to-publish flow defects","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Find real defects in Callisto (a Rust release tool for Cargo/npm/PyPI monorepos) and prove each one.\n\nFocus: the plan-to-publish flow. `callisto version` (plan, apply, persist, changelogs, pre mode, groups), the release decision file, `release plan` / `release pending` / `release`, release execution and recovery after a partial failure or rerun. Anything where one step writes state that a later step reads is where defects hide.\n\nOrient yourself first from AGENTS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md (read its invariants), docs/architecture/, docs/stability.md, docs/errors.md, docs/specs/*.json and docs/releasing.md. Work out what the system promises, then try to break those promises: reruns, interrupted runs, workspaces below the repo root, pre-release mode, fixed/linked groups, several ecosystems in one workspace, odd but valid configs. Where a documented claim and the code disagree, that is a lead. When you find a flaw, look for sibling code with the same flaw.\n\nProve each defect by running the real binary (`cargo build -p callisto-cli`, then target/debug/callisto) in throwaway repos under $TMPDIR, or with a failing test. A test that asserts a behaviour does not make it intended; check git history before calling something a bug. You may run commands and builds freely, but do not edit tracked files, push, or touch the network or any real remote. Commit signing is off in scratch repos: use `-c commit.gpgsign=false` only there.\n\nAlready fixed, do not report: subdirectory-workspace git paths, parenthesized PEP 508 requirements, decision-file path containment, pre-mode version downgrade, changelog dependency-update lines, `release pending --limit 0`. Settled, do not report: the emoji in the release PR body, error code E194, the exit codes of `compose-pr-body --preview`, `release plan --package` with nothing pending, and `--cwd` to a missing directory, the literal `$/.github/actions/...` in generated workflow `uses:` lines, and the registry-tools test `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` failing without network tools.\n\nReport only defects you reproduced, ranked by impact: where it is (file:line), the exact commands, observed versus expected, and the consequence. No suspicions, no progress notes."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a4632c64-4c87-43ce-a3b9-81827ef2d1bc","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch21iH5bj