{"parentUuid":"f4ce9fa2-9cca-4884-8a70-db1982a222c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch21iHQggh4LduuzaXVA7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013KuPH8KdLdn2WSW9bN1VTt","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hunt manifest and cascade defects","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Find real defects in Callisto (a Rust release tool for Cargo/npm/PyPI monorepos) and prove each one.\n\nFocus: how Callisto reads and rewrites package manifests and dependencies. Cargo.toml (workspace inheritance, path and version deps, renamed deps, target-specific tables), package.json (workspaces, catalogs, ranges, peer and optional deps, lockfiles), pyproject.toml (PEP 621, Poetry, Flit, PEP 440 and PEP 508 forms), the cascade that decides which dependents bump and how their specs are rewritten, config loading and validation (callisto.toml and its keys), and the generated GitHub workflows and action inputs against what the code enforces. Cross-module contracts are where defects hide: what the cascade plans versus what each manifest writer actually does for each spec form, formatting and comment preservation on write, and round trips (parse, render, parse).\n\nOrient yourself first from AGENTS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md (read its invariants), docs/architecture/, docs/stability.md, docs/errors.md, docs/specs/*.json and docs/config.md. Work out what the system promises, then try to break those promises with odd but valid inputs. Where a documented claim and the code disagree, that is a lead. When you find a flaw, look for sibling code with the same flaw in the other ecosystems.\n\nProve each defect by running the real binary (`cargo build -p callisto-cli`, then target/debug/callisto) in throwaway repos under $TMPDIR, or with a failing test or property test. A test that asserts a behaviour does not make it intended; check git history before calling something a bug. You may run commands and builds freely, but do not edit tracked files, push, or touch the network or any real remote. Commit signing is off in scratch repos: use `-c commit.gpgsign=false` only there.\n\nAlready fixed, do not report: subdirectory-workspace git paths, parenthesized PEP 508 requirements, decision-file path containment, pre-mode version downgrade, changelog dependency-update lines, `release pending --limit 0`. Settled, do not report: the emoji in the release PR body, error code E194, the literal `$/.github/actions/...` in generated workflow `uses:` lines, a workspace member directory named `br{a}ce`, and the registry-tools test `a_version_the_registry_serves_is_exact_with_no_checksum_or_yank_claim` failing without network tools.\n\nReport only defects you reproduced, ranked by impact: where it is (file:line), the exact commands, observed versus expected, and the consequence. No suspicions, no progress notes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"output_tokens":2456,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2456,"cache_read_input_tokens":240317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013KuPH8KdLdn2WSW9bN1VTt":{"description":"Hunt manifest and cascade defects","subagent_type":"general-purpose","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Find real defects in Callisto (a Rust release tool for Cargo/npm/PyPI monorepos) and prove each one.\n\nFocus: 