{"parentUuid":"94539656-9d7c-40c9-83f3-ee597a01bb20","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f8ca365-27ef-4ebe-9928-f458563a052f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S18VGcu9JfzAevoEjQdSqa","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings/.changeset/init-artifact-target-trims-spaces.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"94a8fe3a-6e37-4815-a709-4f103ef35e27","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:26:39.715Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings/.changeset/init-artifact-target-trims-spaces.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: patch\n---\n\n`callisto init --artifact-target \"a, b\"` no longer writes a config that every later command rejects.\n\n- Before, a space after the comma stayed in the target (`\" aarch64-apple-darwin\"`), and the next command failed with `E197`.\n- Now the spaces are trimmed, and an empty entry such as `a,,b` is a usage error.\n- You do not need to do anything. If `init` already wrote a target with a leading space, remove the space in `callisto.toml`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"94539656-9d7c-40c9-83f3-ee597a01bb20","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"worktree-verify-manifest-findings","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
