{"parentUuid":"460cd04a-e7b1-4280-a4cb-f5f0937108ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch22mHe2bVrQMq84sGtCJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QWxvVaruqggmTJr6qqw5HU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_init.md","content":"## Summary\n- `callisto init --artifact-target \"a, b\"` kept the space after the comma, so it wrote `target = \" b\"` and an asset name with a space. Every later command then failed with E197 until the user edited `callisto.toml` by hand. The help says \"comma-separated\", so a space after the comma is the natural way to type it.\n- Each target is now trimmed while parsing arguments, and an empty entry (`a,,b`) is a usage error (exit 2).\n- Found by a bug hunt over manifests and config after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/init-artifact-target-trims-spaces.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` exit 0; `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-manifests` has no failures\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `init --yes --no-workflow --artifact-target 'x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-apple-darwin'` wrote a target with a leading space and `status` failed with E197. A parse test covers the trimmed and empty cases.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":275436,"output_tokens":702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":275436,"cache_creation_input_tokens":359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":359},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QWxvVaruqggmTJr6qqw5HU":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_init.md","content":"## Summary\n- `callisto init --artifact-target \"a, b\"` kept the space after the comma, so it wrote `target = \" b\"` and an asset name with a space. Every later command then failed with E197 until the user edited `callisto.toml` by hand. The help says \"comma-separated\", so a space after the comma is the natural way to type it.\n- Each target is now trimmed while parsing arguments, and an empty entry (`a,,b`) is a usage error (exit 2).\n- Found by a bug hunt over manifests and config after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/init-artifact-target-trims-spaces.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` exit 0; `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-manifests` has no failures\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `init --yes --no-workflow --artifact-target 'x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-apple-darwin'` wrote a target with a leading space and `status` failed with E197. A parse test covers the trimmed and empty cases.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d89afcc5-b1ba-46af-9083-b2606a0fc04f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch22mHLRqQciFvknwz6G8","requestRef":"d799ab1a-c873-4ae8-ad39-c5e4e2d5a2b0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"43727bec-3452-4bf1-be51-cd401febf9