"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch237GRQZ2EAZdo76eYje","requestRef":"bc27e58c-a2a7-45e9-b481-e306c5f213b1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"62bf860a-1d75-4c13-9b09-af621f84507c","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:32:36.633Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/python-wildcard-pin","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"62bf860a-1d75-4c13-9b09-af621f84507c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch237Gg3zoTNqwZ9ubQiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VG3VQPVmLv7RMGYFgMEAMN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_wild.md","content":"## Summary\n- A Python dependency written as a wildcard, `lib==1.*` or `lib==1.2.*`, was rewritten to an exact pin on the next release of `lib` (`lib==2.0.0`), silently turning a loose constraint into a hard pin. `lib===1.2.3` also became `lib==2.0.0`, changing the operator. `docs/specs/versioning.json` says wildcards that cannot be rewritten mechanically fail with E319, and Cargo and npm wildcards already do.\n- `rewrite_single` now returns `None` for a clause whose version contains `*` or starts with another operator character, which the cascade turns into E319 for a runtime dependency (nothing written) and leaves a dev dependency alone, like any other unrewritable form.\n- Found by a bug hunt over manifests and config after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/python-wildcard-pin-not-rewritten.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: the spec already describes this behaviour.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` exit 0; `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-manifests` has no failures\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `c` with `dependencies=[\"lib==1.*\"]` and a major bump of `lib` rewrote it to `lib==2.0.0`; after the fix `callisto version` stops with E319 and writes nothing. A unit test covers `==1.*`, `==1.2.*` and `===1.2.3`.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1014,"cache_read_input_tokens":283538,"output_tokens":1072,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1014,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":283538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1014},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VG3VQPVmLv7RMGYFgMEAMN":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_wild.md","content":"## Summary\n- A Python dependency written as a wildcard, `lib==1.*` or `lib==1.2.*`, was rewritten to an exact pin on the next release of `lib` (`lib==2.0.0`), silently turning a loose constraint into a hard pin. `lib===1.2.3` also became `lib==2.0.0`, changing the operator. `docs/specs/versioning.json` says wildcards that cannot be rewritten mechanically fail with E319, and Cargo and npm wildcards already do.\n- `rewrite_single` now returns `None` for a clause whose version contains `*` or starts with another operator character, which the cascade turns into E319 for a runtime dependency (nothing written) and leaves a dev dependency alone, like any other unrewritable form.\n- Found by a bug hunt over manifests and config after 0.20.0.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] Added `.changeset/python-wildcard-pin-not-rewritten.md` (patch).\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: the spec already describes this behaviour.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `cargo +1.100.0 clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` exit 0; `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-manifests` has no failures\n- [x] Reproduced with the real binary: `c` with `dependencies=[\"lib==1.*\"]` and a major bump of `lib` rewrote it to `lib==2.0.0`; after the fix `callisto version` stops with E319 and writes nothing. A unit test covers `==1.*`, `==1.2.*` and `===1.2.3`.\n- [ ] Not run: `just workflow-contracts`, CI\n\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ac7dd7d3-49ff-4a09-8b80-d4eeb5f4db58","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch237GRQZ2EAZdo76eYje","requestRef":"bc27e58c-a2a7-45e9-b481-e306c5f213b1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"02623f5b-8ed0-4311-9411-7343c3e7903c","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:32:40.600Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/python-wildcard-pin","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
