 edited.\n  \n  **1. A failed lockfile refresh (E208) leaves a half-applied tree, and the advised retry is refused.** [medium]\n  - Where: `callisto version`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs` (lock refresh after the manifest and changelog writes); help text for E208 in `docs/errors.md:250` and `crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:884`. Planning does not check that the rewritten manifests still resolve.\n  - Cause: apply does not predict a dependent that cannot be rewritten. A dev-dependency range that can't be rewritten is only warned about and left as is (VER-CAS-09, VER-CAS-04), but the written tree no longer resolves.\n  - Repro:\n    - Workspace with crates `a` and `b` (1.0.0), and `b` has `[dev-dependencies] a = { path=\"../a\", version=\">=1.0.0, <2.0.0\" }`.\n    - `callisto add --package cargo/a:major --summary x`, commit, then `callisto version`.\n    - Observed: E208 (`cargo update --workspace` fails: candidate 2.0.0 doesn't match). `crates/a/Cargo.toml` is already 2.0.0 and `CHANGELOG.md` is written but untracked, so the tree is half-applied.\n    - The E208 help says \"fix it, then re-run `callisto version`\". After editing b's dev-dep to `>=2.0.0, <3.0.0`, `callisto version` exits 1 with E121 (\"looks like an interrupted `version` run\").\n    - E121's own advice is to `git rm` the changeset and commit. With a tracked `Cargo.lock`, that commits a release whose lockfile was never refreshed or staged.\n  - Expected: `version` should refuse before writing, or recovery should not need a manual `git restore`.\n  - Same shape with a dev-dependency `*` in pre mode (the `*` spec can't be rewritten to a prerelease).\n  \n  **2. npm dependency specs with a `v` prefix, and `~>`, are never tested or rewritten, silently.** [medium-low]\n  - Where: `crates/callisto-manifests/src/npm.rs:561` (`parse_npm_spec_str` falls through to `DepSpec::Opaque`), because `is_bare_semver` in `crates/callisto-manifests/src/common.rs:15` requires a digit first. Opaque specs are treated as \"covers\" with no diagnostic (`crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:75`).\n  - Repro:\n    - npm workspace with `w` at 1.2.3 and dependents with `\"w\": \"v1.2.3\"`, `\"=v1.2.3\"`, `\"^v1.2.3\"` and `\"~>1.2.3\"`.\n    - `callisto add --package npm/w:major`, then `callisto version --no-refresh-lockfiles`.\n    - Observed: `w` becomes 2.0.0. Those four dependents are not bumped, not rewritten and get no warning. The control specs `1.2.3`, `^1.2.3`, `~1.2.3` and `=1.2.3` all become 2.0.0 and cascade.\n  - Consequence: the dependent keeps pointing at the old `w` (1.2.3), which is a valid npm range for the same version as `1.2.3`.\n  \n  **3. Commit inference re-bumps on every `version` run until the release is tagged.** [medium-low]\n  - Where: inference window in `crates/callisto-graph/src/infer.rs` and `crates/callisto-graph/src/conventional/`; there is no recorded-consumed marker (unlike the changeset id list in `pre.json`).\n  - Repro, stable:\n    - Package `a` with `release-trigger = \"auto\"` and tag `a@1.0.0`. Commit `feat: new f`, run `callisto version` (1.0.0 to 1.1.0), commit `chore(release): version a 1.1.0`.\n    - `callisto status` then reports `cargo/a 1.1.0 (pending: minor)`.\n    - A second `callisto version` bumps 1.1.0 to 1.2.0, and the changelog lists the release commit under \"### Minor Changes: version a 1.1.0 (d5fe85f)\".\n  - Repro, pre mode: `pre enter beta`, then three `version` runs with only chore commits between them gave `1.1.0-beta.0`, `beta.1`, `beta.2`, each with a changelog section.\n  - Expected: a second run with nothing new to release should be a no-op, as it is for changesets.\n  - Caveat: VER-AGG-04 says the window starts at the last release tag, so this follows the spec. It only bites when `version` is rerun before `callisto release` tags.\n  \n  **4. Prepending a changelog entry duplicates the H1 when the existing title isn't exactly `# <package>`.** [low]\n  - Where: `crates/callisto-graph/src/changelog/write.rs:62-75` (the \"No matching H1 found\" branch).\n  - Repro:\n    - `crates/a/CHANGELOG.md` starts `# Changelog for a`, a blank line, a preamble, then `## 1.0.0`. Likewise for the common `# Changelog` title.\n    - `callisto version` writes `# a`, the new `## 1.1.0` section, and then the old `# Changelog for a`, preamble and `## 1.0.0` below it.\n  - Consequence: the file ends up with two H1s and the old title and preamble stranded under the new section. The code comment calls this \"well-formed\", but it is a wart for any project adopting Callisto over an existing changelog.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"I reproduced four defects with the real binary (target/debug/callisto, scratch repos under /tmp/claude-501; npm release flows used a fake `npm` on PATH and a local bare remote, no network). I found nothing in the decision-file verification or the interrupted-release rerun paths: tampered decisions, stale digests, partial failures, reruns and `release pending` all behaved correctly. A randomised Cargo cascade check over about 100 workspaces (groups, dependency kinds, pre mode) found nothing beyond the dev-dependency defect below and the documented multi-clause-range abort E319. I did not run the repo's own check commands, since no tracked files were edited.\n\n**1. A failed lockfile refresh (E208) leaves a half-applied tree, and the advised retry is refused.** [medium]\n- Where: `callisto version`, `crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs` (lock refresh after the manifest and changelog writes); help text for E208 in `docs/errors.md:250` and `crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:884`. Planning does not check that the rewritten manifests still resolve.\n- Cause: apply does not predict a dependent that cannot be rewritten. A dev-dependency range that can't be rewritten is only warned about and left as is (VER-CAS-09, VER-CAS-04), but the written tree no longer resolves.\n- Repro:\n  - Workspace with crates `a` and `b` (1.0.0), and `b` has `[dev-dependencies] a = { path=\"../a