{"parentUuid":"05476f7b-5f93-4974-b6cd-64aa555fb465","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3de37e0d-1775-44fa-86e9-cd5b184c34fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014idLf2cZG3THWHRkqSmvKL","type":"tool_result","content":"14:/// What a plan does to a path, which decides what must hold for it.\n17:    /// A manifest the plan edits: it must exist as a readable regular file and its directory must take a new file.\n19:    /// A file the plan may create or replace, such as a changelog or `pre.json`.\n21:    /// A file the plan deletes: only the path itself is checked.\n25:/// Every path `plan` writes or deletes under `opts`, once each.\n26:fn targets(plan: &VersionPlan, opts: &ApplyOptions) -> BTreeSet<(PathBuf, Target)> {\n74:/// Fails with every target that cannot be written, before anything is.\n75:///\n76:/// # Errors\n77:///\n78:/// [`GraphError::ApplyPreflight`] naming each unwritable path and why.\n113:/// The paths of `paths` that a `.gitignore` ignores and Git does not already track, which `git add` refuses.\n114:///\n115:/// # Errors\n116:///\n117:/// `git check-ignore` could not run or failed (anything but \"some ignored\" and \"none ignored\").\n140:/// Whether `git check-ignore` names at least one of `paths` as ignored (it prints what it matched, `-q` taking one path only).\n141:fn any_ignored<R: CommandRunner>(runner: &R, root: &Path, paths: &[PathBuf]) -> Result<bool, GraphError> {\n157:fn problem(root: &Path, relative: &Path, target: Target, permit: &ApplyPermit) -> Option<String> {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"448ec083-acfb-493f-bb6e-c19ed2e48160","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:42:32.774Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"14:/// What a plan does to a path, which decides what must hold for it.\n17:    /// A manifest the plan edits: it must exist as a readable regular file and its directory must take a new file.\n19:    /// A file the plan may create or replace, such as a changelog or `pre.json`.\n21:    /// A file the plan deletes: on