{"parentUuid":"8d815f65-5cde-461e-8d33-2b03c6fa9e98","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch24bCqWfVAVSvmMyzLx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":323672,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":323672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6524,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"2464588e-1bd8-40c8-b4f0-7314129e5201","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch24bCURaYiUZSv72PtDd","requestRef":"6e3854cb-7a20-4d89-add0-c62656846c42","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"98dd4626-97ab-41f0-b77f-0987f3495211","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:52:07.790Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/version-lock-refresh-rollback","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"98dd4626-97ab-41f0-b77f-0987f3495211","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch24bCqWfVAVSvmMyzLx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #543 is open and ready, and it fixes the E208/E121 problem both agents hit. Here is where the two agents' findings stand.\n\n**Fixed (PRs open, signed, checks green locally)**\n\n| PR | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| #541 | `init --artifact-target \"a, b\"` no longer writes a config that fails E197 |\n| #542 | Python `lib==1.*` no longer silently becomes an exact pin; it fails E319 and writes nothing |\n| #543 | A failed lockfile refresh (E208) now restores the written files, so the documented retry works |\n\nI changed an existing test for #543. It asserted the half-applied manifest, which contradicted the E208 docs. I also changed the E208 help and its docs row, because the old advice (\"run the command yourself\") would succeed against the restored versions.\n\n**Verified, not fixed yet** (all medium-low)\n- **npm overrides:** an exact override `1.2.3` becomes the range `~2.0.0`, and `pnpm.overrides` is left at the old version.\n- **npm `v` prefix and `~>` specs:** `\"v1.2.3\"`, `\"=v1.2.3\"`, `\"^v1.2.3\"` and `\"~>1.2.3\"` are never tested or rewritten, silently. I haven't reproduced this one myself.\n- **Changelog title:** with an existing `# Changelog for a` or `# Changelog` heading, `version` writes a new `# a` heading above it and leaves two H1s. This matters for any project adopting Callisto over an existing changelog. I haven't reproduced it myself.\n\n**Needs your decision**\n- **Commit inference re-bumps on every `version` run until the release is tagged.** With `release-trigger = \"auto\"`, a second `version` run bumps 1.1.0 to 1.2.0, listing the release commit itself. This follows what `VER-AGG-04` says (the window starts at the last tag), so it's a design question, not a regression. Do you want `version` to treat an already-versioned inferred bump as consumed?\n- **Poetry caret and tilde dependents** can't take a snapshot or pre-release version. The spec says that's deliberate, so it's a product gap and not a bug.\n\n**Skipped:** the changelog and changesets-dir config-path edge cases (`Cargo.toml` as a changelog, `.git` as the changesets dir).\n\nI'd do the npm items and the changelog heading next as separate PRs, and wait on your answer for the inference question. Which should I continue with?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":323672,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":323672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2464588e-1bd8-40c8-b4f0-7314129e5201","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch24bCURaYiUZSv72PtDd","requestRef":"6e3854cb-7a20-4d89-add0-c62656846c42","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f15c1a5-1fc8-4453-b51b-413b892a03c6","timestamp":"2026-11-14T02:52:08.335Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/verify-manifest-findings","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/version-lock-refresh-rollback","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
